    'Read stage-a/source-manifest.json, stage-a/context-manifest.json, stage-a/stage-b-brief-context.md, stage-a/stage-b-visual-references.json, stage-a/conversion-policy.json, stage-a/route-context.json, route-context-report.json, and stage-b-visual-parity.json when present. Treat attached briefs/screenshots/assets as supporting context for Stage B while keeping stage-a/drafts/index.html as the canonical primary artifact. Treat conversion-policy.json as required when choosing profile-specific repair actions. A failed stage-b-visual-parity.json is evidence from the immediately previous rejected frontend render: repair its pixel, match-coverage, geometry, computed-style, responsive, and named mismatch deltas in this result before finalizing.',
    'Start from stage-b-bricks-schema-validation.json, stage-b-baseline-report.md, stage-b-fidelity-plan.md, stage-b-route-contract.json, stage-b-theme-style-contract.json, stage-b-theme-style-health.json, stage-b-header-plan.json, and stage-b-footer-plan.json. Read other maps only when one of those concise reports names a concrete gap; do not reread the full Stage A HTML for a clean baseline.',
    'Pixflow-owned: when the fast path reports a concrete gap, inspect only the matching targeted section of .pixflow-skills/bricks-web-prototype/SKILL.md or its routed child file. Do not enumerate or reread every always-loaded child skill for a clean baseline. Treat pixflow-bricks-mcp.md and pixflow-plugin-mcp.md as supplemental contracts only.',
    'Pixflow-owned: use only the matching entry in stage-b-bricks-focused-schemas.json when a concrete repair needs a setting key. Use stage-b-bricks-runtime-knowledge.json only before adding an advanced capability such as dynamic tags, query loops, filters, conditions, forms, interactions, breakpoints, or WooCommerce elements. The deterministic validator already used the full live schema internally.',
    'Pixflow-owned: when focused schema controls include valueShape or controlTree, treat those as authoritative. Spacing/dimensions controls use a single setting key such as _padding or _margin with top/right/bottom/left values and unit.top/unit.right/unit.bottom/unit.left; do not invent _paddingTop/_topPadding-style keys.',
