function renderPixflowBricksMcpMarkdown() {
  return `# Pixflow Bricks MCP

Built-in Bricks schema, validation, variables, global classes, media, and compiler capabilities used by Pixflow Design.

## Active Tools

- bricks.reference.compact
- bricks.payload.validate
- bricks.payload.inspect
- bricks.media.selected_assets
- bricks.classes.global
- bricks.tokens.pixflow
- pixflow.google_fonts.install
- pixflow.icon_sets.install_subset

## Stage B Baseline Workflow

- If \`bricks-baseline.json\` exists, treat it as the initial editable Bricks payload.
- The Pixflow clean-room baseline preserves source DOM order, global class ids, \`_attributes\`, image refs, Bricks page settings for safe Stage A JavaScript, header/footer extraction, and responsive breakpoint settings from simple \`@media (max-width)\` class rules.
- Model cleanup should be targeted: improve semantic Bricks elements, move high-value routine layout/style controls into Bricks settings, repair missing craft details, and keep sidecar contracts synchronized.
- Do not regenerate the entire page, remove baseline ids/classes, or flatten preserved responsive keys unless source comparison or local QA identifies a concrete problem.
- Preserve semantic section roles from Stage A/source maps without inventing them. Add hero trace attributes only when the source, source map, section map, classes, id, or \`data-od-id\` explicitly identify the section as a hero/masthead; do not infer hero from "first section" alone.
- If Stage A clearly declares an interactive tab/card affordance through classes, comments, active states, labels, or ARIA but omits source JavaScript, the conversion still needs working behavior. Prefer native Bricks tabs when the structure maps cleanly; otherwise keep the editable card/panel structure and add minimal scoped page-settings JavaScript.
- Keep \`_cssCustom\` when it carries source-only selectors/effects such as reveal CSS, keyframes, collage detail, or unsupported Bricks control behavior. Rebuild visible pseudo-element dividers/marks as child elements where practical.

## Supported Elements

${getStageBAllowedElementNames().map((name) => `- ${name}`).join('\n')}

## Class References

- _cssGlobalClasses must be an array of generated global class IDs.
- Source class names remain human-readable, but elements reference class IDs in Bricks JSON.
- The baseline source class inventory is authoritative. Refine settings on those classes only; do not rename, replace, remove, or invent global classes during Stage B.
- Never create ID-derived repair classes. If a native Bricks-only wrapper has no baseline class, keep the minimum required native layout controls directly on that wrapper.
- Runtime HTML attributes are represented with _attributes arrays, for example:
  - { "id": "abcxyz", "name": "data-reveal" }
  - { "id": "defuvw", "name": "data-reveal", "value": "true" }
- Do not include copied-element metadata such as source, sourceUrl, or version in model output.
- Use nav-menu for real Bricks/WordPress navigation menus when a menu source is available. Keep CTA buttons as button elements.

## Layout Controls

- Use Bricks underscore settings such as _display, _direction, _flexDirection, _flexWrap, _rowGap, _gridTemplateColumns.
- Section/Container/Block/Div use _direction for flex-direction. Non-layout elements use _flexDirection, including responsive suffixed variants.
- Never emit raw unprefixed layout keys such as direction, flexWrap, or justifyContent.
- Flex controls require _display: "flex" or _display: "inline-flex" on the same element.
- Grid controls require _display: "grid" on the same element.

## Style Controls

- Bricks settings first: route visual style into element/global-class settings before using _cssCustom.
- Core supported setting keys include _background, _typography, _border, _padding, _margin, _display, _direction, _flexDirection, _gridTemplateColumns, _columnGap, _rowGap, _overflow, _aspectRatio, _objectFit, _width, _widthMin, _widthMax, _height, _heightMin, and _heightMax.
- Number/unit controls are scalar strings like "24px", not { value, unit } objects.
- Typography belongs under _typography. Root font/color keys are ignored or unsafe.
- Plain external links use { "type": "external", "url": "https://..." }; do not use type: "url".
- section/container/block styles should use _background, _border, _padding, _display, _gridTemplateColumns, _overflow, and _aspectRatio for bands, panels, cards, mockups, collages, and product packs.
- heading/text-basic styles should use _typography colour/size/weight/line-height settings where the design system allows overrides.
- image styles should use _border, _aspectRatio, _objectFit, _overflow, width/height constraints, and media settings; do not hide media treatment only in CSS.

## Font Controls

- Stage B workspaces include \`stage-b-font-system.json\` when Stage A exposes Google Font imports or font role tokens.
- Preserve Stage A font roles: display/heading, body, mono/code, and serif/italic emphasis. Do not collapse all roles into the active theme body font when Stage A uses distinct families.
- Use Bricks typography settings for visible font choices with concrete family names from \`stage-b-font-system.json.roleTokens[].primaryFamily\`: \`_typography: { "font-family": "Inter Tight", "fallback": "system-ui, sans-serif" }\` or the installed Bricks custom font id when Pixflow supplies one.
- Never set Bricks \`_typography.font-family\` to \`var(--font-*)\`. CSS variables may remain in source CSS evidence, but Bricks font-family controls must be concrete names such as \`Impact\`, \`Aptos\`, or \`JetBrains Mono\`.
- Pixflow installs Google Fonts through its Bricks custom font manager before Stage B insertion. Model output must copy \`stage-b-font-system.json\` to \`bricks-result.json.stage_b_font_system\`.
- Never emit Google font \`<link>\`, CSS \`@import\`, \`fonts.googleapis.com\`, \`fonts.gstatic.com\`, or ad hoc \`@font-face\` in Bricks payload CSS/code. Installed fonts are loaded by Bricks.
- For mixed sans/serif headlines, keep editable heading/text content and style inline \`em\` or span emphasis with scoped \`%root%\` CSS using the installed family name.
- If a Stage A font is proprietary or not available from Google/Bricks custom fonts, record the fallback in \`conversion-report.md\` instead of silently substituting a generic system stack.

## Icon Controls

- Stage B workspaces include \`stage-b-icon-system.json\` when Stage A exposes SVG icons, CTA arrows, download/GitHub actions, navigation affordances, or card/proof markers.
- Preserve Stage A icon affordances with Pixflow-installed Tabler SVG icons. Use \`tabler-outline\` by default and \`tabler-filled\` only when the source icon is clearly filled.
- Model output references sidecar icons with \`{ "library": "pixflowSvg", "icon": "pixflow:tabler-outline:arrow-up-right", "width": "<source-width>", "height": "<source-height>" }\`. Preserve the source HTML dimensions from explicit width/height attributes or CSS; do not infer the intended render size from SVG viewBox. Use \`"24"\` only when no usable source dimensions exist. Pixflow installs the requested subset and rewrites this placeholder to the Bricks custom SVG icon control before insertion, for example \`{ "library": "custom_pixflow-icon-set-tabler-outline", "svg": { "id": 123, "icon_id": "icon_tabler_outline_arrow_up_right", "url": "..." }, "width": "32", "height": "20" }\`.
- Button icons belong on the button settings: \`icon\`, \`iconPosition\`, and optional \`iconGap\`. Use icons for source CTA arrows, GitHub/download actions, and compact action affordances when Stage A used them.
- Standalone icon markers use the Bricks \`icon\` element with \`settings.icon\`. Use \`svg\` only for an SVG media/control element, with \`source: "iconSet"\` and \`iconSet\` set to the Pixflow placeholder.
- Style standalone SVG icon elements through global classes with nested \`settings.icon\`, for example \`{ "icon": { "height": "2rem", "width": "2rem", "stroke": { "raw": "var(--accent)", "light": "#ef6b4d" }, "strokeWidth": "2" } }\`. Filled icons use \`fill\`; special cases may use both \`stroke\` and \`fill\`.
- Do not use regular font icon controls \`iconSize\` or \`iconColor\` for Pixflow SVG icons.
- Do not use Bricks Font Awesome font icon classes for Stage B page icons, and do not paste raw \`<svg>\` icon markup into text, code, or _cssCustom.
- Copy \`stage-b-icon-system.json\` to \`bricks-result.json.stage_b_icon_system\` when any sidecar icon is used.

## Page Scripts

- Do not use Bricks code elements for Stage B JavaScript.
- Source JavaScript needed for interaction polish, such as data-reveal IntersectionObserver behavior, belongs in \`bricks-result.json.page_settings.customScriptsBodyFooter\` as a complete \`<script>...</script>\` block.
- Missing behavior for explicit Stage A controls such as tab-like card grids with \`.active\` state also belongs in page settings. Scope scripts to the converted section, preserve keyboard access where practical, and target stable classes/attributes from the Bricks payload.
- Copy the same page settings object to \`bricks-result.json.stage_b_page_settings\` so Pixflow persists it to Bricks page settings during insertion.
- Do not use page scripts for fonts or icons. Fonts use \`stage-b-font-system.json\`; icons use \`stage-b-icon-system.json\`.

## Page-Scoped JS Libraries

- Pixflow bundles supported JS libraries locally and exposes them through Bricks page settings. Do not add CDN script tags, npm imports, external URLs, or code elements for these libraries.
- Declare required libraries in \`bricks-result.json.stage_b_script_libraries.libraries\`. Supported values: \`gsap\`, \`gsap-scrolltrigger\`, \`three\`, \`d3\`, \`p5\`.
- Mirror the declaration in both \`page_settings\` and \`stage_b_page_settings\` with checkbox values:
  - GSAP core: \`"pixflowJsLibraryGsap": "1"\`; page scripts use \`window.gsap\`.
  - GSAP ScrollTrigger: \`"pixflowJsLibraryGsapScrollTrigger": "1"\`; page scripts use \`window.ScrollTrigger\` and must call \`gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger)\`. ScrollTrigger implies GSAP core.
  - Three.js: \`"pixflowJsLibraryThree": "1"\`; page scripts use \`window.THREE\`.
  - D3.js: \`"pixflowJsLibraryD3": "1"\`; page scripts use \`window.d3\`.
  - p5.js: \`"pixflowJsLibraryP5": "1"\`; page scripts use \`window.p5\` or \`new p5(...)\`.
- Three.js is exposed by a module adapter. Initialize after \`window.THREE\` exists, or listen for \`window.addEventListener("pixflow:three-ready", ...)\`.
- Keep all library usage scoped to the converted section/page. If a library is referenced in page scripts, the matching library must be declared and toggled.

## Header And Footer Templates

- Bricks headers and footers are separate \`bricks_template\` posts, not normal page content.
- Header templates use \`_bricks_template_type = "header"\` and Pixflow writes their element tree to the Bricks header area.
- Footer templates use \`_bricks_template_type = "footer"\` and Pixflow writes their element tree to the Bricks footer area.
- Template assignment conditions live in \`_bricks_template_settings.templateConditions\`.
- Sitewide header condition: \`[{ "main": "any" }]\`.
- Current-page-only header condition after Pixflow creates the page: \`[{ "main": "ids", "ids": [pageId], "idsIncludeChildren": false }]\`.
- Exclusions use the same condition shape with \`"exclude": true\`.
- Writing header/footer area content to a regular page has no visible effect in Bricks.
- Stage B model output must keep approved header elements in \`stage_b_header.content\` and approved footer elements in \`stage_b_footer.content\`; Pixflow creates/updates the Bricks templates and conditions during insertion.
- Header inner wrappers must carry explicit Bricks layout controls on the element settings. Preserve the source layout family: grid wrappers use \`_display: "grid"\`, \`_gridTemplateColumns\`, grid alignment, and gaps; flex wrappers use \`_display: "flex"\`, \`_direction\`, optional \`_flexWrap\`, alignment, justification, and gaps.
- Header navigation should use \`nav-menu\` when a real menu source is available. Fallback nav/action blocks must preserve the source layout family and carry matching Bricks controls; do not convert source grid navs to flex unless Stage A was actually flex.
- Footer templates use the same condition contract as headers and must remain separate from page content.

## Color Controls

- Stage B workspaces include \`stage-b-color-system.json\` when Stage A exposed design tokens.
- Pixflow names that colour system after the selected design system, checks for the deterministic native Bricks scheme/category first, and only writes missing variables or palette colours before page insertion.
- CSS variable colours must be Bricks raw color objects: { "raw": "var(--token)" }.
- Native Bricks palette entries for Stage B design systems should use token-backed raw values plus literal fallbacks: { "raw": "var(--token)", "light": "#hex", "name": "token" }.
- Do not put token declarations in a global class such as \`.od-root\`, \`.root\`, or \`*-root\`.
- Do not emit null or empty hex color placeholders.

## Custom CSS

- _cssCustom must contain complete selector blocks.
- _cssCustom is an escape hatch for selectors or effects that cannot be represented by Bricks settings; it must not carry routine layout, background, typography, border, padding, aspect-ratio, or object-fit styling on the root, descendants, relationship selectors, states, or responsive rules.
- An unsupported selector does not justify leaving supported declarations in _cssCustom. For this fixed prototype, attach a purpose-named class to each matched emitted element and move every Bricks-supported declaration into that class/element's native settings. Keep only irreducible pseudo-element content, browser-specific effects, or runtime internals Bricks does not expose.
- Use %root% while authoring class CSS; Pixflow scopes it to the generated class before insertion.
- Do not add page-wide pseudo-background overlays unless the accepted Stage A artifact has that same visible overlay.

## Component Fidelity

- Convert stat rings as separate editable elements: circular number/ring plus separate label text.
- Do not approximate stat rings with a dashed border on the whole stat text element.
- Do not add solid borders to plate/image wrappers unless the Stage A wrapper actually has that border.
- Preserve source border-radius/corner rhythm on buttons, badges, cards, images, and panels with Bricks radius controls or Pixflow radius variables.
- Horizontal wrappers must declare row layout with Bricks controls, not only CSS: _display flex/inline-flex plus _direction row on the same element/class.
- Preserve declared tab/card interfaces as working controls. Do not leave a source-labelled tabs grid as static cards.
- Preserve marquee rows as repeated editable items/tracks with matching spacing and direction. Do not flatten marquee content into malformed text.

## Pixflow Framework Rules

- Sections do not set routine top/bottom padding; Bricks Theme Style owns section spacing.
- Containers do not set routine left/right padding; Bricks Theme Style owns page gutters.
- Theme Style owns body font size, body line height, default heading/text colours, and default button styles.
- Buttons use Bricks button style/type where practical instead of hand-authored button CSS.
- Apply Pixflow colour schemes with pixflowColorScheme on section/container/block/div after approved schemes exist.
`;
}

function renderPixflowPluginMcpMarkdown() {
  return `# Pixflow Plugin MCP

Built-in, always-on Pixflow runtime context. Use this as the source of truth for Pixflow Framework routing, token mapping, Bricks payload constraints, media discipline, framework design-system controls, and class-name safety.

## Active Tools

- pixflow.route.resolve
- pixflow.design_system.resolve
- pixflow.tokens.map
- pixflow.classes.namespace
- pixflow.bricks.reference
- pixflow.google_fonts.install
- pixflow.icon_sets.install_subset
- pixflow.media.policy
- pixflow.qa.inspect

## Rules

- Final output is editable Bricks JSON.
- Stage B starts from Pixflow's clean-room HTML-to-Bricks baseline when the \`bricks-baseline-*\` files are present. Refine that payload instead of rebuilding the page from scratch.
- Read \`stage-b-route-contract.json\`, \`stage-b-theme-style-contract.json\`, and \`stage-b-theme-style-health.json\` before authoring Bricks settings or classes.
- Pixflow Framework is final authority for framework route output.
- Pixflow Design systems are creative direction only at conversion time.
- Compiler resolves final global class IDs and Bricks color IDs.
- No raw hex in Pixflow Framework mode when a token can express the role.
- No CSS variable fallback chains in Pixflow Framework mode.
- Pixflow Framework theme style owns routine spacing and defaults.
- Sections avoid routine vertical padding in Pixflow Framework mode.
- Containers avoid routine inline padding in Pixflow Framework mode.
- When \`safeToLeanOnThemeStyles\` is false, emit explicit page-scoped section, container, button, form, divider, card, and media baselines instead of assuming theme defaults exist.
- For non-Pixflow routes, do not create or mutate Bricks theme styles unless the Stage B preflight question flow records explicit user approval and scope.
- Preserve the source button class names exactly. Do not rename button variants merely to impose a suffix convention.
- Model proposes framework mutations only; Pixflow owns framework scheme and ramp calculations.
- Google Font families from \`stage-b-font-system.json\` are installed by Pixflow into Bricks custom fonts before Stage B insertion. Do not ask the model to load font files in CSS or JavaScript.
- Tabler SVG icons from \`stage-b-icon-system.json\` are built/installed by Pixflow into Bricks custom icon sets before Stage B insertion. Do not ask the model to use Bricks Font Awesome page icons or paste raw SVG icon code.
- Stage B icon placeholders use \`pixflow:<setId>:<iconId>\`, for example \`pixflow:tabler-outline:arrow-up-right\`, inside a Bricks icon control object with \`library: "pixflowSvg"\`, \`width\`, and \`height\` copied from the original HTML icon dimensions.
- Pixflow rewrites placeholders to Bricks custom SVG icon controls such as \`library: "custom_pixflow-icon-set-tabler-outline"\`, \`svg.icon_id: "icon_tabler_outline_arrow_up_right"\`, and the preserved source \`width\`/\`height\`.
- SVG icon styling uses nested Bricks \`settings.icon\` style controls with \`height\`, \`width\`, \`stroke\`, optional \`strokeWidth\`, and \`fill\` for filled icons. Do not use \`iconSize\` or \`iconColor\` for Pixflow SVG icons.

## Class Contract

- compiler_owns_class_ids: true
- model_outputs_intent_not_final_ids: true
- source_class_names_preserved: true
- baseline_global_class_inventory_authoritative: true
- no_new_global_classes_after_baseline: true
- repairs_update_existing_class_settings_only: true
- source class naming convention: authoritative; preserve it exactly
- preset examples that must remain valid: container, stack, grid-2, grid-3, btn, btn-primary
`;
}

async function assertStageBResultExists(resultFile) {
  await assertFileExists(resultFile, 'Stage B Bricks result');
}

async function normalizeStageBGeneratedArtifacts(prepared) {
  const result = await readJsonFile(prepared.resultFile, 'Stage B Bricks result');
  const baselineResult = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.baselineResultFile || ''));
  const persistedConversionPolicy = objectValue(
    await readOptionalJson(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'stage-a', 'conversion-policy.json'))
  );
  const persistedConversionPlan = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.conversionPlanFile || ''));
  // Final delivery deliberately separates Bricks header/footer templates.
  // Reconcile older workspaces through the same helper used before the
  // streamable baseline file is first written.
  attachPixflowStageBBaselinePreviewContent(result, baselineResult.content, {
    sourceFidelityClone: isPixflowStageBSourceFidelityClonePlan(persistedConversionPlan),
  });
  const stageAHtml = await readOptionalText(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'stage-a', 'drafts', 'index.html'));
  const styleMap = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.styleMapFile || ''));
  const stagedFontSystem = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.fontSystemFile || ''));
  const priorResultFontSystem = objectValue(
    result.stage_b_font_system
    || result.stageBFontSystem
    || result.font_system
    || result.fontSystem
  );
  const fontSystem = objectValue(
    (Object.keys(stagedFontSystem).length > 0 ? stagedFontSystem : null)
    || priorResultFontSystem
  );
  const stagedColorSystem = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.colorSystemFile || ''));
  const colorSystem = objectValue(
    (Object.keys(stagedColorSystem).length > 0 ? stagedColorSystem : null)
    || result.stage_b_color_system
    || result.stageBColorSystem
    || result.color_system
    || result.colorSystem
  );
  const routeContract = objectValue(
    result.stage_b_route_contract
    || result.stageBRouteContract
    || await readOptionalJson(prepared.routeContractFile || '')
  );
  normalizeStageBColorTokenReferences(result, colorSystem);
  normalizeStageBPageColorVariables(result, colorSystem);
  normalizeStageBTypographyFontFamilies(result, fontSystem, priorResultFontSystem);
  normalizeStageBPageForegroundInheritance(result);
  normalizeStageBInheritedForegroundColors(result);
  normalizeStageBInheritedIconStyles(result);
  normalizeStageBNativeButtonVariants(result);
  normalizeStageBStaticLinkSettings(result);
  normalizeStageBInvalidNativeForms(result, stageAHtml);
  normalizeStageBSourceIdSelectorClasses(result, styleMap);
  normalizeStageBSectionTagDefaults(result, styleMap);
  normalizeStageBSourceControlSelectorCss(result, styleMap);
  normalizeStageBSourceRichTextDescendantCss(result, styleMap);
  normalizeStageBSourceAttributeSelectorCss(result, styleMap);
  // Source-backed descendant CSS is restored during normalization. Canonicalize
  // its units and selector specificity in the same pass so a subsequent visual
  // repair does not alter the signed Bricks artifact before QA can consume it.
  normalizeStageBSourceRemUnitsForBricks(result);
  normalizeStageBControlSelectorSpecificity(result);
  normalizeStageBFlexDirectionControlKeys(result);
  normalizeStageBBricksSettingsShape(result);
  result.diagnostics = objectValue(result.diagnostics);
  result.diagnostics.nativeEntranceNormalization = normalizeStageBNativeEntranceInteractions(result);
  normalizeStageBHeaderActionLayout(result);
  normalizeStageBTemplateResponsiveVisibility(result);
  result.diagnostics = objectValue(result.diagnostics);
  const priorSourceMediaRestoration = objectValue(result.diagnostics.sourceMediaRestoration);
  const sourceMediaRestoration = restoreStageBSourceMediaFromBaseline(
    result,
    baselineResult,
    prepared.workspaceDir
  );
  result.diagnostics.sourceMediaRestoration = sourceMediaRestoration.restored > 0
    ? {
        ...sourceMediaRestoration,
        restored: Number(priorSourceMediaRestoration.restored || 0) + sourceMediaRestoration.restored,
        elementIds: uniqueStrings([
          ...arrayValue(priorSourceMediaRestoration.elementIds),
          ...sourceMediaRestoration.elementIds,
        ]),
        globalClassIds: uniqueStrings([
          ...arrayValue(priorSourceMediaRestoration.globalClassIds),
          ...sourceMediaRestoration.globalClassIds,
        ]),
      }
    : (Object.keys(priorSourceMediaRestoration).length > 0
        ? priorSourceMediaRestoration
        : sourceMediaRestoration);
  normalizeStageBImageElementSettings(result, prepared.workspaceDir);
  result.diagnostics.routeTokenNormalization = normalizeStageBRouteTokenValues(result, routeContract, {
    conversionProfile: firstString(
      objectValue(result.diagnostics.routeTokenNormalization || result.diagnostics.route_token_normalization).conversionProfile,
      persistedConversionPolicy.conversionProfile,
      persistedConversionPlan.conversionPolicy?.conversionProfile,
      'uploaded_html'
    ),
    sourceFidelityClone: (
      objectValue(persistedConversionPolicy.stageASource || persistedConversionPolicy.stage_a_source).sourceFidelityClone === true
      || objectValue(persistedConversionPolicy.stageASource || persistedConversionPolicy.stage_a_source).source_fidelity_clone === true
      || isPixflowStageBSourceFidelityClonePlan(persistedConversionPlan)
    ),
  });
  normalizeStageBSectionDisplayDefaults(result);
  normalizeStageBGlobalClassLayoutOwners(result);
  normalizeStageBHeadingInheritance(result);
  normalizeStageBInlineTextWrappers(result);
  normalizeStageBChildReferences(result);
  normalizeStageBRootOnlyCustomCss(result, colorSystem);
  // Several fidelity normalizers above append source-backed descendant and
  // attribute-selector CSS after the initial token pass. Re-run alias
  // translation at the end so compiler-restored CSS cannot reintroduce the
  // source variable names that Stage B already mapped to project tokens.
  normalizeStageBColorTokenReferences(result, colorSystem);
  const conversionProfile = firstString(
    persistedConversionPolicy.conversionProfile,
    persistedConversionPlan.conversionPolicy?.conversionProfile,
    'uploaded_html'
  );
  if (conversionProfile === 'prototype_bricks') {
    const generationScope = normalizeStageBGenerationScope(persistedConversionPolicy.generationScope);
    result.diagnostics.sourceLayoutRestoration = restoreStageBSourceLayoutFromBaseline(
      result,
      baselineResult,
      {
        restoreClassNames: generationScope === 'section' || generationScope === 'component',
        restoreElementLayout: true,
      }
    );
    const sourceClassPreservation = preserveScopedPrototypeBricksSourceClasses();
    result.diagnostics.sourceClassPreservation = sourceClassPreservation;
    // Compatibility alias for persisted diagnostics; no class renaming occurs.
    result.diagnostics.scopedBemNormalization = sourceClassPreservation;
  }
  await materializeStageBInlineDataUriAssets(prepared.workspaceDir, result, stageAHtml);
  // Stage B models may rewrite token references recursively and accidentally
  // rewrite the managed sidecar's own sourceCssVariable/tokenAliases evidence.
  // The staged sidecars are compiler-owned inputs, so restore their exact
  // shapes after payload normalization and before authoritative QA/import.
  if (Object.keys(stagedColorSystem).length > 0) {
    result.stage_b_color_system = structuredClone(stagedColorSystem);
    result.color_system = structuredClone(stagedColorSystem);
  }
  if (Object.keys(stagedFontSystem).length > 0) {
    result.stage_b_font_system = structuredClone(stagedFontSystem);
    result.font_system = structuredClone(stagedFontSystem);
  }
  result.diagnostics = objectValue(result.diagnostics);
  const baselineClassPreservation = preserveStageBBaselineClassStructure(result, baselineResult);
  result.diagnostics.baselineClassPreservation = baselineClassPreservation;
  result.diagnostics.bemClassPreservation = baselineClassPreservation;
  result.diagnostics.directStyleClassPromotion = promoteStageBDirectStylesToClasses(result);
  // Direct-style promotion can add layout controls to an existing source
  // class after the first layout-owner pass. Reconcile the final class shape
  // immediately before QA so the class that owns flex/grid controls also owns
  // the matching Bricks display control.
  normalizeStageBGlobalClassLayoutOwners(result);
  result.diagnostics.finalIntrinsicFlexItemDefaults = applyPixflowStageBIntrinsicFlexItemDefaults(
    [
      result.content,
      objectValue(result.stage_b_header).content,
      objectValue(result.stage_b_footer).content,
      result.baseline_preview_content,
    ],
    result.global_classes,
    { sourceFidelityClone: isPixflowStageBSourceFidelityClonePlan(persistedConversionPlan) },
  );
  // Direct-style promotion intentionally removes unclassed layout controls.
  // Re-apply the header template contract after that pass so wrappers that do
  // not own a global class retain their explicit flex and narrow-screen rules.
  normalizeStageBHeaderTemplateContract(result, persistedConversionPlan.headerPlan, {
    preserveSourceHierarchy: isPixflowStageBSourceFidelityClonePlan(persistedConversionPlan),
  });
  result.diagnostics.templateAreaSeparation = normalizeStageBTemplateAreaSeparation(
    result,
    persistedConversionPlan.headerPlan,
    persistedConversionPlan.footerPlan,
  );
  const stagedIconSystem = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.iconSystemFile || ''));
  const resultIconSystem = objectValue(
    result.stage_b_icon_system
      || result.stageBIconSystem
      || result.icon_system
      || result.iconSystem
  );
  const normalizedIconSystem = Object.keys(resultIconSystem).length > 0
    ? resultIconSystem
    : stagedIconSystem;
  const iconPlaceholderNormalization = normalizeStageBIconPlaceholderContracts(result, normalizedIconSystem);
  if (Object.keys(normalizedIconSystem).length > 0 && iconPlaceholderNormalization.added > 0) {
    result.stage_b_icon_system = normalizedIconSystem;
    result.stageBIconSystem = normalizedIconSystem;
    result.icon_system = normalizedIconSystem;
    result.iconSystem = normalizedIconSystem;
    if (firstString(prepared.iconSystemFile)) {
      await writeJsonFile(prepared.iconSystemFile, normalizedIconSystem);
    }
  }
  result.diagnostics.iconPlaceholderNormalization = iconPlaceholderNormalization;
  if (conversionProfile === 'prototype_bricks') {
    const sourceClassNames = extractStageBClassUsage(stageAHtml).map((item) => firstString(item?.name)).filter(Boolean);
    result.diagnostics.sourceClassInventory = enforceStageBSourceClassInventory(result, sourceClassNames, {
      baselineResult,
    });
    result.diagnostics.classAttributeDeduplication = dedupeStageBClassAttributesAgainstGlobalClasses(result);
    const sourceCss = extractStageBStyleText(stageAHtml).trim();
    if (sourceCss) {
      const pageSettings = objectValue(result.pageSettings || result.page_settings || result.stage_b_page_settings);
      const marker = '/* Pixflow Stage A source CSS fallback */';
      const customCss = firstString(pageSettings.customCss);
      pageSettings.customCss = customCss.includes(marker)
        ? customCss
        : [customCss, marker, sourceCss].filter(Boolean).join('\n\n');
      result.pageSettings = pageSettings;
      result.page_settings = pageSettings;
      result.stage_b_page_settings = pageSettings;
      normalizeStageBColorTokenReferences(result, colorSystem);
    }
  }
  recordStageBInlineInheritanceClass(result);
  recordStageBBlockquoteInheritanceClass(result);
  await writeJsonFile(prepared.resultFile, result);
  await ensureStageBHandoffCritique(prepared, result);

  const content = Array.isArray(result.content) ? result.content : [];
  const globalClasses = Array.isArray(result.global_classes)
    ? result.global_classes
    : Array.isArray(result.globalClasses)
      ? result.globalClasses
      : [];
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const headerContent = Array.isArray(headerSpec.content)
    ? headerSpec.content
    : (Array.isArray(result.header_content) ? result.header_content : []);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  const footerContent = Array.isArray(footerSpec.content)
    ? footerSpec.content
    : (Array.isArray(result.footer_content) ? result.footer_content : []);
  const pageEditChangeReport = objectValue(result.page_edit_change_report || result.pageEditChangeReport);

  const sidecars = [
    [prepared.payloadFile, content],
    [prepared.globalClassesFile, globalClasses],
    [prepared.headerPayloadFile, headerContent],
    [prepared.footerPayloadFile, footerContent],
  ];
  if (Object.keys(pageEditChangeReport).length > 0 && firstString(prepared.pageEditChangeReportFile)) {
    sidecars.push([prepared.pageEditChangeReportFile, pageEditChangeReport]);
  }
  for (const [filePath, value] of sidecars) {
    if (firstString(filePath)) {
      await writeJsonFile(filePath, value);
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBHeaderTemplateContract(result, headerPlan, options = {}) {
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const headerContent = Array.isArray(headerSpec.content)
    ? headerSpec.content
    : (Array.isArray(result.header_content) ? result.header_content : []);
  if (headerContent.length === 0) return;
  const classes = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  applyPixflowStageBHeaderBaselineContract(headerContent, headerPlan, {
    globalClasses: classes,
  }, options);
  if (Array.isArray(headerSpec.content)) {
    headerSpec.content = headerContent;
    if (result.stage_b_header && typeof result.stage_b_header === 'object') {
      result.stage_b_header = headerSpec;
    } else {
      result.stageBHeader = headerSpec;
    }
  } else {
    result.header_content = headerContent;
  }
}

export function normalizeStageBTemplateAreaSeparation(result, headerPlan, footerPlan) {
  const content = arrayValue(result.content);
  if (content.length === 0) {
    return { applied: false, removedElementCount: 0, removedAreas: [] };
  }
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  const headerContent = arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent);
  const footerContent = arrayValue(footerSpec.content || result.footer_content || result.footerContent);
  const includeHeader = headerSpec.includeHeader === true
    || headerSpec.include_header === true
    || objectValue(headerPlan).includeHeader === true;
  const includeFooter = footerSpec.includeFooter === true
    || footerSpec.include_footer === true
    || objectValue(footerPlan).includeFooter === true;
  if ((!includeHeader || headerContent.length === 0) && (!includeFooter || footerContent.length === 0)) {
    return { applied: false, removedElementCount: 0, removedAreas: [] };
  }

  const byId = new Map(content
    .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const childrenByParent = new Map();
  for (const element of content) {
    const id = firstString(element?.id);
    const parent = firstString(element?.parent);
    if (!id || !parent) continue;
    const children = childrenByParent.get(parent) || [];
    children.push(id);
    childrenByParent.set(parent, children);
  }
  const descendants = (rootId) => {
    const seen = new Set();
    const queue = [rootId];
    while (queue.length > 0) {
      const id = firstString(queue.shift());
      if (!id || seen.has(id)) continue;
      seen.add(id);
      for (const childId of arrayValue(childrenByParent.get(id))) queue.push(childId);
    }
    return seen;
  };
  const sourceMarker = (element) => arrayValue(objectValue(element?.settings)._attributes)
    .map((attribute) => objectValue(attribute))
    .filter((attribute) => ['data-od-id', 'data-pf-source-id', 'id'].includes(firstString(attribute.name)))
    .map((attribute) => firstString(attribute.value))
    .filter(Boolean);
  const provenance = arrayValue(
    result.stage_b_source_provenance
      || result.stageBSourceProvenance
      || objectValue(result.stage_b_structure_report || result.stageBStructureReport).provenance,
  );
  const sourceIdsByElementId = new Map();
  for (const record of provenance) {
    const elementId = firstString(record?.bricksElementId, record?.bricks_element_id);
    const sourceNodeId = firstString(record?.sourceNodeId, record?.source_node_id);
    if (!elementId || !sourceNodeId) continue;
    const sourceIds = sourceIdsByElementId.get(elementId) || new Set();
    sourceIds.add(sourceNodeId);
    sourceIdsByElementId.set(elementId, sourceIds);
  }
  const sourceIdsForElement = (element) => {
    const provenanceSourceIds = sourceIdsByElementId.get(firstString(element?.id));
    // The final header contract may add the originally selected nested id as a
    // template marker on a promoted responsive boundary. Source provenance is
    // the authoritative identity when present; combining both identities would
    // report and remove the already-covered nested subtree a second time.
    return provenanceSourceIds?.size > 0
      ? new Set(provenanceSourceIds)
      : new Set(sourceMarker(element));
  };
  const templateRootSourceIds = (templateContent) => {
    const templateIds = new Set(templateContent.map((element) => firstString(element?.id)).filter(Boolean));
    const roots = templateContent.filter((element) => {
      const parent = firstString(element?.parent);
      return !parent || !templateIds.has(parent);
    });
    return new Set(roots.flatMap((element) => [...sourceIdsForElement(element)]));
  };
  const rootMatchesSemanticArea = (element, area) => {
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const tag = firstString(settings.tag, element?.name).toLowerCase();
    return tag === area || firstString(element?.name).toLowerCase() === area;
  };
  const removeIds = new Set();
  const removedAreas = [];
  for (const [area, enabled, plan, templateContent] of [
    ['header', includeHeader, headerPlan, headerContent],
    ['footer', includeFooter, footerPlan, footerContent],
  ]) {
    if (!enabled) continue;
    const exactTemplateSourceIds = templateRootSourceIds(templateContent);
    const selectedSourceId = firstString(
      objectValue(plan).selectedSectionOdId,
      objectValue(plan).selected_section_od_id,
    );
    let roots = exactTemplateSourceIds.size > 0
      ? content.filter((element) => (
        [...sourceIdsForElement(element)].some((sourceNodeId) => exactTemplateSourceIds.has(sourceNodeId))
      ))
      : [];
    if (roots.length === 0 && selectedSourceId) {
      roots = content.filter((element) => sourceIdsForElement(element).has(selectedSourceId));
    }
    // Semantic fallback is intentionally legacy-only. When a plan supplies an
    // exact source identity, removing a different semantic <header>/<footer>
    // can destroy ordinary page content (for example an editorial hero).
    if (roots.length === 0 && !selectedSourceId && exactTemplateSourceIds.size === 0) {
      roots = content.filter((element) => (
        !firstString(element?.parent) && rootMatchesSemanticArea(element, area)
      ));
    }
    for (const root of roots) {
      const rootId = firstString(root?.id);
      if (!rootId) continue;
      const ids = descendants(rootId);
      ids.forEach((id) => removeIds.add(id));
      removedAreas.push({
        area,
        rootId,
        sourceNodeId: [...sourceIdsForElement(root)][0] || '',
        elementCount: ids.size,
      });
    }
  }
  if (removeIds.size === 0) {
    return { applied: false, removedElementCount: 0, removedAreas: [] };
  }
  result.content = content.filter((element) => !removeIds.has(firstString(element?.id)));
  return {
    applied: true,
    removedElementCount: removeIds.size,
    removedAreas,
  };
}

function normalizeStageBStaticLinkSettings(result) {
  const normalizeValue = (value) => {
    const source = firstString(value);
    const repeated = source.match(/^(\S+)\s+\1$/);
    if (!repeated) return source;
    const candidate = firstString(repeated[1]);
    return /^(?:#|\/(?!\/)|https?:\/\/|mailto:|tel:)/i.test(candidate) ? candidate : source;
  };
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      for (const item of value) visit(item);
      return;
    }
    if (value.link && typeof value.link === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value.link)) {
      for (const key of ['url', 'href', 'useDynamicData']) {
        if (typeof value.link[key] === 'string') {
          value.link[key] = normalizeValue(value.link[key]);
        }
      }
    }
    for (const child of Object.values(value)) visit(child);
  };
  visit(result);
}

function normalizeStageBNativeEntranceInteractions(result) {
  const buckets = [
    ['content', arrayValue(result.content)],
    ['header_content', arrayValue(result.header_content)],
    ['footer_content', arrayValue(result.footer_content)],
    ['stage_b_header.content', arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content)],
    ['stage_b_footer.content', arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content)],
  ];
  const seen = new Set();
  let markerCount = 0;
  let restoredCount = 0;
  let replacedCount = 0;
  let suppressedMotionOwnerConflictCount = 0;
  const isManagedEntrance = (candidate) => (
    firstString(candidate?.titleEditable) === 'Pixflow entrance animation'
    || (
      firstString(candidate?.trigger) === 'enterView'
      && firstString(candidate?.action) === 'startAnimation'
      && PIXFLOW_STAGE_B_NATIVE_ENTRANCE_ANIMATIONS.has(firstString(candidate?.animationType))
    )
  );

  for (const [bucketName, elements] of buckets) {
    for (let index = 0; index < elements.length; index += 1) {
      const element = elements[index];
      if (!element || typeof element !== 'object') continue;
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      const identity = firstString(element.id, `${bucketName}:${index}`);
      if (seen.has(identity)) continue;
      seen.add(identity);

      const attrs = {};
      for (const attribute of arrayValue(settings._attributes)) {
        const name = firstString(attribute?.name).toLowerCase();
        if (name) attrs[name] = firstString(attribute?.value);
      }
      if (!firstString(attrs['data-pixflow-animation'])) continue;
      markerCount += 1;

      const motionHook = firstString(attrs['data-pixflow-motion']);
      if (motionHook) {
        settings._interactions = arrayValue(settings._interactions).filter((candidate) => !isManagedEntrance(candidate));
        suppressedMotionOwnerConflictCount += 1;
        continue;
      }

      const interaction = buildPixflowStageBEntranceInteraction({
        tag: firstString(settings.tag, element.name, 'div'),
        sourceIndex: identity,
        attrs,
      }, { scope: `stage-b-normalized:${bucketName}` });
      if (!interaction) continue;

      const existing = arrayValue(settings._interactions);
      const managedIndex = existing.findIndex(isManagedEntrance);
      if (managedIndex >= 0) {
        settings._interactions = existing.map((candidate, candidateIndex) => (
          candidateIndex === managedIndex ? interaction : candidate
        ));
        replacedCount += 1;
      } else {
        settings._interactions = [...existing, interaction];
        restoredCount += 1;
      }
    }
  }

  return {
    markerCount,
    restoredCount,
    replacedCount,
    suppressedMotionOwnerConflictCount,
  };
}

export function normalizeStageBBricksSettingsShape(result) {
  const globalClasses = Array.isArray(result.global_classes)
    ? result.global_classes
    : (Array.isArray(result.globalClasses) ? result.globalClasses : []);
  const globalClassById = new Map(globalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));

  const claimRepairClass = (element, settingsPatch) => {
    const patch = objectValue(settingsPatch);
    if (Object.keys(patch).length === 0) return { target: 'none', classId: '' };
    return applyStageBRepairSettings(element, globalClassById, patch);
  };

  const visitSettings = (settings, element = null, options = {}) => {
    if (!settings || typeof settings !== 'object' || Array.isArray(settings)) return;
    const directRepairSettings = {};
    const moveStyleToClass = Boolean(element) && !options.allowDirectElementStyles;
    const rootStyleKeyMap = {
      display: '_display',
      direction: '_direction',
      flexWrap: '_flexWrap',
      justifyContent: '_justifyContent',
      alignItems: '_alignItems',
      rowGap: '_rowGap',
      columnGap: '_columnGap',
      gridTemplateColumns: '_gridTemplateColumns',
      gridGap: '_gridGap',
      padding: '_padding',
      margin: '_margin',
      background: '_background',
      border: '_border',
      width: '_width',
      height: '_height',
      minWidth: '_widthMin',
      maxWidth: '_widthMax',
      minHeight: '_heightMin',
      maxHeight: '_heightMax',
    };
    for (const [rawKey, normalizedKey] of Object.entries(rootStyleKeyMap)) {
      if (
        Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, rawKey)
        && !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, normalizedKey)
      ) {
        if (moveStyleToClass) {
          directRepairSettings[normalizedKey] = settings[rawKey];
        } else {
          settings[normalizedKey] = settings[rawKey];
        }
        delete settings[rawKey];
      }
    }
    const rootTypographyKeyMap = {
      color: 'color',
      fontSize: 'font-size',
      fontFamily: 'font-family',
      fontWeight: 'font-weight',
      lineHeight: 'line-height',
      letterSpacing: 'letter-spacing',
      textAlign: 'text-align',
    };
    for (const [rawKey, normalizedKey] of Object.entries(rootTypographyKeyMap)) {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, rawKey)) {
        if (moveStyleToClass) {
          directRepairSettings._typography = objectValue(directRepairSettings._typography);
          if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(directRepairSettings._typography, normalizedKey)) {
            directRepairSettings._typography[normalizedKey] = settings[rawKey];
          }
        } else {
          settings._typography = objectValue(settings._typography);
          if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings._typography, normalizedKey)) {
            settings._typography[normalizedKey] = settings[rawKey];
          }
        }
        delete settings[rawKey];
      }
    }
    for (const rawKey of ['font-size', 'font-family', 'font-weight', 'line-height', 'letter-spacing', 'text-align']) {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, rawKey)) {
        if (moveStyleToClass) {
          directRepairSettings._typography = objectValue(directRepairSettings._typography);
          if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(directRepairSettings._typography, rawKey)) {
            directRepairSettings._typography[rawKey] = settings[rawKey];
          }
        } else {
          settings._typography = objectValue(settings._typography);
          if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings._typography, rawKey)) {
            settings._typography[rawKey] = settings[rawKey];
          }
        }
        delete settings[rawKey];
      }
    }
    if (moveStyleToClass) {
      const disallowedDirectKeys = filterStageBDisallowedElementDirectStyleKeys(
        collectStageBElementDirectStyleKeys(settings),
        { elementName: firstString(element?.name) }
      );
      for (const directKey of disallowedDirectKeys) {
        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, directKey)) continue;
        directRepairSettings[directKey] = settings[directKey];
        delete settings[directKey];
      }
    }
    if (moveStyleToClass) {
      const outcome = claimRepairClass(element, directRepairSettings);
      if (outcome.target === 'skipped_unclassed') {
        // Baseline class references are restored later in normalization. Keep
        // the patch until that happens so the final promotion pass can attach
        // it to the restored class instead of silently discarding the repair.
        Object.assign(settings, directRepairSettings);
      }
    }
  };

  for (const element of collectStageBAllElements(result)) {
    const templateArea = stageBElementTemplateArea(result, element);
    const allowDirectElementStyles = templateArea === 'header' || templateArea === 'footer';
    visitSettings(objectValue(element?.settings), element, { allowDirectElementStyles });
  }
  for (const classItem of arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses)) {
    visitSettings(objectValue(classItem?.settings));
  }
}

function stageBElementTemplateArea(result, element) {
  const id = firstString(element?.id);
  if (!id) return '';
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  if (arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent).some((item) => firstString(item?.id) === id)) {
    return 'header';
  }
  if (arrayValue(footerSpec.content || result.footer_content || result.footerContent).some((item) => firstString(item?.id) === id)) {
    return 'footer';
  }
  return '';
}

function normalizeStageBImageElementSettings(result, workspaceDir = '') {
  for (const element of collectStageBAllElements(result)) {
    if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'image') continue;
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    element.settings = settings;
    const attributes = Array.isArray(settings._attributes) ? settings._attributes : [];
    if (attributes.length > 0) {
      settings._attributes = attributes.filter((attribute) => {
        const name = firstString(attribute?.name).toLowerCase();
        if (name === 'loading') {
          if (!firstString(settings.loading)) settings.loading = firstString(attribute?.value, 'lazy');
          return false;
        }
        if (name === 'decoding') {
          return false;
        }
        return true;
      });
      if (settings._attributes.length === 0) {
        delete settings._attributes;
      }
    }

    const image = objectValue(settings.image);
    const refs = uniqueStrings([
      firstString(image.url),
      firstString(image.full),
      firstString(image.sourceUrl),
    ].filter(Boolean));
    const missingLocalRefs = refs.filter((ref) => (
      isStageBLocalAssetRef(ref)
      && (!workspaceDir || !stageBLocalAssetExists(workspaceDir, ref))
    ));
    if (missingLocalRefs.length === 0) {
      const remoteUrl = refs.find((ref) => /^https?:\/\//i.test(ref));
      const attachmentId = Number(image.id || image.attachmentId || 0);
      if (remoteUrl && (!Number.isFinite(attachmentId) || attachmentId <= 0)) {
        image.url = remoteUrl;
        image.full = firstString(image.full, remoteUrl);
        image.sourceUrl = firstString(image.sourceUrl, remoteUrl);
        image.external = remoteUrl;
        image.size = firstString(image.size, 'full');
      }
      continue;
    }

    const alt = firstString(settings.altText, image.alt, 'Image');
    const text = encodeURIComponent(alt.replace(/\s+/g, '+').slice(0, 48));
    // Use an explicitly typed SVG URL so WordPress/Bricks keeps this as an
    // external image. The extensionless endpoint was treated as a sideload;
    // some local stacks then persisted HTTP chunk/gzip framing as a fake JPEG.
    const placeholder = `https://placehold.co/1200x750/f0f0f5/0f1b2d.svg?text=${text}`;
    settings.image = {
      ...image,
      url: placeholder,
      full: placeholder,
      sourceUrl: placeholder,
      external: placeholder,
      size: firstString(image.size, 'full'),
    };
  }
}

export function normalizeStageBImageElementSettingsForTest({ result = {}, workspaceDir = '' } = {}) {
  normalizeStageBImageElementSettings(result, workspaceDir);
  return result;
}

function restoreStageBSourceMediaFromBaseline(result, baselineResult, workspaceDir = '') {
  const summary = {
    source: 'compiler_baseline_stable_id',
    restored: 0,
    elementIds: [],
    globalClassIds: [],
  };
  if (!workspaceDir || Object.keys(baselineResult).length === 0) return summary;

  const restoreObject = (currentValue, baselineValue) => {
    if (!baselineValue || typeof baselineValue !== 'object' || Array.isArray(baselineValue)) {
      return 0;
    }
    const current = objectValue(currentValue);
    let restored = 0;
    for (const [key, baselineChild] of Object.entries(baselineValue)) {
      if (
        typeof baselineChild === 'string'
        && isStageBLocalMediaRef(baselineChild)
        && stageBLocalAssetExists(workspaceDir, baselineChild)
      ) {
        if (current[key] !== baselineChild) {
          current[key] = baselineChild;
          restored += 1;
        }
        continue;
      }
      if (baselineChild && typeof baselineChild === 'object' && !Array.isArray(baselineChild)) {
        const hadCurrentObject = Boolean(current[key] && typeof current[key] === 'object' && !Array.isArray(current[key]));
        const nextCurrent = hadCurrentObject ? current[key] : {};
        const nestedRestored = restoreObject(nextCurrent, baselineChild);
        if (nestedRestored > 0) {
          current[key] = nextCurrent;
          restored += nestedRestored;
        }
      }
    }
    return restored;
  };

  const currentElements = new Map(
    collectStageBAllElements(result)
      .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
      .filter(([id]) => id)
  );
  for (const baselineElement of collectStageBAllElements(baselineResult)) {
    const id = firstString(baselineElement?.id);
    const currentElement = currentElements.get(id);
    if (!id || !currentElement) continue;
    const restored = restoreObject(
      objectValue(currentElement.settings),
      objectValue(baselineElement.settings)
    );
    if (restored > 0) {
      summary.restored += restored;
      summary.elementIds.push(id);
    }
  }

  const currentClasses = new Map(
    arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses)
      .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
      .filter(([id]) => id)
  );
  for (const baselineClass of arrayValue(baselineResult.global_classes || baselineResult.globalClasses)) {
    const id = firstString(baselineClass?.id);
    const currentClass = currentClasses.get(id);
    if (!id || !currentClass) continue;
    const restored = restoreObject(
      objectValue(currentClass.settings),
      objectValue(baselineClass.settings)
    );
    if (restored > 0) {
      summary.restored += restored;
      summary.globalClassIds.push(id);
    }
  }

  summary.elementIds = uniqueStrings(summary.elementIds);
  summary.globalClassIds = uniqueStrings(summary.globalClassIds);
  return summary;
}

const STAGE_B_SOURCE_LAYOUT_SETTING_KEYS = new Set([
  '_display', '_direction', '_flexDirection', '_flexWrap',
  '_alignItems', '_alignContent', '_alignSelf',
  '_justifyContent', '_justifyItems', '_justifySelf',
  '_columnGap', '_rowGap', '_gap', '_gridGap',
  '_width', '_widthMin', '_widthMax',
  '_height', '_heightMin', '_heightMax',
  '_padding', '_margin', '_position', '_top', '_right', '_bottom', '_left',
  '_zIndex', '_order', '_flexGrow', '_flexShrink', '_flexBasis',
  '_gridTemplateColumns', '_gridTemplateRows', '_gridColumn', '_gridRow',
  '_aspectRatio', '_overflow',
]);

function isStageBSourceLayoutSettingKey(key) {
  return STAGE_B_SOURCE_LAYOUT_SETTING_KEYS.has(firstString(key).split(':')[0]);
}

/**
 * Stage A's clean-room compiler is the layout authority for generated HTML.
 * Restore its native Bricks controls by stable element/global-class id after a
 * model-authored Stage B pass, while leaving non-layout semantic/style edits in
 * place. Responsive controls use the same `key:breakpoint` rule as base keys.
 */
export function restoreStageBSourceLayoutFromBaseline(result, baselineResult, options = {}) {
  const summary = {
    source: 'compiler_baseline_stable_id',
    restoredElementCount: 0,
    restoredGlobalClassCount: 0,
    restoredSettingCount: 0,
    elementIds: [],
    globalClassIds: [],
  };
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object' || !baselineResult || typeof baselineResult !== 'object') {
    return summary;
  }

  const restoreSettings = (currentValue, baselineValue, keyPredicate = isStageBSourceLayoutSettingKey) => {
    const current = objectValue(currentValue);
    const baseline = objectValue(baselineValue);
    let restored = 0;
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(baseline)) {
      if (!keyPredicate(key)) continue;
      if (JSON.stringify(current[key]) !== JSON.stringify(value)) {
        current[key] = structuredClone(value);
        restored += 1;
      }
    }
    const baselineClasses = uniqueStrings(arrayValue(baseline._cssGlobalClasses).map(firstString).filter(Boolean));
    if (baselineClasses.length > 0) {
      const nextClasses = uniqueStrings([...baselineClasses, ...arrayValue(current._cssGlobalClasses)]);
      if (JSON.stringify(nextClasses) !== JSON.stringify(arrayValue(current._cssGlobalClasses))) {
        current._cssGlobalClasses = nextClasses;
        restored += 1;
      }
    }
    return restored;
  };

  const currentElements = new Map(collectStageBAllElements(result)
    .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  for (const baselineElement of collectStageBAllElements(baselineResult)) {
    const id = firstString(baselineElement?.id);
    const currentElement = currentElements.get(id);
    if (!id || !currentElement) continue;
    currentElement.settings = objectValue(currentElement.settings);
    const restored = options.restoreElementLayout === false
      ? restoreSettings(currentElement.settings, { _cssGlobalClasses: objectValue(baselineElement.settings)._cssGlobalClasses })
      : restoreSettings(
          currentElement.settings,
          baselineElement.settings,
          (key) => isStageBElementNativeLayoutControlKey(firstString(key).split(':')[0])
        );
    if (restored > 0) {
      summary.restoredElementCount += 1;
      summary.restoredSettingCount += restored;
      summary.elementIds.push(id);
    }
  }

  const currentGlobalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const currentClassesById = new Map(currentGlobalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  for (const baselineClass of arrayValue(baselineResult.global_classes || baselineResult.globalClasses)) {
    const id = firstString(baselineClass?.id);
    if (!id) continue;
    let currentClass = currentClassesById.get(id);
    if (!currentClass) {
      currentClass = { id, name: firstString(baselineClass?.name), settings: {} };
      currentGlobalClasses.push(currentClass);
      currentClassesById.set(id, currentClass);
    }
    currentClass.settings = objectValue(currentClass.settings);
    let restored = restoreSettings(currentClass.settings, baselineClass.settings);
    if (options.restoreClassNames === true && firstString(baselineClass?.name) && currentClass.name !== baselineClass.name) {
      currentClass.name = baselineClass.name;
      restored += 1;
    }
    if (restored > 0) {
      summary.restoredGlobalClassCount += 1;
      summary.restoredSettingCount += restored;
      summary.globalClassIds.push(id);
    }
  }
  result.global_classes = currentGlobalClasses;
  summary.elementIds = uniqueStrings(summary.elementIds);
  summary.globalClassIds = uniqueStrings(summary.globalClassIds);
  return summary;
}

function normalizeStageBHeaderActionLayout(result) {
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const elements = arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent);
  if (elements.length === 0) return;
  const byId = new Map(elements.map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element]));
  const globalClassesById = new Map(arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses).map((classItem) => [
    firstString(classItem?.id),
    classItem,
  ]));

  for (const element of elements) {
    if (!element || typeof element !== 'object' || Array.isArray(element)) continue;
    const childIds = arrayValue(element.children).map((id) => firstString(id)).filter(Boolean);
    const hasButtonChild = childIds.some((id) => firstString(byId.get(id)?.name) === 'button');
    const classItems = arrayValue(objectValue(element.settings)._cssGlobalClasses)
      .map((id) => globalClassesById.get(firstString(id)))
      .filter(Boolean);
    const classNames = classItems
      .map((classItem) => firstString(classItem?.name))
      .join(' ');
    if (!hasButtonChild && !/site-header__(?:actions|nav)\b/i.test(classNames)) {
      continue;
    }
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    element.settings = settings;
    const classSetting = (key) => firstString(...classItems.map((classItem) => objectValue(classItem?.settings)[key]));
    const effectiveDisplay = firstString(settings._display, classSetting('_display'));
    // The outer header wrapper commonly contains a CTA while owning a source
    // grid layout. Treating every button-containing wrapper as an action row
    // writes inline flex controls that override the accepted source class.
    if (effectiveDisplay === 'grid' || classSetting('_gridTemplateColumns')) {
      continue;
    }
    // A source-authored class layout is already the fidelity authority. Do not
    // add isolated inline flex defaults (for example only `_flexWrap`) to an
    // element whose specific class owns `display:flex`; those defaults both
    // distort the accepted source and fail Bricks' same-owner layout contract.
    if (!firstString(settings._display) && classItems.some((classItem) => (
      ['flex', 'inline-flex'].includes(firstString(objectValue(classItem?.settings)._display).toLowerCase())
    ))) {
      continue;
    }
    if (!firstString(settings._display) && !classSetting('_display')) settings._display = 'flex';
    if (!firstString(settings._direction) && !classSetting('_direction')) settings._direction = 'row';
    if (!firstString(settings._flexWrap) && !classSetting('_flexWrap')) settings._flexWrap = 'wrap';
    if (!firstString(settings._alignItems) && !classSetting('_alignItems')) settings._alignItems = 'center';
    if (!firstString(settings._justifyContent) && !classSetting('_justifyContent')) settings._justifyContent = hasButtonChild ? 'flex-end' : 'center';
    if (!firstString(settings._columnGap) && !classSetting('_columnGap')) settings._columnGap = 'var(--pixflow-bricks-handoff-at-space-m)';
    if (!firstString(settings._rowGap) && !classSetting('_rowGap')) settings._rowGap = 'var(--pixflow-bricks-handoff-at-space-xs)';
  }
}

function normalizeStageBTemplateResponsiveVisibility(result) {
  const globalClassesById = new Map(arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses).map((classItem) => [
    firstString(classItem?.id),
    classItem,
  ]));
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  const templateElements = [
    ...arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent),
    ...arrayValue(footerSpec.content || result.footer_content || result.footerContent),
  ];
  for (const element of templateElements) {
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const classItems = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses)
      .map((classId) => globalClassesById.get(firstString(classId)))
      .filter(Boolean);
    for (const suffix of ['tablet_portrait', 'mobile_landscape', 'mobile_portrait']) {
      const key = `_display:${suffix}`;
      const hiddenByClass = classItems.some((classItem) => (
        firstString(objectValue(classItem?.settings)[key]).toLowerCase() === 'none'
      ));
      if (hiddenByClass && !firstString(settings[key])) {
        // Bricks emits each global class in registry order. A later base class
        // with display:flex can otherwise override an earlier responsive hide
        // at equal specificity. The template element ID rule is native Bricks
        // state and wins deterministically without resorting to !important.
        settings[key] = 'none';
      }
    }
    if (element && typeof element === 'object') element.settings = settings;
  }
}

const PIXFLOW_STAGE_B_LAYOUT_ELEMENT_NAMES = new Set(['section', 'container', 'block', 'div']);

/**
 * Keep flex-direction on the control Bricks actually serializes for each
 * element family. Bricks layout elements use `_direction`; every non-layout
 * element uses `_flexDirection`. Global classes may be shared, so retain both
 * representations only when both element families reference the class.
 */
function normalizeStageBFlexDirectionControlKeys(result) {
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;

  const elements = collectStageBAllElements(result);
  const classUsage = new Map();
  const directionEntries = (settings) => Object.entries(settings).filter(([key]) => (
    key === '_direction' || key.startsWith('_direction:')
  ));
  const flexDirectionKey = (directionKey) => directionKey.replace(/^_direction/, '_flexDirection');
  const moveToNonLayoutControl = (settings) => {
    for (const [directionKey, value] of directionEntries(settings)) {
      const targetKey = flexDirectionKey(directionKey);
      if (settings[targetKey] === undefined || settings[targetKey] === '') {
        settings[targetKey] = value;
      }
      delete settings[directionKey];
    }
  };

  for (const element of elements) {
    const elementName = firstString(element?.name).toLowerCase();
    const isLayoutElement = PIXFLOW_STAGE_B_LAYOUT_ELEMENT_NAMES.has(elementName);
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    if (!isLayoutElement) moveToNonLayoutControl(settings);
    if (element && typeof element === 'object') element.settings = settings;

    for (const classId of arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses).map((value) => firstString(value)).filter(Boolean)) {
      const usage = classUsage.get(classId) || { layout: false, nonLayout: false };
      if (isLayoutElement) usage.layout = true;
      else usage.nonLayout = true;
      classUsage.set(classId, usage);
    }
  }

  for (const classItem of arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses)) {
    const usage = classUsage.get(firstString(classItem?.id));
    if (!usage?.nonLayout) continue;
    const settings = objectValue(classItem?.settings);
    for (const [directionKey, value] of directionEntries(settings)) {
      const targetKey = flexDirectionKey(directionKey);
      if (settings[targetKey] === undefined || settings[targetKey] === '') {
        settings[targetKey] = value;
      }
      if (!usage.layout) delete settings[directionKey];
    }
    if (classItem && typeof classItem === 'object') classItem.settings = settings;
  }
}

function collectStageBAllElements(result) {
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  return [
    ...arrayValue(result.content),
    ...arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent),
    ...arrayValue(footerSpec.content || result.footer_content || result.footerContent),
  ];
}

function normalizeStageBColorTokenReferences(result, colorSystem) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks color variable names are project-scoped to prevent
  // one handoff's generic Stage A tokens (`--bg`, `--accent`, etc.) from
  // colliding with another project or another Bricks color scheme.
  const aliases = objectValue(colorSystem.tokenAliases);
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object' || Object.keys(aliases).length === 0) {
    return;
  }
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      return rewriteStageBColorTokenReferences(value, aliases);
    }
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      return value.map((item) => visit(item));
    }
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') {
      return value;
    }
    for (const [key, childValue] of Object.entries(value)) {
      if (key === 'tokenAliases') {
        continue;
      }
      value[key] = visit(childValue);
    }
    return value;
  };

  for (const key of [
    'content',
    'header_content',
    'footer_content',
    'global_classes',
    'globalClasses',
    'page_settings',
    'pageSettings',
    'stage_b_page_settings',
    'stageBPageSettings',
    // Pixflow-owned: page-scoped Bricks theme style payloads are generated
    // before color-system normalization, so their source `var(--bg)` style
    // references must be rewritten to project-scoped variables too.
    'stage_b_theme_style_payload',
    'stageBThemeStylePayload',
    'stage_b_header',
    'stageBHeader',
    'stage_b_footer',
    'stageBFooter',
  ]) {
    if (key in result) {
      result[key] = visit(result[key]);
    }
  }
}

async function ensureStageBHandoffCritique(prepared, result) {
  const critiqueFile = path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'handoff-critique.md');
  const existing = await readOptionalText(critiqueFile);
  if (existing.trim().length >= 300) {
    return;
  }
  const content = arrayValue(result.content);
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const headerContent = arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content);
  const footerContent = arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content);
  const formCount = content.filter((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'form').length;
  const fieldCount = countStageBBricksFormFields(content);
  const headingCount = content.filter((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'heading').length;
  const buttonCount = content.filter((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'button').length;
  const imageCount = content.filter((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'image').length;
  const sourceMap = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.sourceMapFile || ''));
  const sectionCount = arrayValue(sourceMap.sections).length || Number(result.section_count || 0) || 0;
  const documentStats = objectValue(sourceMap.document);
  const sourceHtml = await readOptionalText(firstString(sourceMap?.source?.artifactFile));
  const allElements = [...content, ...headerContent, ...footerContent];
  const sourceLinkCount = Number(documentStats.linkCount || 0);
  const bricksLinkCount = countStageBBricksLinkAffordances(allElements);
  const sourceImageCount = Number(documentStats.imageCount || 0);
  const sourceVideoCount = countStageBSourceTags(sourceHtml, 'video');
  const bricksVideoCount = countStageBElementsByName(allElements, 'video');
  const sourceControlCount = countStageBSourceTags(sourceHtml, 'input')
    + countStageBSourceTags(sourceHtml, 'select')
    + countStageBSourceTags(sourceHtml, 'textarea');
  const lines = [
    '# Stage B Handoff Critique',
    '',
    'Pixflow-owned fallback critique generated by the Stage B normalizer because the runner did not write a full critique artifact. This file records the conversion evidence used by QA; model-authored critiques should replace it when present.',
    '',
    '## Score Table',
    '',
    '| Dimension | Score | Evidence |',
    '| --- | ---: | --- |',
    `| Source structure preservation | 4 | ${content.length} page elements, ${sectionCount} mapped source sections, header elements ${headerContent.length}, footer elements ${footerContent.length}. |`,
    `| Source inventory parity | 3 | Source links ${sourceLinkCount}, Bricks link affordances ${bricksLinkCount}; source images ${sourceImageCount}, Bricks images ${imageCount}; source videos ${sourceVideoCount}, Bricks videos ${bricksVideoCount}; source controls ${sourceControlCount}, Bricks fields ${fieldCount}. Browser side-by-side still required. |`,
    `| Editable Bricks semantics | 4 | ${headingCount} headings, ${buttonCount} native buttons, ${formCount} native forms with ${fieldCount} fields, ${imageCount} image elements. |`,
    `| Styling/token preservation | 4 | ${globalClasses.length} global classes plus stage_b_color_system, stage_b_font_system, and stage_b_icon_system sidecars are present for importer preflight. |`,
    '| Interaction preservation | 3 | Source JavaScript is retained in Bricks page settings when present; frontend runtime parity must still be verified in the browser. |',
    '',
    '## Repairs Performed',
    '',
    '- Preserved the deterministic compiler baseline as the starting tree instead of rebuilding the page from scratch.',
    '- Kept source classes as Bricks global-class ids and mirrored sidecar files from bricks-result.json.',
    '- Converted source form controls to native Bricks form fields so search/newsletter inputs render on the frontend.',
    '- Kept header and footer content separate from normal page content for template assignment.',
    '- Recorded source-vs-Bricks inventory counts so model-authored repairs can target lost links, media, fields, and runtime behavior.',
    '',
    '## Remaining Browser Checks',
    '',
    '- Compare the rendered Bricks page against the accepted HTML screenshot for typography scale, field rendering, media visibility, and section rhythm.',
    '- Verify source scripts still target live Bricks form fields where Bricks generates runtime field ids.',
    '- Verify header/footer template assignment on the target WordPress page.',
  ];
  await fs.writeFile(critiqueFile, `${lines.join('\n')}\n`, 'utf8');
}

function normalizeStageBSourceRemUnitsForBricks(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: convert source-derived rem values to px before import so
  // Bricks' destination root cannot change their geometry. Standalone HTML
  // may author a non-default root (for example 62.5% = 10px), so infer the
  // same root baseline already projected into page CSS instead of assuming
  // every source document used the browser's 16px default.
  const sourceCss = [
    firstString(objectValue(result.page_settings || result.pageSettings).customCss),
    firstString(objectValue(result.stage_b_page_settings || result.stageBPageSettings).customCss),
  ].filter(Boolean).join('\n');
  const sourceRootRemPx = inferStageBRootRemPxFromCss(sourceCss);
  const convertRem = (value, remPx) => String(value).replace(/(-?\d*\.?\d+)rem\b/gi, (match, numberText) => {
    const number = Number(numberText);
    if (!Number.isFinite(number)) return match;
    return `${Math.round(number * remPx * 1000) / 1000}px`;
  });
  const convertValue = (value) => convertRem(
    // CSS Values defines rem units in media-query conditions against the
    // initial browser value (16px), independently of html's authored size.
    // Resolve those preludes first, then resolve declaration values against
    // the source document root.
    String(value).replace(/@media\s*([^{}]+)\{/gi, (match, condition) => (
      `@media ${convertRem(condition, 16)} {`
    )),
    sourceRootRemPx,
  );
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      return /-?\d*\.?\d+rem\b/i.test(value) ? convertValue(value) : value;
    }
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      return value.map((item) => visit(item));
    }
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') {
      return value;
    }
    for (const [childKey, childValue] of Object.entries(value)) {
      if (['stage_b_route_contract', 'stage_b_theme_style_contract', 'stage_b_theme_style_health'].includes(childKey)) {
        continue;
      }
      value[childKey] = visit(childValue);
    }
    return value;
  };

  for (const element of [
    ...arrayValue(result.content),
    ...arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    ...arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ]) {
    if (element?.settings) {
      element.settings = visit(element.settings);
    }
  }
  for (const classItem of arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses)) {
    if (classItem?.settings) {
      classItem.settings = visit(classItem.settings);
    }
  }
  for (const settings of [
    objectValue(result.page_settings || result.pageSettings),
    objectValue(result.stage_b_page_settings || result.stageBPageSettings),
  ]) {
    if (typeof settings.customCss === 'string') {
      settings.customCss = convertValue(settings.customCss);
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBPageColorVariables(result, colorSystem) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks global variables are stored for editing, but source
  // Stage A CSS often references raw CSS variables such as var(--bg) or
  // hsl(var(--text)). Emit page-scoped definitions so the rendered Bricks page
  // has the same CSS variable runtime as the accepted HTML artifact.
  const variables = arrayValue(colorSystem.variables)
    .map((variable) => {
      const cssVariable = firstString(variable?.cssVariable);
      const name = cssVariable || (firstString(variable?.name) ? `--${firstString(variable.name).replace(/^--/, '')}` : '');
      const value = firstString(variable?.value);
      if (!/^--[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(name) || !value) return null;
      const sourceCssVariable = firstString(variable?.sourceCssVariable);
      const sourceName = firstString(variable?.sourceName);
      const legacyName = firstString(variable?.name);
      return { name, value, sourceCssVariable, sourceName, legacyName };
    })
    .filter(Boolean);
  if (variables.length === 0) return;

  const findVariable = (names) => {
    const wanted = new Set(names.map((name) => name.toLowerCase()));
    return variables.find((variable) => {
      const candidates = [
        variable.name,
        variable.sourceCssVariable,
        variable.sourceName ? `--${variable.sourceName.replace(/^--/, '')}` : '',
        variable.legacyName ? `--${variable.legacyName.replace(/^--/, '')}` : '',
      ].filter(Boolean).map((name) => name.toLowerCase());
      return candidates.some((candidate) => wanted.has(candidate));
    })?.name || '';
  };
  const backgroundVariable = findVariable(['--bg', '--background', '--surface']);
  const foregroundVariable = findVariable(['--text', '--fg', '--ink', '--color', '--foreground']);
  const variableCssValue = (name) => {
    const value = variables.find((variable) => variable.name === name)?.value || '';
    const variableRef = `var(${name})`;
    return isStageBHslChannelValue(value) ? `hsl(${variableRef})` : variableRef;
  };

  const block = [
    ':root, #brx-content {',
    ...variables.map((variable) => `  ${variable.name}: ${variable.value};`),
    '}',
    ...(backgroundVariable ? [
      'body, #brx-content {',
      `  background: ${variableCssValue(backgroundVariable)};`,
      ...(foregroundVariable ? [`  color: ${variableCssValue(foregroundVariable)};`] : []),
      '}',
    ] : []),
  ].join('\n');

  for (const key of ['page_settings', 'stage_b_page_settings']) {
    const settings = objectValue(result[key]);
    const existing = firstString(settings.customCss);
    if (existing.includes(variables[0].name) && /:root\s*,\s*#brx-content/i.test(existing)) {
      continue;
    }
    settings.customCss = `${block}\n${existing}`.trim();
    result[key] = settings;
  }
}

function normalizeStageBPageForegroundInheritance(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: section foreground colors are a valid Bricks control
  // baseline. Do not let page-level fallback CSS reset every section back to
  // the page foreground, or dark/light contrast sections lose their local text
  // colour after the Stage B cleanup pass.
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;
  const removeBroadSectionColorReset = (css) => String(css || '')
    .replace(/#brx-content\s*,\s*#brx-content\s+\.brxe-section\s*\{\s*color\s*:\s*inherit\s*;?\s*\}\s*/gi, '')
    .replace(/#brx-content\s+\.brxe-section\s*\{\s*color\s*:\s*inherit\s*;?\s*\}\s*/gi, '')
    .replace(/#brx-content\s+:where\(\.brxe-heading,\s*h1,\s*h2,\s*h3,\s*h4,\s*h5,\s*h6\)\s*\{\s*color\s*:\s*inherit\s*;?\s*\}\s*/gi, '')
    .trim();

  for (const key of ['page_settings', 'pageSettings', 'stage_b_page_settings', 'stageBPageSettings']) {
    const settings = objectValue(result[key]);
    if (typeof settings.customCss === 'string') {
      settings.customCss = removeBroadSectionColorReset(settings.customCss);
      result[key] = settings;
    }
  }
}

const PIXFLOW_STAGE_B_FOREGROUND_LEAF_NAMES = new Set([
  'accordion',
  'accordion-nested',
  'button',
  'counter',
  'form',
  'heading',
  'icon',
  'logo',
  'nav-menu',
  'post-content',
  'post-excerpt',
  'post-reading-time',
  'post-sharing',
  'post-taxonomy',
  'post-title',
  'product-add-to-cart',
  'product-price',
  'product-rating',
  'product-stock',
  'rating',
  'social-icons',
  'tabs',
  'tabs-nested',
  'text',
  'text-basic',
  'text-link',
  'toggle',
]);

function stageBExplicitForegroundColor(value) {
  const raw = typeof value === 'string'
    ? value.trim()
    : firstString(objectValue(value).raw, objectValue(value).hex, objectValue(value).id).trim();
  if (!raw) return null;
  if (/^(?:inherit|initial|unset|transparent)$/i.test(raw)) return null;
  return structuredClone(value);
}

/**
 * Materialize inherited section/container foregrounds on Bricks text-bearing
 * leaves. Bricks theme styles target leaf elements directly, so browser CSS
 * inheritance alone is not strong enough to preserve a dark/light contrast
 * section after conversion. Generated classes are keyed by the responsive
 * typography patch, making this pass shared, deterministic, and idempotent.
 */
function normalizeStageBInheritedForegroundColors(result) {
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;

  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const elements = collectStageBAllElements(result);
  const elementById = new Map(elements
    .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const typographyKeys = new Set(['_typography']);

  const collectTypographyKeys = (settings) => {
    for (const key of Object.keys(objectValue(settings))) {
      if (key === '_typography' || key.startsWith('_typography:')) typographyKeys.add(key);
    }
  };
  for (const classItem of globalClasses) collectTypographyKeys(classItem?.settings);
  for (const element of elements) collectTypographyKeys(element?.settings);

  const isCompilerFallbackClass = (classItem) => /^(?:stage-a-(?:body-type|[a-z0-9-]+-defaults)|pixflow-template-[a-z0-9-]+-reset)(?:-|$)/i
    .test(firstString(classItem?.name));
  const ownColor = (element, typographyKey, options = {}) => {
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    let color = null;
    for (const classId of arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses)) {
      const classItem = classById.get(firstString(classId));
      if (options.ignoreCompilerFallbacks && isCompilerFallbackClass(classItem)) continue;
      const classSettings = objectValue(classItem?.settings);
      const candidate = stageBExplicitForegroundColor(objectValue(classSettings[typographyKey]).color);
      if (candidate !== null) color = candidate;
    }
    const direct = stageBExplicitForegroundColor(objectValue(settings[typographyKey]).color);
    return direct !== null ? direct : color;
  };

  const inheritedColor = (element, typographyKey) => {
    const visited = new Set();
    let parentId = firstString(element?.parent);
    while (parentId && !visited.has(parentId)) {
      visited.add(parentId);
      const parent = elementById.get(parentId);
      if (!parent) return null;
      const color = ownColor(parent, typographyKey, { ignoreCompilerFallbacks: true });
      if (color !== null) return color;
      parentId = firstString(parent.parent);
    }
    return null;
  };

  const classByPatch = new Map();
  for (const classItem of globalClasses) {
    if (!/^(?:stage-a|pixflow)-inherited-foreground-/.test(firstString(classItem?.name))) continue;
    classByPatch.set(JSON.stringify(objectValue(classItem.settings)), classItem);
  }

  for (const element of elements) {
    if (!PIXFLOW_STAGE_B_FOREGROUND_LEAF_NAMES.has(firstString(element?.name).toLowerCase())) continue;
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const patch = {};
    for (const typographyKey of typographyKeys) {
      if (ownColor(element, typographyKey, { ignoreCompilerFallbacks: true }) !== null) continue;
      const color = inheritedColor(element, typographyKey);
      if (color !== null) patch[typographyKey] = { color };
    }
    if (Object.keys(patch).length === 0) continue;

    const signature = JSON.stringify(patch);
    let classItem = classByPatch.get(signature);
    if (!classItem) {
      const id = deterministicBricksId(`stage-b-inherited-foreground:${signature}`);
      classItem = ensureStageBGlobalClass(globalClasses, {
        id,
        name: `pixflow-inherited-foreground-${id}`,
        settings: patch,
      });
      classById.set(id, classItem);
      classByPatch.set(signature, classItem);
    }
    settings._cssGlobalClasses = uniqueStrings([
      ...arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses),
      classItem.id,
    ]);
    element.settings = settings;
  }

  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function normalizeStageBInheritedIconStyles(result) {
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const elements = collectStageBAllElements(result);
  const elementById = new Map(elements
    .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
    .filter(([id]) => id));

  for (const element of elements) {
    if (firstString(element?.name).toLowerCase() !== 'icon') continue;
    const icon = objectValue(objectValue(element?.settings).icon);
    if (!/pixflow:tabler-outline:/i.test(firstString(icon.icon))) continue;
    const parent = elementById.get(firstString(element?.parent));
    if (!parent) continue;
    const parentSettings = objectValue(parent.settings);
    const cssChunks = [firstString(parentSettings._cssCustom)];
    for (const classId of arrayValue(parentSettings._cssGlobalClasses)) {
      cssChunks.push(firstString(objectValue(classById.get(firstString(classId))?.settings)._cssCustom));
    }
    let stroke = '';
    for (const css of cssChunks) {
      const blocks = String(css || '').matchAll(/[^{}]*\bsvg\b[^{}]*\{([^{}]*)\}/gi);
      for (const block of blocks) {
        const declarations = parseStageBCssDeclarations(block[1] || '');
        stroke = firstString(declarations.stroke, declarations.color, declarations.fill, stroke);
      }
    }
    if (!stroke || /^(?:none|inherit|initial|unset|transparent)$/i.test(stroke)) continue;
    const patch = { icon: { stroke: { raw: stroke } } };
    const signature = JSON.stringify(patch);
    const id = deterministicBricksId(`stage-b-inherited-icon-style:${signature}`);
    const classItem = ensureStageBGlobalClass(globalClasses, {
      id,
      name: `pixflow-inherited-icon-style-${id}`,
      settings: patch,
    });
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    settings._cssGlobalClasses = uniqueStrings([...arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses), classItem.id]);
    element.settings = settings;
  }
  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function normalizeStageBInlineTextWrappers(result) {
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(headerSpec.content || result.header_content || result.headerContent),
    arrayValue(footerSpec.content || result.footer_content || result.footerContent),
  ];

  for (const elements of buckets) {
    const elementById = new Map(elements
      .map((element) => [firstString(element?.id), element])
      .filter(([id]) => id));
    const removeIds = new Set();
    for (const wrapper of elements) {
      const childIds = arrayValue(wrapper?.children).map(firstString).filter(Boolean);
      if (childIds.length !== 2) continue;
      const wrapperSettings = objectValue(wrapper?.settings);
      const css = [firstString(wrapperSettings._cssCustom), ...arrayValue(wrapperSettings._cssGlobalClasses)
        .map((classId) => firstString(objectValue(classById.get(firstString(classId))?.settings)._cssCustom))]
        .join('\n');
      const inlineTag = /\bsup\b/i.test(css) ? 'sup' : /\bsub\b/i.test(css) ? 'sub' : '';
      if (!inlineTag) continue;
      const firstLeaf = elementById.get(childIds[0]);
      const branch = elementById.get(childIds[1]);
      const branchChildren = arrayValue(branch?.children).map(firstString).filter(Boolean);
      const inlineLeaf = branchChildren.length === 1 ? elementById.get(branchChildren[0]) : null;
      if (
        firstString(firstLeaf?.name) !== 'text-basic'
        || firstString(inlineLeaf?.name) !== 'text-basic'
        || arrayValue(firstLeaf?.children).length > 0
        || arrayValue(inlineLeaf?.children).length > 0
      ) continue;
      const firstText = firstString(objectValue(firstLeaf.settings).text);
      const inlineText = firstString(objectValue(inlineLeaf.settings).text);
      if (!firstText || !inlineText) continue;
      firstLeaf.settings = objectValue(firstLeaf.settings);
      firstLeaf.settings.text = `${firstText}<${inlineTag}>${inlineText}</${inlineTag}>`;
      wrapper.children = [firstString(firstLeaf.id)];
      removeIds.add(firstString(branch.id));
      removeIds.add(firstString(inlineLeaf.id));
    }
    if (removeIds.size > 0) {
      for (let index = elements.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {
        if (removeIds.has(firstString(elements[index]?.id))) elements.splice(index, 1);
      }
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBNativeButtonVariants(result) {
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result?.global_classes || result?.globalClasses);
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses
    .map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem])
    .filter(([id]) => id));
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];

  for (const elements of buckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
      if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'button') continue;
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      const classes = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses)
        .map((classId) => classById.get(firstString(classId)))
        .filter(Boolean);
      const classesOwnVisualStyle = classes.some((classItem) => {
        const classSettings = objectValue(classItem?.settings);
        const typography = objectValue(classSettings._typography);
        return Boolean(
          classSettings._background
          || classSettings._border
          || classSettings._boxShadow
          || typography.color
        );
      });
      if (!classesOwnVisualStyle) continue;

      // A Bricks button preset is a Theme Style selector, not a semantic
      // translation of class names such as "secondary", "alt", or "ghost".
      // Applying the dark preset here overrides source-accurate class controls
      // (for example a transparent outlined CTA becomes a black button).
      // When the converted classes already own the visual treatment, keep the
      // element unstyled and let those native class controls render it.
      delete settings.style;
      element.settings = settings;
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBInvalidNativeForms(result, stageAHtml) {
  // Pixflow-owned: native Bricks forms are only valid when Stage A contains
  // real form controls. The model can hallucinate form elements for visual
  // interface mockups; those alter parity and can make Bricks frontend render
  // fail. Remove native forms when the accepted source has no form controls.
  if (!result || typeof result !== 'object') return;
  const sourceHasRealControls = /<(?:form|input|select|textarea)\b/i.test(firstString(stageAHtml));
  if (sourceHasRealControls) return;

  const cleanElements = (elements) => {
    const removedIds = new Set();
    const cleaned = [];
    for (const element of arrayValue(elements)) {
      if (firstString(element?.name) === 'form') {
        if (firstString(element?.id)) removedIds.add(firstString(element.id));
        continue;
      }
      cleaned.push(element);
    }
    if (removedIds.size === 0) return elements;
    return cleaned
      .filter((element) => !removedIds.has(firstString(element?.parent)))
      .map((element) => {
        if (!Array.isArray(element?.children)) return element;
        element.children = element.children.filter((childId) => !removedIds.has(firstString(childId)));
        return element;
      });
  };

  result.content = cleanElements(result.content);
  if (Array.isArray(result.header_content)) {
    result.header_content = cleanElements(result.header_content);
  }
  if (Array.isArray(result.footer_content)) {
    result.footer_content = cleanElements(result.footer_content);
  }
  for (const key of ['stage_b_header', 'stageBHeader', 'stage_b_footer', 'stageBFooter']) {
    const spec = objectValue(result[key]);
    if (Array.isArray(spec.content)) {
      spec.content = cleanElements(spec.content);
      result[key] = spec;
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBSourceIdSelectorClasses(result, styleMap) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Stage A frequently uses section id selectors for major
  // bands (#platform, #pricing, etc.). Bricks can keep the id attribute for
  // anchors, but editable styling must live on global classes.
  const rules = arrayValue(styleMap.rules);
  const idRules = new Map();
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const selector = firstString(rule?.selector).trim();
    const match = selector.match(/^#([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)$/);
    if (!match) continue;
    const mapped = mapPixflowCssDeclarationsToBricksSettings(rule.declarations, { deriveResponsive: false });
    if (Object.keys(mapped).length > 0) {
      idRules.set(match[1], mapped);
    }
  }
  if (idRules.size === 0) return;

  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];

  for (const elements of buckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
      const sourceId = findStageBAttributeValue(element, 'id');
      if (!sourceId || !idRules.has(sourceId)) continue;
      const classItem = ensureStageBGlobalClass(globalClasses, {
        id: deterministicBricksId(`stage-b-source-id-class:${sourceId}`),
        name: `pixflow-source-id-${slugify(sourceId)}`,
        settings: idRules.get(sourceId),
      });
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      settings._cssGlobalClasses = uniqueStrings([...arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses), classItem.id]);
      element.settings = settings;
    }
  }
  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function normalizeStageBSectionTagDefaults(result, styleMap) {
  // Pixflow-owned: every resulting Bricks section needs the plain-HTML reset,
  // including semantic roots promoted from a source div/main. Source-tag-only
  // attachment misses those promoted elements and leaves Bricks Theme Style
  // block padding active across the entire page.
  const sectionRule = arrayValue(styleMap.rules).find((rule) => firstString(rule?.selector).trim().toLowerCase() === 'section');
  const sectionDefaults = mapPixflowCssDeclarationsToBricksSettings(objectValue(sectionRule?.declarations), { deriveResponsive: false });
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  let sectionReset = globalClasses.find((classItem) => (
    firstString(classItem?.id) === deterministicBricksId('stage-b-html-synthetic-class:tag:section')
    || /^(?:stage-a-section-display|pixflow-source-section-reset)(?:-\d+)?$/i.test(firstString(classItem?.name))
  ));
  if (!sectionReset) {
    sectionReset = {
      id: deterministicBricksId('stage-b-html-synthetic-class:tag:section'),
      name: 'pixflow-source-section-reset',
      settings: {
        _display: 'block',
        _padding: { top: '0', right: '0', bottom: '0', left: '0' },
      },
    };
    globalClasses.unshift(sectionReset);
  }
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses.map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem]).filter(([id]) => id));
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];

  for (const elements of buckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
      if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'section') continue;
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      settings._cssGlobalClasses = uniqueStrings([
        firstString(sectionReset.id),
        ...arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses),
      ]);
      element.settings = settings;
      if (Object.keys(sectionDefaults).length === 0) continue;
      const classItems = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses)
        .map((classId) => classById.get(firstString(classId)))
        .filter(Boolean);
      const targetClass = classItems.find((classItem) => firstString(classItem.name) !== 'stage-a-body-type') || classItems[0];
      if (!targetClass) continue;
      targetClass.settings = mergePixflowStageBMissingSettings(objectValue(targetClass.settings), sectionDefaults);
    }
  }
  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function findStageBAttributeValue(element, name) {
  const wanted = firstString(name).toLowerCase();
  for (const attribute of arrayValue(objectValue(element?.settings)._attributes)) {
    if (firstString(attribute?.name).toLowerCase() === wanted) {
      return firstString(attribute?.value);
    }
  }
  return '';
}

function mergePixflowStageBMissingSettings(target, defaults) {
  const result = { ...objectValue(target) };
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(objectValue(defaults))) {
    if (value === undefined || value === null || value === '') continue;
    if (key === '_padding' || key === '_margin') {
      result[key] = mergePixflowStageBBoxMissing(objectValue(result[key]), objectValue(value));
      continue;
    }
    if (key === '_typography') {
      result[key] = { ...objectValue(value), ...objectValue(result[key]) };
      continue;
    }
    if (result[key] === undefined || result[key] === null || result[key] === '') {
      result[key] = value;
    }
  }
  return result;
}

function mergePixflowStageBBoxMissing(target, defaults) {
  return {
    top: firstString(target.top, defaults.top),
    right: firstString(target.right, defaults.right),
    bottom: firstString(target.bottom, defaults.bottom),
    left: firstString(target.left, defaults.left),
  };
}

function normalizeStageBSectionDisplayDefaults(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: native Bricks sections default to flex, while plain HTML
  // sections default to block. Preserve the accepted Stage A section flow unless
  // the model already mapped the source section to grid/flex/native display.
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  if (globalClasses.length === 0) return;
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses.map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem]).filter(([id]) => id));

  const sectionBuckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];

  for (const elements of sectionBuckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
      if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'section') continue;
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      if (firstString(settings._display)) continue;
      const classIds = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses).map(firstString).filter(Boolean);
      const classItems = classIds.map((id) => classById.get(id)).filter(Boolean);
      const specificClass = classItems.find((classItem) => firstString(classItem.name) !== 'stage-a-body-type');
      if (classItems.some((classItem) => firstString(objectValue(classItem.settings)._display))) continue;
      if (specificClass) {
        specificClass.settings = objectValue(specificClass.settings);
        specificClass.settings._display = 'block';
      }
    }
  }

  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

export function normalizeStageBSourceRemUnitsForBricksForTest(result = {}) {
  normalizeStageBSourceRemUnitsForBricks(result);
  return result;
}

function normalizeStageBGlobalClassLayoutOwners(result) {
  // Stage B/model output can merge source state into a global class after the
  // baseline mapper has run. Reconcile the final class shape before QA so a
  // class carrying grid/flex controls cannot retain Bricks' incompatible
  // block default and trigger a repair-required P0.
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const normalizeGridResponsive = (settings) => {
    const display = firstString(settings._display).toLowerCase();
    if (
      display === 'grid'
      && stageBGridColumnCountHint(firstString(settings._gridTemplateColumns)) > 1
      && !firstString(settings['_gridTemplateColumns:mobile_portrait'], settings['_gridTemplateColumns:tablet_portrait'])
    ) {
      // A direct Stage B class/style promotion may bypass the baseline mapper
      // that normally derives Bricks responsive controls. Preserve the source
      // multi-column layout at desktop, but collapse it through a native
      // Bricks breakpoint so the payload remains valid on narrow screens.
      settings['_gridTemplateColumns:mobile_portrait'] = '1fr';
    }
    return settings;
  };
  for (const classItem of globalClasses) {
    const settings = normalizeGridResponsive(objectValue(classItem?.settings));
    const display = firstString(settings._display).toLowerCase();
    const hasGridControl = [
      '_gridTemplateColumns',
      '_gridTemplateRows',
      '_justifyItemsGrid',
      '_alignItemsGrid',
      '_justifyContentGrid',
      '_alignContentGrid',
    ].some((key) => Boolean(settings[key]) && firstString(settings[key]) !== '');
    const hasFlexControl = ['_direction', '_flexDirection', '_flexWrap']
      .some((key) => Boolean(settings[key]) && firstString(settings[key]) !== '');
    if (display === 'none') {
      // A source class can be intentionally hidden at desktop and enabled as
      // grid/flex only at a narrower breakpoint. Its responsive container
      // controls are dormant while hidden; promoting `none` to a base layout
      // value makes both desktop/mobile navigation variants visible together.
      classItem.settings = settings;
      continue;
    }
    if (hasGridControl && hasFlexControl) {
      // A model repair can merge a grid-only declaration into a source class
      // that already owns flex layout. Keep the explicit source display and
      // drop the incompatible control family; Bricks cannot apply both layout
      // owners to one class and QA would otherwise report contradictory P0s.
      if (['flex', 'inline-flex'].includes(display)) {
        for (const key of [
          '_gridTemplateColumns',
          '_gridTemplateRows',
          '_justifyItemsGrid',
          '_alignItemsGrid',
          '_justifyContentGrid',
          '_alignContentGrid',
        ]) {
          delete settings[key];
        }
      } else if (['grid', 'inline-grid'].includes(display)) {
        for (const key of ['_direction', '_flexDirection', '_flexWrap']) {
          delete settings[key];
        }
      } else {
        settings._display = 'grid';
        for (const key of ['_direction', '_flexDirection', '_flexWrap']) {
          delete settings[key];
        }
      }
    } else if (hasGridControl && !['grid', 'inline-grid'].includes(display)) {
      settings._display = 'grid';
    } else if (hasFlexControl && !['flex', 'inline-flex'].includes(display)) {
      settings._display = 'flex';
    }
    classItem.settings = settings;
  }
  for (const element of collectStageBAllElements(result)) {
    if (element && typeof element === 'object') {
      element.settings = normalizeGridResponsive(objectValue(element.settings));
    }
  }
  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function normalizeStageBIconPlaceholderContracts(result, iconSystem) {
  const system = objectValue(iconSystem);
  if (Object.keys(system).length === 0) {
    return { added: 0, placeholders: [] };
  }
  const placeholders = new Set();
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      const match = value.trim().match(/^pixflow:([a-z0-9-]+):([a-z0-9-]+)$/i);
      if (match) placeholders.add(`${match[1]}:${match[2]}`.toLowerCase());
      return;
    }
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      value.forEach(visit);
      return;
    }
    for (const child of Object.values(value)) visit(child);
  };
  // Inspect only the payload. Looking at the sidecar itself would make every
  // declared icon look like a used placeholder and would defeat the
  // proportional icon-install filter in WordPress.
  visit({
    content: result.content,
    header_content: result.header_content,
    footer_content: result.footer_content,
    stage_b_header: result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader,
    stage_b_footer: result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter,
    global_classes: result.global_classes || result.globalClasses,
    page_settings: result.page_settings || result.pageSettings,
  });
  let added = 0;
  for (const placeholder of placeholders) {
    const [setId, iconId] = placeholder.split(':');
    if (!stageBIconSystemContainsPlaceholder(system, `pixflow:${setId}:${iconId}`)) {
      ensurePixflowStageBIconSystemIcon(system, {
        setId,
        id: iconId,
        roles: ['payload_placeholder'],
        reason: 'Declared because the final Bricks payload references this Pixflow icon placeholder.',
      });
      added += 1;
    }
  }
  return { added, placeholders: [...placeholders].sort() };
}

function normalizeStageBHeadingInheritance(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks Theme Styles set default heading color/font. Source
  // HTML often relies on inherited section/body typography, so only add
  // inherited heading controls when neither the element nor attached classes
  // specify the property.
  const globalClasses = arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses);
  const classById = new Map(globalClasses.map((classItem) => [firstString(classItem?.id), classItem]).filter(([id]) => id));
  const inheritColorClass = ensureStageBGlobalClass(globalClasses, {
    id: deterministicBricksId('stage-b-heading-inherit:color'),
    name: 'pixflow-source-heading-inherit-color',
    settings: { _typography: { color: { raw: 'inherit' } } },
  });
  classById.set(inheritColorClass.id, inheritColorClass);
  const inheritFontClassId = deterministicBricksId('stage-b-heading-inherit:font');
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];

  for (const elements of buckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
      if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'heading') continue;
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      const elementTypography = objectValue(settings._typography);
      const classIds = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses).map(firstString).filter(Boolean);
      const attachedTypography = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses)
        .map((classId) => objectValue(classById.get(firstString(classId))?.settings)._typography)
        .map(objectValue);
      if (!hasStageBTypographyColor([elementTypography, ...attachedTypography])) {
        classIds.push(inheritColorClass.id);
      }
      if (elementTypography.color && objectValue(elementTypography.color).raw === 'inherit') {
        delete elementTypography.color;
        classIds.push(inheritColorClass.id);
      }
      if (firstString(elementTypography['font-family']) === 'inherit' || firstString(elementTypography.fontFamily) === 'inherit') {
        delete elementTypography['font-family'];
        delete elementTypography.fontFamily;
      }
      settings._cssGlobalClasses = uniqueStrings(classIds.filter((classId) => classId !== inheritFontClassId));
      if (Object.keys(elementTypography).length > 0) {
        settings._typography = elementTypography;
      } else {
        delete settings._typography;
      }
      element.settings = settings;
    }
  }

  result.global_classes = globalClasses;
}

function hasStageBTypographyColor(typographies) {
  return typographies.some((typography) => {
    const color = objectValue(typography).color;
    return typeof color === 'string'
      ? Boolean(color)
      : Boolean(firstString(objectValue(color).raw, objectValue(color).hex, objectValue(color).id));
  });
}

function hasStageBTypographyFontFamily(typographies) {
  return typographies.some((typography) => Boolean(firstString(objectValue(typography)['font-family'], objectValue(typography).fontFamily)));
}

function normalizeStageBChildReferences(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: keep Bricks parent/child references coherent after model or
  // normalizer repairs remove invalid generated elements.
  const buckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];
  for (const elements of buckets) {
    const ids = new Set(elements.map((element) => firstString(element?.id)).filter(Boolean));
    for (const element of elements) {
      if (!element || typeof element !== 'object' || Array.isArray(element)) {
        continue;
      }
      if (Array.isArray(element?.children)) {
        element.children = element.children.filter((childId) => ids.has(firstString(childId)));
      }
      const parent = element.parent === 0 || element.parent === '0' ? '' : firstString(element.parent);
      if (!parent && firstString(element.name) === 'section') {
        element.parent = '';
        continue;
      }
      if (parent && !ids.has(parent)) {
        element.parent = '';
      }
    }
  }
}

function ensureStageBGlobalClass(globalClasses, classItem) {
  const existing = globalClasses.find((item) => firstString(item?.id) === classItem.id || firstString(item?.name) === classItem.name);
  if (existing) {
    existing.settings = { ...objectValue(classItem.settings), ...objectValue(existing.settings) };
    return existing;
  }
  globalClasses.push(classItem);
  return classItem;
}

function normalizeStageBRootOnlyCustomCss(result, colorSystem = {}) {
  // Pixflow-owned: keep custom CSS for selectors Bricks cannot express, but
  // remove routine %root% declarations after they have been mapped to native
  // Bricks class settings. This prevents model output from carrying duplicate
  // layout/type styles in _cssCustom while preserving pseudo/media rules.
  const managedCssVariables = new Set([
    ...Object.keys(objectValue(colorSystem.tokenAliases)),
    ...Object.values(objectValue(colorSystem.tokenAliases)).map((value) => firstString(value)),
    ...arrayValue(colorSystem.variables).flatMap((variable) => [
      firstString(variable?.sourceCssVariable),
      firstString(variable?.cssVariable),
    ]),
  ].filter((value) => /^--[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(value)));
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      for (const item of value) visit(item);
      return;
    }
    if (typeof value._cssCustom === 'string' && value._cssCustom.trim()) {
      value._cssCustom = stripStageBRootOnlyRoutineCustomCss(value._cssCustom, value, {
        managedCssVariables,
      });
      if (!value._cssCustom.trim()) {
        delete value._cssCustom;
      }
    }
    for (const item of Object.values(value)) {
      visit(item);
    }
  };
  visit(result);
}

export function normalizeStageBRootOnlyCustomCssForTest(result, colorSystem = {}) {
  normalizeStageBRootOnlyCustomCss(result, colorSystem);
  return result;
}

function stripStageBRootOnlyRoutineCustomCss(customCss, settings = null, context = {}) {
  const text = String(customCss || '').trim();
  if (!text || !settings || typeof settings !== 'object') return text;
  return rewriteStageBRootScopedCustomCss(text, settings, context).trim();
}

function rewriteStageBRootScopedCustomCss(customCss, settings, context = {}) {
  // Pixflow-owned: model repair passes may append native declarations beside
  // pseudo rules, inside media queries, or on a Bricks-supported state. Walk
  // balanced CSS blocks so every directly addressable %root% rule is lifted,
  // while irreducible selectors and conditional effects remain byte-stable.
  const source = String(customCss || '');
  const blocks = [];
  let cursor = 0;
  while (cursor < source.length) {
    while (cursor < source.length && /\s/.test(source[cursor])) cursor += 1;
    if (cursor >= source.length) break;
    const openIndex = source.indexOf('{', cursor);
    if (openIndex < 0) {
      const remainder = source.slice(cursor).trim();
      if (remainder) blocks.push(remainder);
      break;
    }
    const closeIndex = findPixflowCssBlockClose(source, openIndex);
    if (closeIndex < 0) {
      blocks.push(source.slice(cursor).trim());
      break;
    }
    const header = source.slice(cursor, openIndex).trim();
    const body = source.slice(openIndex + 1, closeIndex);
    const originalBlock = source.slice(cursor, closeIndex + 1).trim();
    cursor = closeIndex + 1;

    const mediaMatch = header.match(/^@media\s+(.+)$/i);
    if (mediaMatch) {
      const suffixes = pixflowStageBResponsiveSuffixesForMediaCondition(mediaMatch[1]);
      if (suffixes.length === 0) {
        blocks.push(originalBlock);
        continue;
      }
      const rewrittenBody = rewriteStageBRootScopedCustomCss(body, settings, {
        ...context,
        responsiveSuffixes: suffixes,
      }).trim();
      if (rewrittenBody) {
        blocks.push(`${header} { ${rewrittenBody} }`);
      }
      continue;
    }

    if (header.startsWith('@')) {
      blocks.push(originalBlock);
      continue;
    }

    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(header).map((selector) => selector.trim()).filter(Boolean);
    const baseRootRule = selectors.length > 0 && selectors.every((selector) => /^%root%$/i.test(selector));
    const stateMatches = selectors.map((selector) => selector.match(
      /^%root%:(hover|focus|focus-visible|focus-within|active|visited|disabled|checked)$/i,
    ));
    const stateRootRule = selectors.length > 0
      && stateMatches.every(Boolean)
      && stateMatches.every((match) => firstString(match?.[1]).toLowerCase() === firstString(stateMatches[0]?.[1]).toLowerCase());
    if (!baseRootRule && !stateRootRule) {
      blocks.push(originalBlock);
      continue;
    }

    const responsiveSuffixes = uniqueStrings(context.responsiveSuffixes);
    if (stateRootRule && responsiveSuffixes.length > 0) {
      // Bricks state+breakpoint key ordering is version-sensitive. Preserve the
      // conditional state rather than silently materializing the wrong control.
      blocks.push(originalBlock);
      continue;
    }

    const parsedDeclarations = parseStageBCssDeclarations(body);
    const isolatedGapProperty = !firstString(parsedDeclarations.gap)
      && Boolean(firstString(parsedDeclarations['column-gap'])) !== Boolean(firstString(parsedDeclarations['row-gap']))
      ? (firstString(parsedDeclarations['column-gap']) ? 'column-gap' : 'row-gap')
      : '';
    const customDeclarations = {};
    for (const [property, value] of Object.entries(parsedDeclarations)) {
      if (
        property.startsWith('--')
        && context.managedCssVariables instanceof Set
        && context.managedCssVariables.has(property)
      ) {
        // The colour-system sidecar owns both generated and live-route
        // variables. Re-declaring them on a page class creates a token bucket,
        // shadows the site authority, and makes otherwise-native styling fail
        // the final Stage B gate.
        continue;
      }
      if (/!important\s*$/i.test(value)) {
        customDeclarations[property] = value;
        continue;
      }
      if (property === isolatedGapProperty) {
        // Bricks 2.4 drops a class that owns only one native gap axis. This is
        // an intentional compatibility fallback, not routine CSS waiting to
        // be lifted. Keep the exact authored axis scoped to the same class so
        // independent gap-x/gap-y utilities remain composable.
        customDeclarations[property] = value;
        continue;
      }
      const mapped = mapPixflowCssDeclarationsToBricksSettings(
        { [property]: value },
        { deriveResponsive: false },
      );
      const nativeSettings = stateRootRule
        ? pickPixflowStageBStateDeclarations(mapped)
        : responsiveSuffixes.length > 0
          ? pickPixflowStageBResponsiveDeclarations(mapped)
          : mapped;
      if (Object.keys(nativeSettings).length === 0) {
        customDeclarations[property] = value;
        continue;
      }
      if (stateRootRule) {
        const state = firstString(stateMatches[0]?.[1]).toLowerCase();
        mergePixflowStageBSettings(settings, Object.fromEntries(
          Object.entries(nativeSettings).map(([key, nativeValue]) => [`${key}:${state}`, nativeValue]),
        ));
        continue;
      }
      if (responsiveSuffixes.length > 0) {
        for (const suffix of responsiveSuffixes) {
          for (const [key, nativeValue] of Object.entries(nativeSettings)) {
            applyPixflowStageBResponsiveBaseDefault(settings, key);
            mergePixflowStageBSettings(settings, { [`${key}:${suffix}`]: nativeValue });
          }
        }
        continue;
      }
      mergePixflowStageBSettings(settings, nativeSettings);
    }

    const customEntries = Object.entries(customDeclarations);
    if (customEntries.length > 0) {
      blocks.push(`${header} { ${customEntries.map(([property, value]) => `${property}: ${value};`).join(' ')} }`);
    }
  }
  return blocks.join('\n');
}

async function materializeStageBInlineDataUriAssets(workspaceDir, result, stageAHtml = '') {
  // Pixflow-owned: generated Stage A drafts can define inline data URI images
  // and the baseline converter can assign deterministic local filenames for
  // those images. Write the files before QA/import so Bricks receives real
  // media assets instead of unresolved filename references.
  if (!workspaceDir || !result || typeof result !== 'object') return;
  const writes = new Map();
  const runtimeImageMap = collectStageBRuntimeDataImageMap(stageAHtml);
  const stageBuckets = [
    arrayValue(result.content),
    arrayValue(result.header_content),
    arrayValue(result.footer_content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader).content),
    arrayValue(objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter).content),
  ];
  let inlineImageIndex = 0;
  for (const elements of stageBuckets) {
    for (const element of elements) {
    if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'image') continue;
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    const dataImageKey = findStageBAttributeValue(element, 'data-img');
    const directDataUri = firstString(objectValue(settings.image).url);
    const dataUri = /^data:image\//i.test(directDataUri)
      ? directDataUri
      : (dataImageKey ? runtimeImageMap.get(dataImageKey) : '');
    if (!dataUri) continue;
    const extension = stageBDataUriExtension(dataUri);
    if (!extension) continue;
    const key = dataImageKey || firstString(element.id) || `inline-${inlineImageIndex}`;
    const ref = `assets/${slugify(key) || `stage-b-inline-${inlineImageIndex}`}.${extension}`;
    inlineImageIndex += 1;
    writes.set(ref, dataUri);
    settings.image = {
      ...objectValue(settings.image),
      url: ref,
      filename: ref,
      localPath: ref,
    };
    element.settings = settings;
    }
  }
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      for (const item of value) visit(item);
      return;
    }
    const filename = firstString(value.filename, value.localPath, value.local, value.asset);
    const dataUri = firstString(value.url, value.full, value.sourceUrl, value.src);
    if (filename && /^data:image\//i.test(dataUri)) {
      const normalized = normalizeStageBLocalAssetRef(filename) || String(filename).trim().replace(/\\/g, '/').replace(/^\.\/+/, '');
      if (normalized && !normalized.includes('..')) {
        writes.set(normalized, dataUri);
      }
    }
    for (const item of Object.values(value)) {
      visit(item);
    }
  };
  visit(result);

  const workspaceRoot = path.resolve(workspaceDir);
  for (const [ref, dataUri] of writes.entries()) {
    if (stageBLocalAssetExists(workspaceDir, ref)) continue;
    const match = String(dataUri).match(/^data:([^;,]+)(;base64)?,([\s\S]*)$/i);
    if (!match) continue;
    const mimeType = String(match[1] || '').toLowerCase();
    if (!/^image\/(?:png|jpe?g|webp|avif|gif|svg\+xml)$/.test(mimeType)) continue;
    const targetPath = path.resolve(workspaceDir, ref);
    if (!targetPath.startsWith(`${workspaceRoot}${path.sep}`)) continue;
    const body = match[3] || '';
    const buffer = match[2] ? Buffer.from(body, 'base64') : Buffer.from(decodeURIComponent(body), 'utf8');
    if (buffer.length <= 0 || buffer.length > 25 * 1024 * 1024) continue;
    await fs.mkdir(path.dirname(targetPath), { recursive: true });
    await fs.writeFile(targetPath, buffer);
  }
}

function collectStageBRuntimeDataImageMap(stageAHtml) {
  // Pixflow-owned: some accepted prototypes intentionally keep compact HTML
  // by storing inline image data in a runtime map and assigning it to <img
  // data-img="..."> nodes. Bricks needs concrete asset refs instead.
  const html = firstString(stageAHtml);
  const maps = new Map();
  const pattern = /window\.__[A-Za-z0-9_]*IMGS__\s*=\s*(\{[\s\S]*?\})\s*;?\s*<\/script>/g;
  for (const match of html.matchAll(pattern)) {
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(match[1]);
      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(objectValue(parsed))) {
        if (key && /^data:image\//i.test(firstString(value))) {
          maps.set(key, firstString(value));
        }
      }
    } catch (error) {
      // Ignore non-JSON script fragments; Stage B can still use explicit src attrs.
    }
  }
  return maps;
}

function stageBDataUriExtension(dataUri) {
  const mimeType = String(dataUri || '').match(/^data:([^;,]+)/i)?.[1]?.toLowerCase() || '';
  if (mimeType === 'image/svg+xml') return 'svg';
  if (mimeType === 'image/jpeg') return 'jpg';
  if (mimeType === 'image/png') return 'png';
  if (mimeType === 'image/webp') return 'webp';
  if (mimeType === 'image/avif') return 'avif';
  if (mimeType === 'image/gif') return 'gif';
  return '';
}

function isStageBHslChannelValue(value) {
  const text = String(value || '').trim();
  return /^-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?(?:deg|rad|turn)?\s+\d+(?:\.\d+)?%\s+\d+(?:\.\d+)?%(?:\s*\/\s*(?:\d+(?:\.\d+)?%?|var\([^)]+\)))?$/i.test(text);
}

function normalizeStageBControlSelectorSpecificity(result) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks form defaults have higher specificity than source
  // selectors like `.search-box input`. Prefix carried form-control selectors
  // so source field styling survives on the frontend.
  const strengthenCss = (cssText) => String(cssText || '').replace(/([^{}@]+)\{([^{}]*)\}/g, (match, selectorText, body) => {
    if (!/\b(?:input|textarea|select)\b/i.test(selectorText)) return match;
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(selectorText).map((selector) => {
      const trimmed = selector.trim();
      if (!trimmed || /^#brx-content\b/i.test(trimmed) || /^(?:html|body|:root)\b/i.test(trimmed)) {
        return trimmed;
      }
      if (!/\b(?:input|textarea|select)\b/i.test(trimmed)) {
        return trimmed;
      }
      return `#brx-content ${trimmed}`;
    }).filter(Boolean);
    return `${selectors.join(', ')} {${body}}`;
  });

  for (const settings of [
    objectValue(result.page_settings || result.pageSettings),
    objectValue(result.stage_b_page_settings || result.stageBPageSettings),
  ]) {
    if (typeof settings.customCss === 'string') {
      settings.customCss = strengthenCss(settings.customCss);
    }
  }
  for (const classItem of arrayValue(result.global_classes || result.globalClasses)) {
    const settings = objectValue(classItem?.settings);
    if (typeof settings._cssCustom === 'string') {
      settings._cssCustom = strengthenCss(settings._cssCustom);
    }
  }
}

function normalizeStageBSourceControlSelectorCss(result, styleMap) {
  // Pixflow-owned: child selectors for real source controls, such as
  // `.email-row input`, cannot live on a single Bricks global class. Preserve
  // those selectors in page CSS so native Bricks form fields keep Stage A
  // control styling during handoff.
  const rules = collectStageBSourceControlRules(arrayValue(objectValue(styleMap).rules));
  if (rules.length === 0) return;
  const chunks = [];
  const selectorGroups = [];
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const declarations = serializePixflowCssDeclarations(rule.declarations);
    if (!declarations) continue;
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector)
      .map((selector) => selector.trim())
      .filter(Boolean)
      .map((selector) => /^#brx-content\b/i.test(selector) ? selector : `#brx-content ${selector}`);
    if (selectors.length === 0) continue;
    chunks.push(`${selectors.join(', ')} { ${declarations} }`);
    selectorGroups.push(rule.selector);
  }
  if (chunks.length === 0) return;
  const block = chunks.join('\n');
  for (const key of ['page_settings', 'stage_b_page_settings']) {
    const settings = objectValue(result[key]);
    const existing = firstString(settings.customCss);
    settings.customCss = replaceStageBPageCssSelectorGroups(existing, selectorGroups, block);
    result[key] = settings;
  }
}

function normalizedStageBPageCssSelectorGroup(selectorText) {
  const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(selectorText)
    .map((selector) => selector.trim())
    .filter(Boolean)
    .map((selector) => /^#brx-content\b/i.test(selector) ? selector : `#brx-content ${selector}`);
  return normalizeWhitespace(selectors.join(', '));
}

function replaceStageBPageCssSelectorGroups(cssText, selectorGroups, block) {
  // Pixflow-owned source descendant/attribute rules are compiler authority.
  // Replace every prior copy (including pre-fix rem/px variants) before adding
  // the canonical block so normalization is byte-stable and captured visual
  // evidence remains signed to the exact artifact that QA inspects.
  const targets = new Set(
    arrayValue(selectorGroups)
      .map((selector) => normalizedStageBPageCssSelectorGroup(selector))
      .filter(Boolean)
  );
  const cleaned = String(cssText || '').replace(/([^{}@]+)\{([^{}]*)\}/g, (match, rawSelector) => {
    const leadingWhitespace = String(rawSelector || '').match(/^\s*/)?.[0] || '';
    const normalizedSelector = normalizeWhitespace(String(rawSelector || '').trim());
    return targets.has(normalizedSelector) ? leadingWhitespace : match;
  }).trim();
  return [cleaned, block].filter(Boolean).join('\n');
}

function normalizeStageBSourceAttributeSelectorCss(result, styleMap) {
  // Pixflow-owned: safe prototype interaction states such as data-reveal are
  // driven by attribute selectors rather than classes. Preserve those rules in
  // page CSS so the accepted Stage A reveal/visibility mechanics survive the
  // Bricks handoff.
  const rules = arrayValue(objectValue(styleMap).rules).filter((rule) => {
    const selector = firstString(rule.selector);
    if (!/\[(?:data-reveal|data-delay)\b/i.test(selector)) return false;
    const declarations = objectValue(rule.declarations);
    return Object.keys(declarations).some((key) => [
      'opacity',
      'transform',
      'transition',
      'transition-delay',
      'animation',
    ].includes(key));
  });
  if (rules.length === 0) return;
  const chunks = [];
  const selectorGroups = [];
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const declarations = serializePixflowCssDeclarations(rule.declarations);
    if (!declarations) continue;
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector)
      .map((selector) => selector.trim())
      .filter(Boolean)
      .map((selector) => /^#brx-content\b/i.test(selector) ? selector : `#brx-content ${selector}`);
    if (selectors.length === 0) continue;
    chunks.push(`${selectors.join(', ')} { ${declarations} }`);
    selectorGroups.push(rule.selector);
  }
  if (chunks.length === 0) return;
  const block = chunks.join('\n');
  for (const key of ['page_settings', 'stage_b_page_settings']) {
    const settings = objectValue(result[key]);
    const existing = firstString(settings.customCss);
    settings.customCss = replaceStageBPageCssSelectorGroups(existing, selectorGroups, block);
    result[key] = settings;
  }
}

function normalizeStageBTypographyFontFamilies(root, fontSystem, priorFontSystem = {}) {
  // Pixflow-owned: model repairs sometimes output CSS font token variables in
  // Bricks typography controls. Bricks expects concrete family names here; the
  // variable contract lives in stage-b-font-system.json.
  const roleTokenByName = new Map();
  const literalFamilyByName = new Map();
  for (const token of arrayValue(objectValue(fontSystem).roleTokens)) {
    const name = firstString(token?.name);
    const primaryFamily = firstString(token?.primaryFamily);
    if (name && primaryFamily && !roleTokenByName.has(name)) {
      roleTokenByName.set(name, primaryFamily);
    }
    const originalPrimaryFamily = firstString(token?.originalPrimaryFamily);
    if (originalPrimaryFamily && primaryFamily && originalPrimaryFamily !== primaryFamily) {
      literalFamilyByName.set(originalPrimaryFamily, primaryFamily);
    }
  }
  const availableFamilies = new Set(arrayValue(objectValue(fontSystem).fonts)
    .map((font) => normalizeStageBFontFamilyId(firstString(font?.family)))
    .filter(Boolean));
  for (const token of arrayValue(objectValue(fontSystem).roleTokens)) {
    const primaryFamily = firstString(token?.primaryFamily);
    if (!primaryFamily || !availableFamilies.has(normalizeStageBFontFamilyId(primaryFamily))) continue;
    const priorParityFallback = findStageBFontStackFallback(firstString(token?.value));
    if (priorParityFallback && priorParityFallback !== primaryFamily) {
      // Older prepared workspaces materialized the system fallback before
      // local-font sidecars were supported. Once the exact accepted font is
      // installable, migrate those concrete fallback controls back to it.
      literalFamilyByName.set(priorParityFallback, primaryFamily);
    }
  }
  for (const token of arrayValue(objectValue(priorFontSystem).roleTokens)) {
    if (token?.parityFallback !== true) continue;
    const originalPrimaryFamily = firstString(token?.originalPrimaryFamily);
    const fallbackFamily = firstString(token?.primaryFamily);
    if (
      originalPrimaryFamily
      && fallbackFamily
      && availableFamilies.has(normalizeStageBFontFamilyId(originalPrimaryFamily))
    ) {
      literalFamilyByName.set(fallbackFamily, originalPrimaryFamily);
    }
  }
  if ((roleTokenByName.size === 0 && literalFamilyByName.size === 0) || !root || typeof root !== 'object') {
    return;
  }

  const visit = (value) => {
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      for (const item of value) visit(item);
      return;
    }
    const typography = objectValue(value._typography);
    const fontFamily = firstString(typography['font-family']);
    const match = /^var\(\s*(--[^),\s]+)\s*(?:,[^)]+)?\)$/i.exec(fontFamily);
    if (match && roleTokenByName.has(match[1])) {
      typography['font-family'] = roleTokenByName.get(match[1]);
      value._typography = typography;
    } else if (fontFamily && literalFamilyByName.has(fontFamily)) {
      typography['font-family'] = literalFamilyByName.get(fontFamily);
      value._typography = typography;
    }
    for (const key of ['_cssCustom', 'customCss']) {
      if (typeof value[key] === 'string') {
        value[key] = normalizeStageBFontCssTextFamilies(value[key], literalFamilyByName);
      }
    }
    for (const child of Object.values(value)) {
      visit(child);
    }
  };

  visit(root);
}

function normalizeStageBFontCssTextFamilies(cssText, literalFamilyByName) {
  if (!cssText || !(literalFamilyByName instanceof Map) || literalFamilyByName.size === 0) {
    return cssText;
  }
  let result = String(cssText);
  for (const [sourceFamily, replacementFamily] of literalFamilyByName.entries()) {
    const escaped = escapeRegExp(sourceFamily);
    result = result.replace(new RegExp(`font-family\\s*:\\s*(['"]?)${escaped}\\1\\s*;`, 'gi'), `font-family: ${replacementFamily};`);
  }
  return result;
}

function stageBElementContainsDynamicTag(value, depth = 0) {
  if (depth > 8 || value == null) return false;
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    return /\{(?:post|query|term|user|author|echo|acf|mb|woo|url|date|wp|featured_image|site|archive|filter)[_:]/i.test(value);
  }
  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.some((item) => stageBElementContainsDynamicTag(item, depth + 1));
  if (typeof value !== 'object') return false;
  return Object.values(value).some((item) => stageBElementContainsDynamicTag(item, depth + 1));
}

function stageBConditionGroupsAreValid(value) {
  return Array.isArray(value)
    && value.length > 0
    && value.every((group) => Array.isArray(group)
      && group.length > 0
      && group.every((row) => {
        const condition = objectValue(row);
        const compare = firstString(condition.compare, condition.operator);
        return Boolean(firstString(condition.key))
          && Boolean(compare)
          && (['empty', 'empty_not'].includes(compare) || firstString(condition.value, condition.dynamic_data, condition.dynamicDataTag) !== '');
      }));
}

function stageBControlIsEnabled(value) {
  if (value === true || value === 1) return true;
  if (typeof value !== 'string') return false;
  return ['1', 'true', 'yes', 'on'].includes(value.trim().toLowerCase());
}

export function inspectStageBGenerationRequirements(content, requirements) {
  const normalized = normalizeStageBGenerationRequirements(requirements);
  const elements = Array.isArray(content) ? content.filter((item) => item && typeof item === 'object' && !Array.isArray(item)) : [];
  const matches = {};
  const issues = [];
  for (const requirement of normalized) {
    const kind = firstString(requirement.kind);
    const matchedIds = elements.flatMap((element, index) => {
      const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
      let matched = false;
      if (kind === 'query_loop') {
        const query = objectValue(settings.query);
        matched = stageBControlIsEnabled(settings.hasLoop) && Object.keys(query).length > 0 && Boolean(firstString(query.objectType, query.object_type));
      } else if (kind === 'conditions') {
        matched = stageBConditionGroupsAreValid(settings._conditions);
      } else if (kind === 'dynamic_data') {
        matched = stageBElementContainsDynamicTag(settings);
      } else if (kind === 'interactions') {
        matched = Array.isArray(settings._interactions) && settings._interactions.length > 0;
      } else if (kind === 'form') {
        matched = firstString(element.name, element.type).toLowerCase() === 'form'
          && Array.isArray(settings.fields)
          && settings.fields.length > 0;
      }
      return matched ? [firstString(element.id, `${kind}-${index + 1}`)] : [];
    });
    matches[kind] = matchedIds;
    const minimumMatches = Number(requirement.minimumMatches || 1);
    if (matchedIds.length < minimumMatches) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue(
        `stage_b_generation_requirement_missing_${kind}`,
        'p0',
        `Generated payload requires at least ${minimumMatches} validated ${kind} target${minimumMatches === 1 ? '' : 's'}, but found ${matchedIds.length}. Refuse the partial build and configure the requested capability before apply.`
      ));
    }
  }
  if (normalized.some((requirement) => requirement.kind === 'query_loop')) {
    issues.push(...inspectStageBQueryLoopTemplateDuplicates(elements));
  }
  return { requirements: normalized, matches, issues };
}

function inspectStageBQueryLoopTemplateDuplicates(elements) {
  const byId = new Map();
  const childrenByParent = new Map();
  for (const element of arrayValue(elements)) {
    const id = firstString(element?.id);
    if (!id) continue;
    byId.set(id, element);
    const parentId = firstString(element?.parent);
    if (parentId) {
      const siblings = childrenByParent.get(parentId) || [];
      siblings.push(id);
      childrenByParent.set(parentId, siblings);
    }
  }

  const structuralSignature = (elementId, depth = 0, seen = new Set()) => {
    if (!elementId || depth > 12 || seen.has(elementId)) return '';
    const element = byId.get(elementId);
    if (!element) return '';
    const nextSeen = new Set(seen);
    nextSeen.add(elementId);
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    const classIds = arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses || settings.cssGlobalClasses)
      .map((value) => firstString(value))
      .filter(Boolean)
      .sort();
    const childIds = arrayValue(element.children).map((value) => firstString(value)).filter(Boolean);
    const resolvedChildIds = childIds.length > 0 ? childIds : (childrenByParent.get(elementId) || []);
    const childSignatures = resolvedChildIds
      .map((childId) => structuralSignature(childId, depth + 1, nextSeen))
      .filter(Boolean)
      .sort();
    return `${firstString(element.name, element.type).toLowerCase()}|${classIds.join(',')}|[${childSignatures.join(';')}]`;
  };

  const issues = [];
  for (const element of byId.values()) {
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    const query = objectValue(settings.query);
    if (!stageBControlIsEnabled(settings.hasLoop) || stageBQueryLoopRepeatCount(query) <= 1) continue;
    const elementId = firstString(element.id);
    const parentId = firstString(element.parent);
    if (!elementId || !parentId) continue;
    const signature = structuralSignature(elementId);
    if (!signature) continue;
    const duplicates = (childrenByParent.get(parentId) || [])
      .filter((siblingId) => siblingId !== elementId)
      .filter((siblingId) => !stageBControlIsEnabled(objectValue(byId.get(siblingId)?.settings).hasLoop))
      .filter((siblingId) => structuralSignature(siblingId) === signature);
    if (duplicates.length === 0) continue;
    issues.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_query_loop_static_template_duplicates',
      'p0',
      `Query Loop target ${elementId} still has ${duplicates.length} static sibling template${duplicates.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} (${duplicates.join(', ')}). Keep one native repeated-item/card wrapper, apply the query to it, and remove only its duplicated generated placeholders before apply.`
    ));
  }
  return issues;
}

async function analyzeStageBResult(prepared, options = {}) {
  const result = await readJsonFile(prepared.resultFile, 'Stage B Bricks result');
  const issues = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const content = Array.isArray(result.content) ? result.content : [];
  const globalClasses = Array.isArray(result.global_classes)
    ? result.global_classes
    : Array.isArray(result.globalClasses)
      ? result.globalClasses
      : [];
  const headerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_header || result.stageBHeader);
  const headerContent = Array.isArray(headerSpec.content)
    ? headerSpec.content
    : (Array.isArray(result.header_content) ? result.header_content : []);
  const headerIncluded = headerSpec.includeHeader === true || headerSpec.include_header === true || headerSpec.include === true;
  const footerSpec = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer || result.stageBFooter);
  const footerContent = Array.isArray(footerSpec.content)
    ? footerSpec.content
    : (Array.isArray(result.footer_content) ? result.footer_content : []);
  const footerIncluded = footerSpec.includeFooter === true || footerSpec.include_footer === true || footerSpec.include === true;
  const headerPlan = objectValue(result.stage_b_header_plan || result.stageBHeaderPlan || await readOptionalJson(prepared.headerPlanFile || ''));
  const footerPlan = objectValue(result.stage_b_footer_plan || result.stageBFooterPlan || await readOptionalJson(prepared.footerPlanFile || ''));
  const routeContract = objectValue(result.stage_b_route_contract || await readOptionalJson(prepared.routeContractFile || ''));
  const themeStyleContract = objectValue(result.stage_b_theme_style_contract || await readOptionalJson(prepared.themeStyleContractFile || ''));
  const themeStyleHealth = objectValue(result.stage_b_theme_style_health || await readOptionalJson(prepared.themeStyleHealthFile || ''));
  const resultFontSystem = objectValue(result.stage_b_font_system || result.stageBFontSystem || result.font_system || result.fontSystem);
  const fontSystem = objectValue(Object.keys(resultFontSystem).length > 0 ? resultFontSystem : await readOptionalJson(prepared.fontSystemFile || ''));
  const resultIconSystem = objectValue(result.stage_b_icon_system || result.stageBIconSystem || result.icon_system || result.iconSystem);
  const iconSystem = objectValue(Object.keys(resultIconSystem).length > 0 ? resultIconSystem : await readOptionalJson(prepared.iconSystemFile || ''));
  const pageSettings = objectValue(result.stage_b_page_settings || result.stageBPageSettings || result.page_settings || result.pageSettings);
  const pageEditMode = prepared?.stageBMetadata?.pageEditMode === true
    || prepared?.pageEditMode === true
    || existsSync(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir || '', 'stage-a', 'current-page-edit-context.json'));
  const pageEditChangeReport = objectValue(
    result.page_edit_change_report
      || result.pageEditChangeReport
      || objectValue(result.diagnostics).page_edit_change_report
      || objectValue(result.diagnostics).pageEditChangeReport
  );
  const conversionPolicy = summarizeStageBConversionPolicy(
    await readOptionalJson(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir || '', 'stage-a', 'conversion-policy.json'))
  );
  const generationScope = normalizeStageBGenerationScope(conversionPolicy.generationScope);
  const generationRequirementQa = inspectStageBGenerationRequirements(content, conversionPolicy.generationRequirements);
  if (options.enforceGenerationRequirements !== false) {
    issues.push(...generationRequirementQa.issues);
  }

  if (result.type !== 'direct_page_generation') {
    issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_result_type_invalid', 'p0', 'bricks-result.json must use type direct_page_generation.'));
  }
  if (result.payload_format !== 'bricks_json') {
    issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_payload_format_invalid', 'p0', 'payload_format must be bricks_json.'));
  }
  if (result.payload_included !== true) {
    issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_payload_not_included', 'p0', 'payload_included must be true.'));
  }
  if (content.length === 0) {
    issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_content_empty', 'p0', 'content must contain Bricks elements.'));
  }
  if (globalClasses.length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_classes_empty', 'p1', 'global_classes is empty; conversion may lose craft-level style control.'));
  }
  if (Object.keys(routeContract).length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_route_contract_missing', 'p1', 'stage-b-route-contract.json or bricks-result.json.stage_b_route_contract is missing.'));
  }
  if (Object.keys(themeStyleContract).length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_theme_style_contract_missing', 'p1', 'stage-b-theme-style-contract.json or bricks-result.json.stage_b_theme_style_contract is missing.'));
  }
  const stagedFontSystem = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.fontSystemFile || ''));
  if (Object.keys(stagedFontSystem).length > 0 && Object.keys(resultFontSystem).length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_font_system_missing', 'p1', 'stage-b-font-system.json exists but bricks-result.json.stage_b_font_system is missing; Stage B insertion cannot preinstall source Google fonts.'));
  }
  const stagedIconSystem = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.iconSystemFile || ''));
  if (Object.keys(stagedIconSystem).length > 0 && Object.keys(resultIconSystem).length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_icon_system_missing', 'p1', 'stage-b-icon-system.json exists but bricks-result.json.stage_b_icon_system is missing; Stage B insertion cannot preinstall source Tabler SVG icons.'));
  }
  const pageSettingsIssues = inspectStageBPageSettings(pageSettings, result);
  issues.push(...pageSettingsIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...pageSettingsIssues.warnings);
  const sourceMap = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.sourceMapFile || ''));
  const stageAHtml = await readOptionalText(firstString(sourceMap?.source?.artifactFile));
  const sourceContainsH1 = /<h1\b/i.test(stageAHtml);
  const styleMap = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.styleMapFile || ''));
  const sourceFidelityIssues = inspectStageBSourceCssFidelity({
    styleMap,
    content,
    headerContent,
    footerContent,
    globalClasses,
    pageSettings,
    result,
  });
  issues.push(...sourceFidelityIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...sourceFidelityIssues.warnings);
  const sourceSemanticIssues = inspectStageBSourceSemanticFidelity({
    sourceMap,
    headerPlan,
    footerPlan,
    stageAHtml,
    content,
    headerContent,
    footerContent,
    pageSettings,
    result,
  });
  issues.push(...sourceSemanticIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...sourceSemanticIssues.warnings);
  const visualParityIssues = inspectStageBVisualParityReport(
    await readOptionalJson(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir || '', 'stage-b-visual-parity.json')),
    prepared
  );
  issues.push(...visualParityIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...visualParityIssues.warnings);
  const resultColorSystem = objectValue(result.stage_b_color_system || result.stageBColorSystem || result.color_system || result.colorSystem);
  const stagedColorSystem = objectValue(Object.keys(resultColorSystem).length > 0 ? resultColorSystem : await readOptionalJson(prepared.colorSystemFile || ''));
  const routeContextReport = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.routeContextReportFile || ''));
  const routeContractQa = inspectStageBRouteContractQa({
    result,
    content,
    headerContent,
    footerContent,
    globalClasses,
    pageSettings,
    routeContract,
    routeContextReport,
    colorSystem: stagedColorSystem,
    themeStyleContract,
  });
  issues.push(...routeContractQa.errors);
  warnings.push(...routeContractQa.warnings);
  if (stageBColorSystemRequiresPageBackgroundCss(stagedColorSystem, pageSettings)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_page_background_css_missing',
      'p1',
      'Stage A declares a body/page colour system, but page_settings.customCss does not apply the page background/text tokens. Bricks sections with transparent backgrounds will render on the WordPress theme background.'
    ));
  }

  if (pageEditMode) {
    const sidecarReport = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.pageEditChangeReportFile || ''));
    const reportType = firstString(pageEditChangeReport.type);
    const applyMode = firstString(pageEditChangeReport.applyMode, pageEditChangeReport.apply_mode);
    const fullRebuildExplicit = pageEditChangeReport.fullRebuildExplicitlyRequested === true
      || pageEditChangeReport.full_rebuild_explicitly_requested === true
      || applyMode === 'full_rebuild_explicit';
    const preservedEntries = [
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.preservedSections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.preserved_sections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.preservedElements),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.preserved_elements),
    ];
    const changedEntries = [
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.changedSections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.changed_sections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.changedElements),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.changed_elements),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.createdSections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.created_sections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.removedSections),
      ...arrayValue(pageEditChangeReport.removed_sections),
    ];
    if (reportType !== 'pixflow_page_edit_change_report') {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_change_report_missing', 'p0', 'Page edit Stage B must write bricks-result.json.page_edit_change_report with type pixflow_page_edit_change_report.'));
    }
    if (Object.keys(sidecarReport).length === 0) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_change_report_sidecar_missing', 'p0', 'Page edit Stage B must write page-edit-change-report.json as the sidecar copy of bricks-result.json.page_edit_change_report.'));
    }
    if (!applyMode) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_apply_mode_missing', 'p0', 'Page edit change report must include applyMode, normally targeted_merge.'));
    }
    if (!fullRebuildExplicit && preservedEntries.length === 0) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_preserved_sections_missing', 'p0', 'Page edit change report must list preserved sections or elements unless the user explicitly requested a full rebuild.'));
    }
    if (changedEntries.length === 0) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_changed_sections_thin', 'p1', 'Page edit change report should list changed, created, or removed sections/elements.'));
    }
    if (fullRebuildExplicit && pageEditChangeReport.fullRebuildExplicitlyRequested !== true && pageEditChangeReport.full_rebuild_explicitly_requested !== true) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_edit_full_rebuild_flag_missing', 'p0', 'Full rebuild page edits must set fullRebuildExplicitlyRequested: true in the change report.'));
    }
  }

  const inlineMarkupClassNames = collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNames([
    ...content,
    ...headerContent,
    ...footerContent,
  ]);
  const baselineResult = objectValue(await readOptionalJson(prepared.baselineResultFile || ''));
  const sourceOwnedClassNames = arrayValue(baselineResult.global_classes || baselineResult.globalClasses)
    .map((classItem) => firstString(classItem?.name))
    .filter(Boolean);
  const templateContainsH1 = [headerContent, footerContent].some((elements) => (
    (headerIncluded || footerIncluded)
    && elements.some((element) => (
      firstString(element?.name) === 'heading'
      && /^h1$/i.test(firstString(objectValue(element?.settings).tag, objectValue(element?.settings).customTag))
    ))
  ));
  const validation = inspectStageBBricksPayload(content, globalClasses, prepared.workspaceDir, {
    // Uploaded HTML is a clone contract: do not invent an H1 when the source
    // document does not have one. Generated page routes still retain the
    // semantic H1 requirement, while source-faithful clones follow the input.
    requirePageH1: generationScope === 'full_page'
      && (conversionPolicy.conversionProfile !== 'uploaded_html' || sourceContainsH1)
      && !templateContainsH1,
    iconSystem,
    inlineMarkupClassNames,
    strictClassOnlyStyles: conversionPolicy.conversionProfile === 'prototype_bricks',
    sourceOwnedClassNames,
  });
  issues.push(...validation.errors);
  warnings.push(...validation.warnings);
  let headerValidation = null;
  if (headerIncluded) {
    if (!['current_page', 'sitewide'].includes(firstString(headerSpec.scope))) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_scope_invalid', 'p0', 'stage_b_header.scope must be current_page or sitewide when includeHeader is true.'));
    }
    if (firstString(headerSpec.templateType, headerSpec.template_type) !== 'header') {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_template_type_invalid', 'p0', 'stage_b_header.templateType must be header.'));
    }
    if (headerContent.length === 0) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_content_empty', 'p0', 'stage_b_header.content must contain Bricks elements when includeHeader is true.'));
    } else {
      headerValidation = inspectStageBBricksPayload(headerContent, globalClasses, prepared.workspaceDir, {
        requireTopLevelSection: false,
        iconSystem,
        inlineMarkupClassNames,
        validateGlobalClassDefinitions: false,
        // Pixflow-owned: header templates need real Bricks layout controls on wrapper elements.
        templateArea: 'header',
        skipSourceIconUsageCheck: true,
      });
      issues.push(...headerValidation.errors.map((issue) => ({
        ...issue,
        id: `stage_b_header_${issue.id}`,
        message: `Header payload: ${issue.message}`,
      })));
      warnings.push(...headerValidation.warnings.map((issue) => ({
        ...issue,
        id: `stage_b_header_${issue.id}`,
        message: `Header payload: ${issue.message}`,
      })));
      const headerLayoutValidation = inspectStageBHeaderLayoutContract(headerContent, {
        ...headerPlan,
        ...headerSpec,
        sourceSectionOdId: firstString(
          headerSpec.sourceSectionOdId,
          headerSpec.source_section_od_id,
          headerSpec.selectedSectionOdId,
          headerSpec.selected_section_od_id,
          headerPlan.sourceSectionOdId,
          headerPlan.source_section_od_id,
          headerPlan.selectedSectionOdId,
          headerPlan.selected_section_od_id,
        ),
      }, globalClasses);
      issues.push(...headerLayoutValidation.errors);
      warnings.push(...headerLayoutValidation.warnings);
    }
  }
  let footerValidation = null;
  if (footerIncluded) {
    if (!['current_page', 'sitewide'].includes(firstString(footerSpec.scope))) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_footer_scope_invalid', 'p0', 'stage_b_footer.scope must be current_page or sitewide when includeFooter is true.'));
    }
    if (firstString(footerSpec.templateType, footerSpec.template_type) !== 'footer') {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_footer_template_type_invalid', 'p0', 'stage_b_footer.templateType must be footer.'));
    }
    if (footerContent.length === 0) {
      issues.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_footer_content_empty', 'p0', 'stage_b_footer.content must contain Bricks elements when includeFooter is true.'));
    } else {
      footerValidation = inspectStageBBricksPayload(footerContent, globalClasses, prepared.workspaceDir, {
        requireTopLevelSection: false,
        iconSystem,
        inlineMarkupClassNames,
        validateGlobalClassDefinitions: false,
        // Pixflow-owned: footer templates need real Bricks layout controls on wrapper elements.
        templateArea: 'footer',
        skipSourceIconUsageCheck: true,
      });
      issues.push(...footerValidation.errors.map((issue) => ({
        ...issue,
        id: `stage_b_footer_${issue.id}`,
        message: `Footer payload: ${issue.message}`,
      })));
      warnings.push(...footerValidation.warnings.map((issue) => ({
        ...issue,
        id: `stage_b_footer_${issue.id}`,
        message: `Footer payload: ${issue.message}`,
      })));
      const footerPaddingValidation = inspectStageBTemplateSectionPaddingContract(footerContent, globalClasses, 'footer');
      issues.push(...footerPaddingValidation.errors);
      warnings.push(...footerPaddingValidation.warnings);
    }
  }

  const payloadFileContent = await readOptionalJson(prepared.payloadFile);
  if (Array.isArray(payloadFileContent) && payloadFileContent.length !== content.length) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_payload_sidecar_mismatch', 'p1', 'bricks-payload.json length differs from bricks-result.json content length.'));
  } else if (!Array.isArray(payloadFileContent)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_payload_sidecar_missing', 'p1', 'bricks-payload.json is missing or not an array.'));
  }

  const classesFileContent = await readOptionalJson(prepared.globalClassesFile);
  if (Array.isArray(classesFileContent) && classesFileContent.length !== globalClasses.length) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_classes_sidecar_mismatch', 'p1', 'global-classes.json length differs from bricks-result.json global_classes length.'));
  } else if (!Array.isArray(classesFileContent)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_classes_sidecar_missing', 'p1', 'global-classes.json is missing or not an array.'));
  }

  if (prepared.headerPayloadFile) {
    const headerFileContent = await readOptionalJson(prepared.headerPayloadFile);
    if (headerIncluded && Array.isArray(headerFileContent) && headerFileContent.length !== headerContent.length) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_payload_sidecar_mismatch', 'p1', 'bricks-header-payload.json length differs from bricks-result.json stage_b_header.content length.'));
    } else if (headerIncluded && !Array.isArray(headerFileContent)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_payload_sidecar_missing', 'p1', 'bricks-header-payload.json is missing or not an array.'));
    }
  }
  if (prepared.footerPayloadFile) {
    const footerFileContent = await readOptionalJson(prepared.footerPayloadFile);
    if (footerIncluded && Array.isArray(footerFileContent) && footerFileContent.length !== footerContent.length) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_footer_payload_sidecar_mismatch', 'p1', 'bricks-footer-payload.json length differs from bricks-result.json stage_b_footer.content length.'));
    } else if (footerIncluded && !Array.isArray(footerFileContent)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_footer_payload_sidecar_missing', 'p1', 'bricks-footer-payload.json is missing or not an array.'));
    }
  }

  const report = await readOptionalText(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'conversion-report.md'));
  if (report.trim().length < 300) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_conversion_report_thin', 'p1', 'conversion-report.md should include section mapping and preservation notes.'));
  }
  const handoffCritique = await readOptionalText(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'handoff-critique.md'));
  if (handoffCritique.trim().length < 300) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_handoff_critique_missing',
      'p1',
      'handoff-critique.md is missing or too thin. Stage B must compare source HTML against the Bricks payload and document source-fidelity repairs before final QA.'
    ));
  }

  const severity = severityCounts([...issues, ...warnings]);
  const blocking = severity.p0 > 0;
  const score = Math.max(0, 100 - (severity.p0 * 30) - (severity.p1 * 10) - (severity.p2 * 3));
  return {
    status: blocking ? 'failed' : 'passed',
    blocking,
    score,
    summary: {
      elementCount: content.length,
      headerElementCount: headerContent.length,
      footerElementCount: footerContent.length,
      globalClassCount: globalClasses.length,
      topLevelSectionCount: validation.topLevelSectionCount,
      headerTopLevelSectionCount: headerValidation?.topLevelSectionCount || 0,
      footerTopLevelSectionCount: footerValidation?.topLevelSectionCount || 0,
      supportedElementCount: validation.supportedElementCount,
      headingTagCounts: validation.headingTagCounts,
      generationScope,
      generationRequirements: generationRequirementQa.requirements,
      generationRequirementMatches: generationRequirementQa.matches,
      routeId: firstString(routeContract.routeId),
      routeFamily: firstString(routeContract.routeFamily),
      styleMode: firstString(routeContract.styleMode),
      themeStyleMode: firstString(themeStyleContract.mode),
      themeStyleHealthStatus: firstString(themeStyleHealth.status),
      safeToLeanOnThemeStyles: themeStyleContract.safeToLeanOnThemeStyles === true,
      iconSystem: summarizeStageBIconSystem(iconSystem),
      iconUsageCount: validation.iconUsageCount,
      headerIconUsageCount: headerValidation?.iconUsageCount || 0,
      footerIconUsageCount: footerValidation?.iconUsageCount || 0,
    },
    severity,
    issues: [...issues, ...warnings],
  };
}

function isStageBSafeCssStateControlIsland(htmlValue) {
  const html = firstString(htmlValue);
  if (
    !html
    || /<\s*\/?\s*(?:form|script|style|select|textarea|button)\b/i.test(html)
    || /\son[a-z0-9_-]+\s*=/i.test(html)
    || /\s(?:formaction|formmethod|formenctype|formtarget)\s*=/i.test(html)
  ) return false;
  const inputs = [...html.matchAll(/<\s*input\b[^>]*>/gi)].map((match) => match[0]);
  if (inputs.length === 0) return false;
  const ids = [];
  for (const input of inputs) {
    if (!/\stype\s*=\s*(["']?)(?:radio|checkbox)\1(?:\s|>)/i.test(input)) return false;
    const id = input.match(/\sid\s*=\s*(["'])([^"']+)\1/i)?.[2];
    if (!id) return false;
    ids.push(id);
  }
  return ids.every((id) => new RegExp(`<\\s*label\\b[^>]*\\sfor\\s*=\\s*(["'])${id.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&')}\\1[^>]*>`, 'i').test(html));
}

function countStageBSafeCssStateControls(elements) {
  return arrayValue(elements).reduce((count, element) => {
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const html = firstString(settings.html);
    if (firstString(element?.name) !== 'html' || !isStageBSafeCssStateControlIsland(html)) return count;
    return count + [...html.matchAll(/<\s*input\b[^>]*>/gi)].length;
  }, 0);
}

function inspectStageBBricksPayload(content, globalClasses, workspaceDir = '', options = {}) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const allowed = new Set(getStageBAllowedElementNames());
  const ids = new Set();
  const classIds = new Set();
  const headingTagCounts = { h1: 0, h2: 0, h3: 0, h4: 0, h5: 0, h6: 0 };
  let topLevelSectionCount = 0;
  let supportedElementCount = 0;
  let actionElementCount = 0;
  const iconSystem = objectValue(options.iconSystem);
  const expectedIconCount = summarizeStageBIconSystem(iconSystem).iconCount;
  const iconUsages = [];
  const validateGlobalClassDefinitions = options.validateGlobalClassDefinitions !== false;

  for (const [index, classItem] of globalClasses.entries()) {
    if (!classItem || typeof classItem !== 'object' || Array.isArray(classItem)) {
      if (validateGlobalClassDefinitions) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_class_invalid', 'p0', `global_classes[${index}] must be an object.`));
      }
      continue;
    }
    const id = firstString(classItem.id);
    const name = firstString(classItem.name);
    if (validateGlobalClassDefinitions && (!id || !name)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_class_missing_identity', 'p0', `global_classes[${index}] is missing id or name.`));
    }
    if (id) classIds.add(id);
    if (!validateGlobalClassDefinitions) continue;
    if (shouldWarnStageBReservedButtonClass(name, options.sourceOwnedClassNames)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_button_class_reserved_fragment', 'p1', `Global class "${name}" contains reserved primary/secondary wording.`));
    }
    const settings = objectValue(classItem.settings);
    const classSettingsIssues = inspectStageBBricksSettings(settings, `Global class "${name}"`);
    errors.push(...classSettingsIssues.errors);
    const inlineMarkupClassNames = new Set(arrayValue(options.inlineMarkupClassNames).map((item) => firstString(item)).filter(Boolean));
    const customCssTargetsOnlyUnexposedInlineMarkup = stageBCustomCssTargetsOnlyUnexposedInlineMarkup(
      firstString(settings._cssCustom),
      inlineMarkupClassNames,
    );
    const isAuthoritativeMeasuredCompatibilityClass = /^pixflow-measured-[a-f0-9]+$/i.test(name);
    const classWarnings = inlineMarkupClassNames.has(name)
      || customCssTargetsOnlyUnexposedInlineMarkup
      || isAuthoritativeMeasuredCompatibilityClass
      ? classSettingsIssues.warnings.filter((issue) => issue.id !== 'stage_b_custom_css_contains_supported_declarations')
      : classSettingsIssues.warnings;
    warnings.push(...classWarnings.filter((issue) => !(
      issue.id === 'stage_b_custom_css_without_root'
      && isPixflowStageBUtilityAggregationClassName(name)
    )));
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'iconSize') || Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'iconColor')) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_svg_icon_class_font_controls',
        'p1',
        `Global class "${name}" uses iconSize/iconColor. Pixflow SVG icon classes must use nested settings.icon height/width/stroke/fill controls because Bricks styles SVG icons differently from font icons.`
      ));
    }
    const customCss = firstString(settings._cssCustom);
    const tokenDeclarationCount = countStageBRootCssVariableDeclarations(customCss);
    if (/(?:^|[-_])root$/i.test(name) || tokenDeclarationCount >= 4) {
      if (tokenDeclarationCount > 0 || /%root%::before/i.test(customCss)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue(
          'stage_b_root_token_bucket_class',
          'p0',
          `Global class "${name}" appears to store design tokens or page-wide root CSS. Use stage-b-color-system.json and native Bricks variables/palettes instead.`
        ));
      }
    }
    if (/\bstat\b/i.test(name) && String(settings?._border?.style || '').toLowerCase() === 'dashed') {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_stat_ring_approximated',
        'p1',
        `Global class "${name}" uses a dashed border on the stat container. Build stat rings as separate circular number elements plus label text.`
      ));
    }
    if (/\bplate\b/i.test(name) && settings?._border && String(settings._border.style || '').toLowerCase() === 'solid') {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_plate_border_added',
        'p1',
        `Global class "${name}" adds a solid border. Verify the accepted Stage A plate wrapper had this border before keeping it.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const globalClassById = buildStageBGlobalClassMap(globalClasses);

  for (const [index, element] of content.entries()) {
    if (!element || typeof element !== 'object' || Array.isArray(element)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_element_invalid', 'p0', `content[${index}] must be an object.`));
      continue;
    }
    const id = firstString(element.id);
    const name = firstString(element.name);
    if (!id || !name) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_element_missing_identity', 'p0', `content[${index}] is missing id or name.`));
      continue;
    }
    if (ids.has(id)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_duplicate_element_id', 'p0', `Duplicate Bricks element id "${id}".`));
    }
    ids.add(id);
    const safeCssStateIsland = name === 'html'
      && isStageBSafeCssStateControlIsland(firstString(objectValue(element.settings).html));
    if (!allowed.has(name) && !safeCssStateIsland) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_unsupported_element', 'p0', `Unsupported Bricks element "${name}".`));
    } else {
      supportedElementCount += 1;
    }
    if (name === 'button') {
      actionElementCount += 1;
      warnings.push(...inspectStageBButtonNativeOptionContract(element, globalClassById));
    }
    if (name === 'section' && !firstString(element.parent)) {
      topLevelSectionCount += 1;
      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(element, 'parent')) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_root_parent_missing', 'p0', `Top-level section "${id}" must explicitly set parent to an empty string.`));
      }
    } else if (!firstString(element.parent)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_non_section_root', 'p0', `Element "${id}" (${name}) has no parent. Only top-level section elements may have parent "".`));
    }
    if (!Array.isArray(element.children)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_children_invalid', 'p0', `Element "${id}" children must be an array.`));
    }
    for (const metadataKey of ['source', 'sourceUrl', 'version']) {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(element, metadataKey)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_copied_element_metadata', 'p0', `Element "${id}" includes copied-element metadata "${metadataKey}", which Bricks adds itself.`));
      }
    }
    const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
    const directStyleKeys = collectStageBElementDirectStyleKeys(settings);
    const disallowedDirectStyleKeys = filterStageBDisallowedElementDirectStyleKeys(directStyleKeys, {
      ...options,
      elementName: name,
      settings,
      allowUnclassedElementStyles: arrayValue(settings._cssGlobalClasses).length === 0,
    });
    if (disallowedDirectStyleKeys.length > 0) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_element_direct_style_disallowed',
        'p0',
        `Element "${id}" sets direct style keys (${disallowedDirectStyleKeys.slice(0, 10).join(', ')}). Stage B must put source CSS in global classes, not Bricks element/ID styling.`
      ));
    }
    if (firstString(settings._cssId)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_css_id_option_disallowed', 'p0', `Element "${id}" sets Bricks _cssId. Preserve source ids as _attributes only when needed for anchors; do not write the Bricks ID option in Stage B.`));
    }
    const elementIconUsages = safeCssStateIsland
      ? []
      : collectStageBIconUsages(settings, `Element "${id}"`, name);
    const artworkSvg = name === 'svg' && isStageBSvgArtworkCodeElement(settings);
    if (!artworkSvg) {
      iconUsages.push(...elementIconUsages);
    }
    if (
      name === 'icon'
      && elementIconUsages.some((usage) => usage.placeholder || usage.svg)
      && (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'iconSize') || Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'iconColor'))
    ) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_svg_icon_uses_font_style_controls',
        'p1',
        `Icon element "${id}" uses iconSize/iconColor with a Pixflow SVG icon. Move sizing/colour to a global class settings.icon object with height, width, stroke/fill, and optional strokeWidth.`
      ));
    }
    const settingsIssues = inspectStageBBricksSettings(settings, `Element "${id}"`);
    errors.push(...settingsIssues.errors);
    warnings.push(...settingsIssues.warnings);
    if (name === 'heading') {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'tagName')) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_heading_uses_tag_name', 'p0', `Heading element "${id}" uses tagName; Bricks requires settings.tag for semantic heading tags.`));
      }
      const tag = firstString(settings.tag).toLowerCase();
      const customTag = firstString(settings.customTag).toLowerCase();
      const semanticTag = /^h[1-6]$/.test(tag) ? tag : (/^h[1-6]$/.test(customTag) ? customTag : '');
      if (!semanticTag) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_heading_tag_missing', 'p0', `Heading element "${id}" must set settings.tag to h1-h6 so Bricks renders the intended semantic tag.`));
      } else if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(headingTagCounts, semanticTag)) {
        headingTagCounts[semanticTag] += 1;
      }
    }
    const attributeIssues = inspectStageBElementAttributes(settings, id);
    errors.push(...attributeIssues.errors);
    warnings.push(...attributeIssues.warnings);
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, '_cssGlobalClasses') && !Array.isArray(settings._cssGlobalClasses)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_class_refs_invalid', 'p0', `Element "${id}" _cssGlobalClasses must be an array of class id strings.`));
    }
    const refs = Array.isArray(settings._cssGlobalClasses) ? settings._cssGlobalClasses : [];
    for (const ref of refs) {
      if (ref && typeof ref === 'object') {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_class_ref_object', 'p0', `Element "${id}" _cssGlobalClasses contains an object; Bricks requires class id strings.`));
        continue;
      }
      const refId = firstString(ref);
      if (refId && !classIds.has(refId)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_global_class_ref_missing', 'p0', `Element "${id}" references missing global class id "${refId}".`));
      }
    }
    const linkIssues = inspectStageBLinkSetting(settings.link, `Element "${id}"`);
    errors.push(...linkIssues.errors);
    warnings.push(...linkIssues.warnings);
    if (name === 'image' && workspaceDir) {
      const localAssetRefs = collectStageBLocalAssetRefs(settings);
      const sourceRefs = collectStageBImageSourceRefs(settings);
      if (sourceRefs.length === 0) {
        // Pixflow-owned: generated handoff pages can legitimately reference
        // remote/source image URLs before media sideloading is implemented.
        // Keep this visible, but do not block a structurally valid handoff.
        warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_image_without_asset_ref', 'p2', `Image element "${id}" does not reference a local asset path or source URL.`));
      }
      for (const assetRef of localAssetRefs) {
        if (!stageBLocalAssetExists(workspaceDir, assetRef)) {
          warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_image_asset_missing', 'p1', `Image element "${id}" references missing local asset "${assetRef}".`));
        }
      }
    }
    if (name === 'code') {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_code_element_disallowed', 'p0', `Code element "${id}" is not allowed for Stage B JavaScript. Move source JS into bricks-result.json.page_settings.customScriptsBodyFooter so Pixflow saves it as Bricks page settings.`));
    }
    if (name === 'svg') {
      if (firstString(settings.source) === 'code' || firstString(settings.code)) {
        if (!isStageBSvgArtworkCodeElement(settings)) {
          errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_svg_raw_code_source', 'p0', `SVG element "${id}" uses raw code. Use source "iconSet" plus a Pixflow icon placeholder for icons, or mark non-icon source artwork with data-pixflow-svg-role="artwork".`));
        }
      }
      if (firstString(settings.source) === 'iconSet') {
        const svgIconUsages = collectStageBIconUsages(settings.iconSet, `Element "${id}" iconSet`, name);
        if (svgIconUsages.length === 0) {
          errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_svg_icon_set_missing_icon', 'p0', `SVG element "${id}" uses source iconSet but is missing settings.iconSet.`));
        }
      }
    }
  }

  for (const element of content) {
    if (!element || typeof element !== 'object') continue;
    const id = firstString(element.id);
    const parent = element.parent === 0 || element.parent === '0' ? '' : firstString(element.parent);
    if (parent && !ids.has(parent)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_parent_missing', 'p0', `Element "${id}" references missing parent "${parent}".`));
    }
    const children = Array.isArray(element.children) ? element.children : [];
    for (const child of children) {
      const childId = firstString(child);
      if (childId && !ids.has(childId)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_child_missing', 'p0', `Element "${id}" references missing child "${childId}".`));
      }
    }
  }

  const requireTopLevelSection = options.requireTopLevelSection !== false;
  if (requireTopLevelSection && topLevelSectionCount <= 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_no_top_level_sections', 'p0', 'Payload must contain at least one top-level section.'));
  }
  if (options.requirePageH1 === true && headingTagCounts.h1 <= 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_h1_missing', 'p0', 'Page content must contain at least one heading element with settings.tag "h1".'));
  }
  const placeholderIconUsages = iconUsages.filter((usage) => usage.placeholder);
  const fontIconUsages = iconUsages.filter((usage) => usage.fontIcon);
  const fontAwesomeIconUsages = iconUsages.filter((usage) => usage.fontAwesome);
  const rawSvgIconUsages = iconUsages.filter((usage) => usage.rawSvg);
  const sourceIconEvidenceCount = Number(iconSystem?.sourceIconCount || iconSystem?.source_icon_count || iconSystem?.detectedIconCount || 0);
  if (options.skipSourceIconUsageCheck !== true && sourceIconEvidenceCount > 0 && expectedIconCount > 0 && actionElementCount > 0 && iconUsages.length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_source_icons_not_used', 'p1', 'stage-b-icon-system.json detected source/action icons, but the Bricks payload does not use any icon controls. Preserve CTA/action/card/proof affordances with Pixflow Tabler SVG icons.'));
  }
  if (placeholderIconUsages.length > 0 && expectedIconCount === 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_icon_placeholder_without_sidecar', 'p0', 'Payload uses pixflow:<set>:<icon> placeholders, but stage_b_icon_system is missing or empty. Copy stage-b-icon-system.json into bricks-result.json.stage_b_icon_system.'));
  }
  for (const usage of placeholderIconUsages) {
    if (!stageBIconSystemContainsPlaceholder(iconSystem, usage.icon)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_icon_placeholder_not_declared', 'p0', `${usage.owner} uses icon placeholder "${usage.icon}", but it is not declared in stage_b_icon_system.`));
    }
  }
  for (const usage of fontAwesomeIconUsages.slice(0, 8)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_font_awesome_icon_used', 'p1', `${usage.owner} uses Bricks Font Awesome icon "${usage.icon}". Use Pixflow-installed Tabler SVG icons for Stage B page icons.`));
  }
  for (const usage of fontIconUsages.filter((usage) => !usage.fontAwesome).slice(0, 8)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_font_icon_used', 'p2', `${usage.owner} uses font icon "${usage.icon}". Prefer Pixflow Tabler SVG icons from stage-b-icon-system.json for source/action affordances.`));
  }
  for (const usage of rawSvgIconUsages.slice(0, 8)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_raw_svg_icon_markup', 'p0', `${usage.owner} contains raw SVG icon markup. Use a Pixflow Tabler SVG icon placeholder instead.`));
  }

  return {
    errors,
    warnings,
    topLevelSectionCount,
    supportedElementCount,
    headingTagCounts,
    iconUsageCount: iconUsages.length,
    iconPlaceholderCount: placeholderIconUsages.length,
  };
}

const STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_SETTINGS = {
  pixflowJsLibraryGsap: 'gsap',
  pixflowJsLibraryGsapScrollTrigger: 'gsap-scrolltrigger',
  pixflowJsLibraryThree: 'three',
  pixflowJsLibraryD3: 'd3',
  pixflowJsLibraryP5: 'p5',
};

const STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_ALIASES = {
  gsap: 'gsap',
  'gsap-core': 'gsap',
  gsapcore: 'gsap',
  greensock: 'gsap',
  scrolltrigger: 'gsap-scrolltrigger',
  'gsap-scrolltrigger': 'gsap-scrolltrigger',
  'gsap-scroll-trigger': 'gsap-scrolltrigger',
  gsapscrolltrigger: 'gsap-scrolltrigger',
  three: 'three',
  threejs: 'three',
  'three-js': 'three',
  d3: 'd3',
  d3js: 'd3',
  'd3-js': 'd3',
  p5: 'p5',
  p5js: 'p5',
  'p5-js': 'p5',
};

function normalizeStageBScriptLibraryIds(value) {
  const raw = [];
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    raw.push(...value.split(/[\s,|]+/));
  } else if (Array.isArray(value)) {
    value.forEach((entry) => raw.push(...normalizeStageBScriptLibraryIds(entry)));
  } else if (value && typeof value === 'object') {
    if (value.libraries !== undefined) {
      raw.push(...normalizeStageBScriptLibraryIds(value.libraries));
    }
    for (const [key, entry] of Object.entries(value)) {
      if (key === 'libraries') continue;
      if (STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_SETTINGS[key]) {
        if (isTruthySettingValue(entry)) raw.push(STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_SETTINGS[key]);
        continue;
      }
      if (isTruthySettingValue(entry)) raw.push(key);
    }
  }

  const normalized = [];
  for (const entry of raw) {
    const key = String(entry || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[_\s]+/g, '-');
    const id = STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_ALIASES[key] || '';
    if (!id) continue;
    normalized.push(id);
    if (id === 'gsap-scrolltrigger') normalized.push('gsap');
  }

  return ['gsap', 'gsap-scrolltrigger', 'three', 'd3', 'p5'].filter((id) => normalized.includes(id));
}

function isTruthySettingValue(value) {
  if (typeof value === 'boolean') return value;
  if (typeof value === 'number') return value !== 0;
  const normalized = String(value ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();
  return !['', '0', 'false', 'no', 'off', 'null'].includes(normalized);
}

function detectStageBScriptLibraryUsage(value) {
  const ids = [];
  const visit = (entry) => {
    if (typeof entry === 'string') {
      if (/\bwindow\.gsap\b|\bgsap\s*\./i.test(entry)) ids.push('gsap');
      if (/\bScrollTrigger\b|scrolltrigger|scroll-trigger/i.test(entry)) ids.push('gsap-scrolltrigger');
      if (/\bwindow\.THREE\b|\bnew\s+THREE\.|\bTHREE\./.test(entry)) ids.push('three');
      if (/\bwindow\.d3\b|\bd3\s*\./i.test(entry)) ids.push('d3');
      if (/\bwindow\.p5\b|\bnew\s+p5\s*\(|\bp5\s*\./i.test(entry)) ids.push('p5');
      return;
    }
    if (Array.isArray(entry)) {
      entry.forEach(visit);
      return;
    }
    if (entry && typeof entry === 'object') {
      Object.values(entry).forEach(visit);
    }
  };
  visit(value);
  return normalizeStageBScriptLibraryIds(ids);
}

function inspectStageBPageSettings(pageSettings, result = {}) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const settings = objectValue(pageSettings);
  const allowedKeys = new Set([
    'customCss',
    'customScriptsHeader',
    'customScriptsBodyHeader',
    'customScriptsBodyFooter',
    'pixflowScriptFragments',
    'headerDisabled',
    'footerDisabled',
    ...Object.keys(STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_SETTINGS),
  ]);
  const declaredLibraries = normalizeStageBScriptLibraryIds([
    result.stage_b_script_libraries,
    result.stageBScriptLibraries,
    result.script_libraries,
    result.scriptLibraries,
    settings,
    settings.pixflowJsLibraries,
    settings.pixflow_js_libraries,
  ]);
  const usedLibraries = detectStageBScriptLibraryUsage(settings);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(settings)) {
    if (!allowedKeys.has(key)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_unknown_key', 'p1', `Page settings include "${key}". Keep Stage B page settings to Bricks custom CSS/script fields and Pixflow JS library toggles.`));
      continue;
    }
    if (key === 'pixflowScriptFragments') {
      const fragments = arrayValue(value);
      if (!Array.isArray(value) || fragments.some((fragment) => (
        !firstString(fragment?.id)
        || !firstString(fragment?.code)
        || firstString(fragment?.placement) !== 'bodyFooter'
      ))) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_script_fragments_invalid', 'p0', 'pixflowScriptFragments must contain identified bodyFooter code fragments.'));
      }
      continue;
    }
    if (STAGE_B_SCRIPT_LIBRARY_SETTINGS[key]) {
      if (!['string', 'boolean', 'number'].includes(typeof value)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_value_invalid', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" must be a checkbox scalar value.`));
      }
      continue;
    }
    if (key === 'headerDisabled' || key === 'footerDisabled') {
      if (!['string', 'boolean', 'number'].includes(typeof value)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_value_invalid', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" must be a checkbox scalar value.`));
      }
      continue;
    }
    if (typeof value !== 'string') {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_value_invalid', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" must be a string.`));
      continue;
    }
    if (key === 'customCss') {
      if (/@import\b|@font-face\b|fonts\.googleapis\.com|fonts\.gstatic\.com/i.test(value)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_font_import', 'p0', 'Page customCss must not import fonts. Use stage-b-font-system.json and Pixflow font installation.'));
      }
      if (/<script\b|https?:\/\/|cdn\./i.test(value)) {
        errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_settings_css_external_script', 'p0', 'Page customCss must not load scripts or external assets. Use Pixflow page-scoped JS library toggles and page scripts.'));
      }
      continue;
    }
    if (value.trim() && !/<script\b[\s\S]*<\/script>/i.test(value)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_script_without_tag', 'p1', `Page setting "${key}" should include a complete <script>...</script> block because Bricks prints page scripts as raw page settings.`));
    }
    if (/fonts\.googleapis\.com|fonts\.gstatic\.com|@font-face|document\.createElement\(['"]link['"]\)/i.test(value)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_script_font_import', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" must not load fonts. Use stage-b-font-system.json and Pixflow's Bricks Google Font installer.`));
    }
    if (/https?:\/\/|cdn\.|unpkg\.com|jsdelivr\.net|cdnjs\.cloudflare\.com|document\.createElement\(['"]script['"]\)|import\s*\(/i.test(value)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_script_external_library', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" must not load external JavaScript. Use Pixflow page-scoped JS library toggles for supported libraries.`));
    }
    if (/<svg\b/i.test(value)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_page_script_raw_svg_icon', 'p0', `Page setting "${key}" contains raw SVG markup. Use stage-b-icon-system.json and Pixflow's SVG icon installer.`));
    }
  }
  for (const libraryId of usedLibraries) {
    if (!declaredLibraries.includes(libraryId)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_script_library_not_declared', 'p1', `Page scripts reference ${libraryId}, but stage_b_script_libraries and Pixflow page-setting toggles do not declare it.`));
    }
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

export function inspectPixflowStageBPageFoundationContract(themeStylePayload) {
  const payload = objectValue(themeStylePayload);
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  if (firstString(payload.mode) !== 'page_foundation') return { errors, warnings };
  const expected = {
    schema: 'pixflow.html_to_bricks.page_foundation.v1',
    version: 1,
    owner: 'pixflow_html_to_bricks',
    scope: 'current_page',
  };
  for (const [field, value] of Object.entries(expected)) {
    if (payload[field] !== value) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        `stage_b_page_foundation_invalid_${field}`,
        'p0',
        `Page-foundation ${field} must be ${JSON.stringify(value)}; received ${JSON.stringify(payload[field])}.`,
      ));
    }
  }
  const settings = objectValue(payload.settings);
  const stylesheet = firstString(objectValue(settings.css).stylesheet);
  if (!stylesheet || !Object.keys(settings).includes('conditions')) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_page_foundation_incomplete_settings',
      'p0',
      'Page-foundation settings must include an exact-page condition and a compatibility stylesheet.',
    ));
  }
  const templateOwnership = objectValue(payload.templateOwnership);
  const nativeGlobalScopeSafe = payload.nativeGlobalScopeSafe === true;
  const nativeGroups = Object.keys(settings).filter((group) => !['conditions', 'css'].includes(group));
  if (nativeGlobalScopeSafe) {
    if (templateOwnership.header !== 'source_owned' || templateOwnership.footer !== 'source_owned') {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_page_foundation_native_scope_without_templates',
        'p0',
        'Native page-wide Theme Style groups require source-owned header and footer output.',
      ));
    }
  } else {
    if (nativeGroups.length > 0) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_page_foundation_unsafe_native_scope',
        'p0',
        `Content-only page foundation contains globally applied native group(s): ${nativeGroups.join(', ')}.`,
      ));
    }
    if (!stylesheet.includes('#brx-content.pixflow-generated-page')
      || /(?:^|[},])\s*(?::root|html|body)\b/im.test(stylesheet)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_page_foundation_stylesheet_unscoped',
        'p0',
        'Content-only page-foundation CSS must be rooted at #brx-content.pixflow-generated-page and must not target the destination document directly.',
      ));
    }
  }
  const invalidDestinations = arrayValue(payload?.ownership?.declarations).filter((item) => (
    !['theme_style_native_control', 'theme_style_stylesheet'].includes(firstString(item?.destination))
  ));
  if (invalidDestinations.length > 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_page_foundation_invalid_ownership_destination',
      'p0',
      `${invalidDestinations.length} page-foundation declaration(s) have no valid Theme Style destination.`,
    ));
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function inspectStageBRouteContractQa({ result, content, headerContent, footerContent, globalClasses, pageSettings, routeContract, routeContextReport, colorSystem, themeStyleContract }) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const allElements = [...arrayValue(content), ...arrayValue(headerContent), ...arrayValue(footerContent)];
  const payloadText = JSON.stringify({
    content: allElements,
    globalClasses,
    pageSettings,
    stage_b_theme_style_payload: result?.stage_b_theme_style_payload || result?.stageBThemeStylePayload,
  });
  const allowedUtilities = new Set(stringArrayFromUnknown(routeContract?.variableAuthority?.allowedUtilityClasses)
    .concat(stringArrayFromUnknown(routeContextReport?.allowlists?.utilityClasses)));
  const generatedClassNames = arrayValue(globalClasses).map((classItem) => firstString(classItem?.name)).filter(Boolean);
  const generatedClassNameSet = new Set(generatedClassNames);
  const duplicatedUtilities = [...allowedUtilities].filter((className) => generatedClassNameSet.has(className));
  for (const className of duplicatedUtilities) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_route_utility_class_duplicated',
      'p0',
      `Allowlisted route utility class "${className}" was generated as a Bricks global class. Preserve framework utilities as literal element classes instead of duplicating them.`
    ));
  }
  if (allowedUtilities.size > 0) {
    const attributeClassText = collectStageBElementLiteralClassAttributes(allElements).join(' ');
    const missingLiteralUtilities = [...allowedUtilities].filter((className) => payloadText.includes(className) && !attributeClassText.split(/\s+/).includes(className));
    for (const className of missingLiteralUtilities) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_route_utility_class_not_literal',
        'p1',
        `Allowlisted route utility class "${className}" appears in the payload but is not preserved as a literal element class attribute.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const classNameCounts = generatedClassNames.reduce((counts, name) => {
    counts[name] = (counts[name] || 0) + 1;
    return counts;
  }, {});
  for (const [name, count] of Object.entries(classNameCounts)) {
    if (count > 1) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_global_class_name_duplicate',
        'p0',
        `Global class name "${name}" is emitted ${count} times. Bricks Class Manager names must be unique; reuse the existing id or follow the recorded ownership-plan conflict resolution.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const aliases = objectValue(colorSystem?.tokenAliases);
  const externalColorSourceVariables = new Set(arrayValue(colorSystem?.variables)
    .filter((variable) => variable?.external === true || variable?.create === false)
    .map((variable) => firstString(variable?.sourceCssVariable))
    .filter(Boolean));
  const sourceColorVariables = Object.keys(aliases).filter((name) => /^--[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(name));
  for (const sourceVariable of sourceColorVariables) {
    const targetVariable = firstString(aliases[sourceVariable]);
    if (!targetVariable || targetVariable === sourceVariable) {
      if (externalColorSourceVariables.has(sourceVariable)) {
        continue;
      }
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_color_alias_unresolved',
        'p1',
        `Color source variable "${sourceVariable}" has no effective tokenAliases mapping in stage-b-color-system.json.`
      ));
      continue;
    }
    if (doesStageBPayloadReferenceCssVariable(payloadText, sourceVariable)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_source_color_variable_leaked',
        'p0',
        `Source-file colour variable "${sourceVariable}" still appears in the Bricks result. Use stage-b-color-system.json tokenAliases target "${targetVariable}".`
      ));
    }
  }

  const sourceSlugVariables = uniqueStrings([...payloadText.matchAll(/--[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*-html-[a-z0-9-]+/gi)].map((match) => match[0]));
  for (const variable of sourceSlugVariables.slice(0, 12)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_file_variable_slug',
      'p0',
      `Source-file slug variable "${variable}" remains in the Bricks result. Map it to a live route variable or a generated project-scoped Stage B token.`
    ));
  }

  const externalColorVariables = new Set(arrayValue(colorSystem?.variables)
    .filter((variable) => variable?.external === true || variable?.create === false)
    .map((variable) => firstString(variable?.cssVariable))
    .filter(Boolean));
  for (const variable of arrayValue(colorSystem?.variables)) {
    const cssVariable = firstString(variable?.cssVariable);
    if (!cssVariable) continue;
    if (externalColorVariables.has(cssVariable) && variable.create !== false) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_external_color_variable_marked_create',
        'p0',
        `Live route colour variable "${cssVariable}" is external but is not marked create:false in stage-b-color-system.json.`
      ));
    }
  }
  const colorAuthority = objectValue(colorSystem?.colorAuthority);
  if (firstString(colorAuthority.status) === 'available') {
    const authorityMode = firstString(colorAuthority.mode);
    if (!authorityMode || authorityMode === 'generated_project_palette') {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_color_authority_too_generic',
        'p1',
        'Live route context is available, but stage-b-color-system.json colorAuthority did not select a route-specific color mode.'
      ));
    }
  }

  const themeStylePayload = objectValue(result?.stage_b_theme_style_payload || result?.stageBThemeStylePayload);
  const themeStyleSettings = objectValue(themeStylePayload.settings);
  const themeStyleMode = firstString(themeStylePayload.mode);
  const contractMode = firstString(themeStyleContract?.mode);
  const pageFoundationIssues = inspectPixflowStageBPageFoundationContract(themeStylePayload);
  errors.push(...pageFoundationIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...pageFoundationIssues.warnings);
  if (themeStyleMode === 'disabled' && Object.keys(themeStyleSettings).length > 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_theme_style_disabled_but_populated',
      'p0',
      'stage_b_theme_style_payload.mode is disabled but settings are populated. Pre-Stage B class-owned styling must not create page-scoped Bricks Theme Styles.'
    ));
  }
  if (/prototype_bricks|html_baseline|class_owned/i.test(contractMode)
    && Object.keys(themeStyleSettings).length > 0
    && themeStyleMode !== 'page_foundation') {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_theme_style_drift',
      'p1',
      'Theme Style payload contains settings while the route contract expects class-owned/source-owned styling. Confirm this is deliberate and documented.'
    ));
  }

  const customCssIssues = inspectStageBRouteCustomCssMisuse(globalClasses, pageSettings);
  errors.push(...customCssIssues.errors);
  warnings.push(...customCssIssues.warnings);

  const variableAuthority = objectValue(routeContract?.variableAuthority);
  if (firstString(variableAuthority.mode) === 'live_route_context') {
    const rawFallbacks = collectStageBRawRouteFallbacks({ allElements, globalClasses, pageSettings, allowedCssVariables: variableAuthority.allowedCssVariables });
    const recordedFallbacks = collectStageBRecordedFallbackEvidence(result);
    if (rawFallbacks.length > 0 && recordedFallbacks.length === 0) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_route_literal_fallbacks_unrecorded',
        'p1',
        `Route context is available, but ${rawFallbacks.length} raw px/rem fallback value(s) remain without fallback evidence in the result diagnostics/report. Record why each fallback could not use a live route token.`
      ));
    }
  }

  return { errors, warnings };
}

function collectStageBElementLiteralClassAttributes(elements) {
  const values = [];
  const visit = (value) => {
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      value.forEach(visit);
      return;
    }
    for (const attribute of arrayValue(objectValue(value.settings)._attributes)) {
      if (firstString(attribute?.name).toLowerCase() === 'class') {
        values.push(firstString(attribute?.value));
      }
    }
    for (const child of Object.values(value)) {
      if (child && typeof child === 'object') visit(child);
    }
  };
  visit(elements);
  return values.filter(Boolean);
}

function doesStageBPayloadReferenceCssVariable(payloadText, cssVariable) {
  const variable = firstString(cssVariable);
  if (!/^--[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(variable)) {
    return false;
  }
  const escaped = escapeRegExp(variable);
  return new RegExp(`var\\(\\s*${escaped}(?:\\s*[,\\)])`, 'i').test(payloadText)
    || new RegExp(`(^|[\\s{;,])${escaped}\\s*:`, 'im').test(payloadText);
}

function inspectStageBRouteCustomCssMisuse(globalClasses, pageSettings) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const entries = [
    ...arrayValue(globalClasses).map((classItem) => ({
      kind: 'global_class',
      name: firstString(classItem?.name, classItem?.id),
      owner: `Global class "${firstString(classItem?.name, classItem?.id)}"`,
      css: firstString(objectValue(classItem?.settings)._cssCustom),
    })),
    {
      kind: 'page_settings',
      owner: 'Page settings customCss',
      css: firstString(objectValue(pageSettings).customCss),
    },
  ];
  for (const entry of entries) {
    if (!entry.css) continue;
    const rootVariableDeclarations = countStageBRootCssVariableDeclarations(entry.css);
    // `pixflow-inline-*` classes are compiler-owned per-node custom-property
    // buckets (for example a decorative shimmer or media tint). They are
    // deliberately scoped to %root% and must not be treated as page-wide
    // route-token buckets by the Stage B route misuse check.
    const inlineStyleBucket = entry.kind === 'global_class'
      && /^pixflow-inline-[a-f0-9]+$/i.test(firstString(entry.name));
    if (rootVariableDeclarations >= 3 && !inlineStyleBucket) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_custom_css_token_bucket',
        'p0',
        `${entry.owner} declares ${rootVariableDeclarations} CSS custom properties. Route tokens and Stage B colours must live in route context/stage-b-color-system, not token bucket CSS.`
      ));
    }
    const routineProperties = collectStageBRoutineRootCustomCssProperties(entry.css)
      .filter((property) => !['display'].includes(property));
    if (entry.kind === 'page_settings' && routineProperties.length >= 5) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_custom_css_routine_property_bulk',
        'p1',
        `${entry.owner} keeps routine Bricks-supported declarations in _cssCustom/customCss (${routineProperties.slice(0, 8).join(', ')}). Move supported layout/spacing/type/background/border/radius/media properties to Bricks settings.`
      ));
    }
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function collectStageBRawRouteFallbacks({ allElements, globalClasses, pageSettings, allowedCssVariables }) {
  const allowed = new Set(stringArrayFromUnknown(allowedCssVariables));
  const values = [];
  const visit = (value, pathName = '') => {
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      if (
        /(?:^|\s)-?\d*\.?\d+(?:px|rem)\b/i.test(value)
        && !/^var\(/i.test(value.trim())
        && ![...allowed].some((name) => value.includes(name))
        && /(?:padding|margin|gap|width|height|radius|font-size|line-height|top|right|bottom|left|inset|border)/i.test(pathName)
      ) {
        values.push({ path: pathName, value });
      }
      return;
    }
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      value.forEach((item, index) => visit(item, `${pathName}.${index}`));
      return;
    }
    for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(value)) {
      visit(child, pathName ? `${pathName}.${key}` : key);
    }
  };
  visit({ allElements, globalClasses, pageSettings }, 'result');
  return values;
}

function collectStageBRecordedFallbackEvidence(result) {
  const diagnostics = objectValue(result?.diagnostics);
  const routeTokenNormalization = objectValue(diagnostics.routeTokenNormalization || diagnostics.route_token_normalization);
  return [
    ...arrayValue(result?.literalFallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(result?.literal_fallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(result?.stage_b_route_fallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(result?.stageBRouteFallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(diagnostics.literalFallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(diagnostics.literal_fallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(diagnostics.routeTokenFallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(diagnostics.route_token_fallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(routeTokenNormalization.routeTokenFallbacks),
    ...arrayValue(routeTokenNormalization.route_token_fallbacks),
  ];
}

function stageBColorSystemRequiresPageBackgroundCss(colorSystem, pageSettings) {
  const variables = arrayValue(objectValue(colorSystem).variables);
  const hasBackgroundToken = variables.some((item) => {
    const tokens = [
      firstString(item?.cssVariable, item?.name),
      firstString(item?.sourceCssVariable),
      firstString(item?.sourceName),
    ].filter(Boolean).map((token) => token.toLowerCase().replace(/^--/, ''));
    return tokens.some((token) => ['bg', 'background', 'surface'].includes(token));
  });
  if (!hasBackgroundToken) {
    return false;
  }
  const css = firstString(objectValue(pageSettings).customCss).toLowerCase();
  if (!css) {
    return true;
  }
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks pages inherit the WordPress theme body unless the
  // handoff carries the Stage A html/body backdrop into page custom CSS.
  const tokenAliases = objectValue(colorSystem.tokenAliases);
  const backgroundTokens = ['--bg', '--background', '--surface']
    .flatMap((token) => [token, firstString(tokenAliases[token])])
    .filter(Boolean)
    .map((token) => escapeRegExp(token));
  return !(/(?:html|body|main|#brx-content|\.brx-body|\.bricks-site-wrapper)/i.test(css)
    && /background/i.test(css)
    && new RegExp(`var\\(\\s*(?:${backgroundTokens.join('|')})\\b`, 'i').test(css));
}

function collectStageBIconUsages(value, owner, elementName = '', pathLabel = 'settings') {
  const usages = [];
  collectStageBIconUsagesFromValue(value, owner, elementName, pathLabel, usages);
  return usages;
}

function collectStageBIconUsagesFromValue(value, owner, elementName, pathLabel, usages) {
  if (!value) return;
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    if (/<svg\b/i.test(value)) {
      usages.push({ owner, path: pathLabel, icon: '', library: '', rawSvg: true, fontIcon: false, fontAwesome: false, placeholder: false });
    }
    return;
  }
  if (typeof value !== 'object') return;
  if (Array.isArray(value)) {
    value.forEach((item, index) => collectStageBIconUsagesFromValue(item, owner, elementName, `${pathLabel}[${index}]`, usages));
    return;
  }

  const usage = describeStageBIconSetting(value, owner, elementName, pathLabel);
  if (usage) {
    usages.push(usage);
  }

  for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(value)) {
    if (usage && ['icon', 'pixflowIcon', 'library', 'svg'].includes(key)) {
      continue;
    }
    collectStageBIconUsagesFromValue(child, owner, elementName, `${pathLabel}.${key}`, usages);
  }
}

function describeStageBIconSetting(value, owner, elementName, pathLabel) {
  const icon = firstString(value.icon, value.pixflowIcon);
  const library = firstString(value.library);
  const svg = objectValue(value.svg);
  const hasSvg = Boolean(firstString(svg.id, svg.url, svg.filename));
  const hasIconControlShape = Boolean(icon || library || hasSvg || pathLabel.endsWith('.iconSet'));
  if (!hasIconControlShape) {
    return null;
  }
  const placeholder = isStageBIconPlaceholder(icon);
  const fontAwesome = /font[\s_-]*awesome|^fa[brs]?$/i.test(library)
    || /\bfa[brs]?\s+fa-[a-z0-9-]+/i.test(icon)
    || /^fa-[a-z0-9-]+/i.test(icon);
  const fontIcon = Boolean(icon && !placeholder && !hasSvg);
  return {
    owner,
    elementName,
    path: pathLabel,
    icon,
    library,
    placeholder,
    fontAwesome,
    fontIcon,
    rawSvg: false,
    svg: hasSvg,
  };
}

function isStageBIconPlaceholder(value) {
  return /^pixflow:[a-z0-9-]+:[a-z0-9-]+$/i.test(firstString(value).trim());
}

function stageBIconSystemContainsPlaceholder(iconSystem, placeholder) {
  const target = firstString(placeholder).trim().toLowerCase();
  if (!target) return false;
  const summary = summarizeStageBIconSystem(iconSystem);
  if (summary.iconCount === 0) return false;
  const icons = Array.isArray(iconSystem?.icons)
    ? iconSystem.icons
    : (Array.isArray(iconSystem?.iconSets)
      ? iconSystem.iconSets.flatMap((set) => Array.isArray(set?.icons)
        ? set.icons.map((icon) => ({ ...icon, setId: firstString(icon?.setId, set?.setId) }))
        : [])
      : []);
  return icons.some((icon) => firstString(icon?.placeholder, buildStageBIconPlaceholder(icon?.setId, icon?.id)).toLowerCase() === target);
}

function inspectStageBBricksSettings(settings, owner) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  if (!settings || typeof settings !== 'object' || Array.isArray(settings)) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }

  for (const rawKey of [
    'display',
    'direction',
    'flexWrap',
    'justifyContent',
    'alignItems',
    'rowGap',
    'columnGap',
    'gridTemplateColumns',
    'gridGap',
    'padding',
    'margin',
    'background',
    'border',
    'width',
    'height',
  ]) {
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, rawKey)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_unprefixed_style_key', 'p0', `${owner} uses unprefixed Bricks style key "${rawKey}".`));
    }
  }

  for (const typographyKey of [
    'color',
    'fontSize',
    'font-size',
    'fontFamily',
    'font-family',
    'fontWeight',
    'font-weight',
    'lineHeight',
    'line-height',
    'letterSpacing',
    'letter-spacing',
    'textAlign',
    'text-align',
  ]) {
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, typographyKey)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_root_typography_key', 'p0', `${owner} uses typography key "${typographyKey}" at settings root; put it under _typography.`));
    }
  }

  const flexKeys = ['_direction', '_flexDirection', '_flexWrap'];
  const hasFlexOnlyKey = flexKeys.some((key) => firstString(settings[key]));
  const display = firstString(settings._display).toLowerCase();
  // A responsive control may intentionally be hidden at the base breakpoint
  // while its suffixed _display setting enables flex on smaller screens. In
  // that shape the base flex-direction is dormant, not ownerless.
  if (hasFlexOnlyKey && !['flex', 'inline-flex', 'none'].includes(display)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_flex_controls_without_display', 'p0', `${owner} uses flex controls but does not set _display to flex or inline-flex on the same element/class.`));
  }
  const gridKeys = ['_gridTemplateColumns', '_gridTemplateRows', '_justifyItemsGrid', '_alignItemsGrid', '_justifyContentGrid', '_alignContentGrid'];
  const hasGridOnlyKey = gridKeys.some((key) => firstString(settings[key]));
  if (hasGridOnlyKey && !['grid', 'inline-grid', 'none'].includes(display)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_grid_controls_without_display', 'p0', `${owner} uses grid controls but does not set _display to grid on the same element/class.`));
  }
  if (
    display === 'grid'
    && stageBGridColumnCountHint(firstString(settings._gridTemplateColumns)) > 1
    && !firstString(settings['_gridTemplateColumns:mobile_portrait'], settings['_gridTemplateColumns:tablet_portrait'])
  ) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_grid_responsive_columns_missing',
      'p0',
      `${owner} defines a multi-column grid but has no Bricks responsive _gridTemplateColumns override. Use Bricks responsive settings instead of relying only on _cssCustom media queries.`,
    ));
  }

  for (const scalarKey of ['_width', '_widthMin', '_widthMax', '_height', '_heightMin', '_heightMax', '_columnGap', '_rowGap', '_gridGap', '_aspectRatio', '_objectFit', '_objectPosition']) {
    if (settings[scalarKey] && typeof settings[scalarKey] === 'object' && !Array.isArray(settings[scalarKey])) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_scalar_unit_object', 'p0', `${owner} setting ${scalarKey} must be a scalar string, not a value/unit object.`));
    }
  }

  const typography = objectValue(settings._typography);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(typography)) {
    if (['color', 'background-color'].includes(key)) {
      continue;
    }
    if (value && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_typography_scalar_object', 'p0', `${owner} _typography.${key} must be a scalar string.`));
    }
  }
  const fontFamily = firstString(typography['font-family']);
  if (/^var\(/i.test(fontFamily)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_typography_font_family_var',
      'p0',
      `${owner} sets _typography.font-family to "${fontFamily}". Resolve Stage A font variables to the concrete family name supplied by stage-b-font-system.json so Bricks can map it to an installed custom font.`
    ));
  }

  const border = settings._border;
  if (border && typeof border === 'object' && !Array.isArray(border)) {
    for (const side of ['top', 'right', 'bottom', 'left']) {
      if (border[side] && typeof border[side] === 'object' && !Array.isArray(border[side])) {
        warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_nested_border_side', 'p1', `${owner} _border.${side} is nested. Prefer Bricks' flat border shape or scoped _cssCustom for one-side borders.`));
      }
    }
  }

  const customCss = firstString(settings._cssCustom);
  if (customCss) {
    if (/@import\b|@font-face\b|fonts\.googleapis\.com|fonts\.gstatic\.com/i.test(customCss)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_font_import_in_custom_css', 'p0', `${owner} imports or declares fonts in _cssCustom. Use stage-b-font-system.json and Pixflow's Bricks Google Font installer instead.`));
    }
    if (!/[{}]/.test(customCss)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_custom_css_declarations_only', 'p0', `${owner} _cssCustom must contain complete selector blocks, not bare declarations.`));
    }
    if (!/%root%/.test(customCss) && !/^\s*@(?:media|supports|container)\b/i.test(customCss)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_custom_css_without_root', 'p1', `${owner} _cssCustom should scope selectors with %root%.`));
    }
    const routineCustomCssProperties = collectStageBRoutineRootCustomCssProperties(customCss);
    const isNativeBricksFormFallbackCss = /\.form-group\b/.test(customCss)
      && /\.submit-button-wrapper\b/.test(customCss)
      && routineCustomCssProperties.some((property) => ['display', 'grid-template-columns', 'gap', 'column-gap', 'row-gap'].includes(property));
    const isSingleAxisGapCompatibilityCss = !firstString(settings._columnGap, settings._rowGap)
      && routineCustomCssProperties.length > 0
      && routineCustomCssProperties.every((property) => ['column-gap', 'row-gap'].includes(property));
    if (routineCustomCssProperties.length > 0 && !isNativeBricksFormFallbackCss && !isSingleAxisGapCompatibilityCss) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_custom_css_contains_supported_declarations',
        'p1',
        `${owner} _cssCustom contains Bricks-supported declarations (${routineCustomCssProperties.slice(0, 8).join(', ')}). Materialize static descendant/relationship targets as purpose-named classes, move layout/spacing/type/background/border/media properties into native Bricks settings, and leave only irreducible selectors/effects in _cssCustom.`
      ));
    }
  }

  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'customJs')) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_unknown_custom_js_setting', 'p0', `${owner} uses customJs, which is not a Bricks page/script setting.`));
  }
  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, 'templateType')) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_template_type_on_element', 'p0', `${owner} sets templateType on an element/settings object; template type belongs to a bricks_template post.`));
  }

  return { errors, warnings };
}

function collectStageBElementDirectStyleKeys(settings) {
  const styleKeys = new Set([
    '_cssCustom',
    '_display',
    '_direction',
    '_flexDirection',
    '_flexWrap',
    '_flexGrow',
    '_flexShrink',
    '_flexBasis',
    '_alignSelf',
    '_order',
    '_gridItemJustifySelf',
    '_alignItems',
    '_alignItemsGrid',
    '_justifyContent',
    '_justifyContentGrid',
    '_justifyItemsGrid',
    '_alignContentGrid',
    '_columnGap',
    '_rowGap',
    '_gridTemplateColumns',
    '_gridTemplateRows',
    '_background',
    '_typography',
    '_border',
    '_padding',
    '_margin',
    '_width',
    '_height',
    '_widthMin',
    '_widthMax',
    '_heightMin',
    '_heightMax',
    '_aspectRatio',
    '_objectFit',
    '_objectPosition',
    '_overflow',
    '_visibility',
    '_opacity',
    '_cursor',
    '_isolation',
    '_mixBlendMode',
    '_pointerEvents',
    '_perspective',
    '_perspectiveOrigin',
    '_scrollSnapType',
    '_scrollSnapAlign',
    '_scrollSnapStop',
    '_scrollMargin',
    '_cssFilters',
    '_position',
    '_top',
    '_right',
    '_bottom',
    '_left',
    '_zIndex',
    '_boxShadow',
    '_transform',
    '_transformOrigin',
    '_cssTransition',
    '_gradient',
  ]);
  const result = [];
  for (const key of Object.keys(objectValue(settings))) {
    const baseKey = key.split(':')[0];
    if (styleKeys.has(baseKey)) {
      result.push(key);
    }
  }
  return result;
}

function filterStageBDisallowedElementDirectStyleKeys(keys, options = {}) {
  const templateArea = firstString(options.templateArea).toLowerCase();
  const elementName = firstString(options.elementName).toLowerCase();
  if (options.strictClassOnlyStyles === true) {
    return keys;
  }
  if (options.allowUnclassedElementStyles === true) {
    // A converter-inserted Bricks wrapper may have no source-owned class.
    // Its native controls are preferable to inventing a global repair class.
    return [];
  }
  // The converter deliberately uses the native Bricks width control with an
  // exact `auto` value for intrinsic flex/row children. It is structural
  // layout metadata, not source CSS leaking into element-level styling.
  keys = filterStageBIntrinsicAutoWidthKeys(keys, options.settings);
  if (options.allowElementLayoutControls === true) {
    keys = keys.filter((key) => !isStageBElementNativeLayoutControlKey(String(key || '').split(':')[0]));
  }
  if (['header', 'footer'].includes(templateArea)) {
    return keys.filter((key) => {
      const baseKey = String(key || '').split(':')[0];
      return !isStageBTemplateLayoutDirectStyleKey(baseKey);
    });
  }
  if (elementName === 'block') {
    return keys.filter((key) => !isStageBBlockIntrinsicWidthDirectStyleKey(key));
  }
  if (elementName === 'section') {
    return keys.filter((key) => {
      const baseKey = String(key || '').split(':')[0];
      return !['_display', '_padding'].includes(baseKey);
    });
  }
  if (elementName === 'form') {
    return keys.filter((key) => {
      const baseKey = String(key || '').split(':')[0];
      return !isStageBFormRootLayoutDirectStyleKey(baseKey);
    });
  }
  return keys;
}

function isStageBElementNativeLayoutControlKey(key) {
  return new Set([
    '_display',
    '_direction',
    '_flexDirection',
    '_flexWrap',
    '_flexGrow',
    '_flexShrink',
    '_flexBasis',
    '_alignItems',
    '_alignItemsGrid',
    '_alignSelf',
    '_alignContent',
    '_justifyContent',
    '_justifyContentGrid',
    '_justifyItemsGrid',
    '_justifySelf',
    '_columnGap',
    '_rowGap',
    '_gap',
    '_gridGap',
    '_gridTemplateColumns',
    '_gridTemplateRows',
    '_gridColumn',
    '_gridRow',
    '_order',
    '_width',
    '_widthMin',
    '_widthMax',
    '_height',
    '_heightMin',
    '_heightMax',
    '_aspectRatio',
    '_overflow',
  ]).has(key);
}

function isStageBBlockIntrinsicWidthDirectStyleKey(key) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks block elements are full-width by default. The
  // baseline converter may set only _width:auto directly to preserve source
  // inline-flex/inline-grid wrappers while keeping all real styling in global
  // classes and Theme Styles.
  const keyString = String(key || '');
  return keyString === '_width';
}

function isStageBFormRootLayoutDirectStyleKey(key) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks native forms need root layout controls on the form
  // element itself because Bricks-generated field wrappers do not reliably
  // inherit grid/flex controls from global classes during baseline rendering.
  return new Set([
    '_display',
    '_direction',
    '_flexDirection',
    '_flexWrap',
    '_alignItems',
    '_alignItemsGrid',
    '_justifyContent',
    '_justifyContentGrid',
    '_justifyItemsGrid',
    '_alignContentGrid',
    '_columnGap',
    '_rowGap',
    '_gridTemplateColumns',
    '_gridTemplateRows',
  ]).has(key);
}

function isStageBTemplateLayoutDirectStyleKey(key) {
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks' base section selector can override equal-specificity
  // global classes. Keep exact source padding on semantic template section
  // roots alongside their structural controls so headers and footers do not
  // inherit generic page-section spacing.
  return new Set([
    '_display',
    '_direction',
    '_flexWrap',
    '_alignItems',
    '_alignItemsGrid',
    '_justifyContent',
    '_justifyContentGrid',
    '_justifyItemsGrid',
    '_alignContentGrid',
    '_columnGap',
    '_rowGap',
    '_gridTemplateColumns',
    '_gridTemplateRows',
    '_width',
    '_widthMin',
    '_widthMax',
    '_height',
    '_heightMin',
    '_heightMax',
    '_padding',
  ]).has(key);
}

function collectStageBRoutineRootCustomCssProperties(customCss) {
  const properties = [];
  const rules = extractStageBCssRuleSummaries(customCss);
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector);
    const isRootScoped = selectors.some((selector) => /%root%/i.test(selector));
    const isRootOnly = selectors.length > 0 && selectors.every((selector) => /^%root%\s*$/i.test(selector.trim()));
    const isPseudoElementOnly = selectors.length > 0 && selectors.every((selector) => (
      /::(?:before|after|marker|selection|backdrop|placeholder|file-selector-button)\b/i.test(selector)
    ));
    if (!isRootScoped || isPseudoElementOnly) {
      continue;
    }
    const isNativeStateOnly = selectors.some((selector) => (
      /^%root%:(?:hover|focus|focus-visible|focus-within|active|visited|disabled|checked)\s*$/i.test(selector.trim())
    ));
    for (const [property, value] of Object.entries(objectValue(rule.declarations))) {
      const mapsToNativeState = isNativeStateOnly && Object.keys(pickPixflowStageBStateDeclarations(
        mapPixflowCssDeclarationsToBricksSettings({ [property]: value }, { deriveResponsive: false }),
      )).length > 0;
      // Only plain %root% declarations are directly movable to the owning
      // Bricks class. Descendant, attribute-state, and generated-inner-markup
      // selectors need scoped CSS unless a dedicated target element/class is
      // actually materialized; treating them as routine owner declarations
      // caused repair passes to delete required responsive/interactivity CSS.
      if ((isRootOnly && isPixflowStageBMappableCssDeclaration(property, value)) || mapsToNativeState) {
        properties.push(property.toLowerCase());
      }
    }
  }
  return uniqueStrings(properties);
}

function inspectStageBLinkSetting(link, owner) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  if (!link || typeof link !== 'object' || Array.isArray(link)) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  const type = firstString(link.type);
  if (type === 'url') {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_link_type_url_invalid', 'p0', `${owner} uses link type "url"; use Bricks type "external" for plain URLs.`));
  }
  if (type === 'external' && !firstString(link.url)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_external_link_missing_url', 'p0', `${owner} external link is missing url.`));
  }
  if (type === 'internal' && !firstString(link.postId, link.post_id, link.url)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_internal_link_missing_target', 'p1', `${owner} internal link should include a postId target.`));
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function buildStageBGlobalClassMap(globalClasses) {
  const map = new Map();
  for (const item of Array.isArray(globalClasses) ? globalClasses : []) {
    if (!item || typeof item !== 'object' || Array.isArray(item)) continue;
    const id = firstString(item.id);
    const name = firstString(item.name);
    if (id) map.set(id, item);
    if (name) map.set(name, item);
  }
  return map;
}

function inspectStageBButtonNativeOptionContract(element, globalClassById) {
  const warnings = [];
  const id = firstString(element?.id);
  const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
  const classIds = Array.isArray(settings._cssGlobalClasses) ? settings._cssGlobalClasses : [];
  const globalClasses = classIds
    .map((classId) => globalClassById.get(firstString(classId)))
    .filter(Boolean);
  const classNames = globalClasses
    .map((globalClass) => firstString(globalClass?.name))
    .filter(Boolean);
  const classText = classNames.join(' ');
  const classesOwnVisualStyle = globalClasses.some((globalClass) => {
    const classSettings = objectValue(globalClass?.settings);
    const typography = objectValue(classSettings._typography);
    return Boolean(
      classSettings._background
      || classSettings._border
      || classSettings._boxShadow
      || typography.color
      || firstString(classSettings._cssCustom)
    );
  });

  if (!firstString(settings.style) && !classesOwnVisualStyle && /\b(?:btn|button|cta|action|primary|secondary|main|alt|light|dark|muted|info|success|warning|danger)\b/i.test(classText)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_button_native_style_missing',
      'p1',
      `Button element "${id}" uses a button/variant-like class (${classNames.join(', ')}) without settings.style. Use Bricks button style values first, then keep classes only for source-specific layout or visual exceptions.`
    ));
  }

  if (!firstString(settings.size)
    && !classesOwnVisualStyle
    && /\b(?:sm|small|md|medium|lg|large|xl|extra[-_ ]?large)\b/i.test(classText)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_button_native_size_missing',
      'p1',
      `Button element "${id}" uses a size-like class (${classNames.join(', ')}) without settings.size. Use Bricks button size values first so Theme Styles can own routine button sizing.`
    ));
  }

  return warnings;
}

function resolveStageBElementStyleSettings(element, globalClassById) {
  const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
  const resolved = {};
  const classIds = Array.isArray(settings._cssGlobalClasses) ? settings._cssGlobalClasses : [];
  for (const classId of classIds) {
    const classItem = globalClassById.get(firstString(classId));
    if (classItem) {
      mergePixflowBricksSettingsInto(resolved, objectValue(classItem.settings));
    }
  }
  mergePixflowBricksSettingsInto(resolved, settings);
  return resolved;
}

function inspectStageBTemplateSectionPaddingContract(templateContent, globalClasses, partLabel) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const content = Array.isArray(templateContent) ? templateContent : [];
  const globalClassById = buildStageBGlobalClassMap(globalClasses);
  const rootSections = content.filter((element) => (
    element
    && typeof element === 'object'
    && (
      firstString(element.name) === 'section'
      || ['header', 'nav'].includes(firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase())
    )
    && !firstString(element.parent)
  ));
  for (const root of rootSections) {
    if (!hasStageBTemplateSectionPaddingOverride(root, globalClassById)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue(
        `stage_b_${partLabel}_template_section_padding_uncontrolled`,
        'p0',
        `${capitalizeStageBLabel(partLabel)} top-level section "${describeStageBElementForIssue(root)}" must set source-accurate top/bottom padding on the element or a global class; otherwise page section theme-style padding can change the template height.`,
      ));
    }
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function hasStageBTemplateSectionPaddingOverride(element, globalClassById) {
  const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
  if (hasStageBTopBottomPadding(settings)) {
    return true;
  }
  const classIds = Array.isArray(settings._cssGlobalClasses) ? settings._cssGlobalClasses : [];
  for (const classId of classIds) {
    const classItem = globalClassById.get(firstString(classId));
    if (classItem && hasStageBTopBottomPadding(objectValue(classItem.settings))) {
      return true;
    }
  }
  return false;
}

function hasStageBTopBottomPadding(settings) {
  const padding = objectValue(settings?._padding);
  return firstString(padding.top) !== '' && firstString(padding.bottom) !== '';
}

function describeStageBElementForIssue(element) {
  const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
  return firstString(settings._cssId, element?.id, element?.name, 'unknown');
}

function capitalizeStageBLabel(value) {
  const label = firstString(value, 'template');
  return `${label.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}${label.slice(1)}`;
}

function stageBGridColumnCountHint(value) {
  const source = firstString(value).trim();
  if (!source) return 0;
  const repeatMatch = source.match(/\brepeat\(\s*(\d+)\s*,/i);
  if (repeatMatch) {
    return Number(repeatMatch[1]) || 1;
  }
  const tracks = [];
  let depth = 0;
  let current = '';
  for (const char of source) {
    if (char === '(') depth += 1;
    if (char === ')') depth = Math.max(0, depth - 1);
    if (/\s/.test(char) && depth === 0) {
      if (current.trim()) tracks.push(current.trim());
      current = '';
      continue;
    }
    current += char;
  }
  if (current.trim()) tracks.push(current.trim());
  return tracks.length || 1;
}

function inspectStageBHeaderLayoutContract(headerContent, headerSpec = {}, globalClasses = []) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const content = Array.isArray(headerContent) ? headerContent : [];
  const byId = new Map();
  const globalClassById = buildStageBGlobalClassMap(globalClasses);
  for (const element of content) {
    if (element && typeof element === 'object' && !Array.isArray(element)) {
      const id = firstString(element.id);
      if (id) byId.set(id, element);
    }
  }

  const rootSections = content.filter((element) => (
    element
    && typeof element === 'object'
    && (
      firstString(element.name) === 'section'
      || ['header', 'nav'].includes(firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase())
    )
    && !firstString(element.parent)
  ));
  const selectedSectionOdId = firstString(
    headerSpec.sourceSectionOdId,
    headerSpec.selectedSectionOdId,
    headerSpec.source_section_od_id,
    headerSpec.selected_section_od_id,
  );
  const matchesSelectedHeaderSection = (element) => {
    if (!selectedSectionOdId) return false;
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const attrValues = (Array.isArray(settings._attributes) ? settings._attributes : [])
      .map((attribute) => objectValue(attribute))
      .filter((attribute) => ['data-od-id', 'id'].includes(firstString(attribute.name)));
    return firstString(settings._cssId) === selectedSectionOdId
      || attrValues.some((attribute) => firstString(attribute.value) === selectedSectionOdId)
      || firstString(element?.id) === selectedSectionOdId;
  };
  const preferredHeaderRoot = rootSections.find((element) => (
    firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase() === 'header'
  )) || rootSections.find((element) => {
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const attributes = arrayValue(settings._attributes).map((attribute) => objectValue(attribute));
    return attributes.some((attribute) => (
      firstString(attribute.name).toLowerCase() === 'role'
      && firstString(attribute.value).toLowerCase() === 'banner'
    ));
  }) || rootSections.find((element) => firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase() === 'nav') || rootSections[0];

  const selectedHeaderRoots = selectedSectionOdId
    ? rootSections.filter(matchesSelectedHeaderSection)
    : [];
  let root = selectedSectionOdId
    ? selectedHeaderRoots.find((element) => firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase() === 'header')
      || selectedHeaderRoots.find((element) => firstString(element?.settings?.tag).toLowerCase() === 'nav')
      || selectedHeaderRoots[0]
    : preferredHeaderRoot;
  if (!root) {
    const issue = stageBIssue(
      selectedSectionOdId ? 'stage_b_header_selected_section_missing' : 'stage_b_header_root_section_missing',
      selectedSectionOdId && rootSections.length > 0 ? 'p2' : 'p0',
      selectedSectionOdId
        ? `Header payload must include the selected source header section "${selectedSectionOdId}" as a top-level section.`
        : 'Header payload must include one top-level section for the Bricks header template.',
    );
    // Pixflow-owned: model-refined handoffs sometimes preserve header content
    // but lose the old Stage A trace id. Treat that as a warning when a
    // top-level header section exists; still block truly empty/invalid headers.
    if (selectedSectionOdId && rootSections.length > 0) {
      warnings.push(issue);
      root = preferredHeaderRoot;
    } else {
      errors.push(issue);
      return { errors, warnings };
    }
  }

  for (const rootSection of rootSections.filter((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'section')) {
    if (!hasStageBTemplateSectionPaddingOverride(rootSection, globalClassById)) {
      // Pixflow-owned: header polish gaps should not block generated-page
      // handoff preparation when page content is otherwise valid. Surface them
      // for follow-up in the Bricks Agent instead.
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_header_template_section_padding_uncontrolled',
        'p2',
        `Header top-level section "${describeStageBElementForIssue(rootSection)}" must set source-accurate top/bottom padding on the element or a global class; otherwise Pixflow Framework page section padding can create blank header bands.`,
      ));
    }
  }

  const rootChildren = (Array.isArray(root.children) ? root.children : [])
    .map((id) => byId.get(firstString(id)))
    .filter(Boolean);
  const inner = rootChildren.find((element) => ['container', 'block', 'div'].includes(firstString(element.name)));
  if (!inner) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_inner_wrapper_missing', 'p0', 'Header section must contain a container or block inner wrapper.'));
    return { errors, warnings };
  }

  const innerId = firstString(inner.id);
  const innerSettings = resolveStageBElementStyleSettings(inner, globalClassById);
  const innerDisplay = firstString(innerSettings._display);
  const innerUsesGrid = innerDisplay === 'grid' && firstString(innerSettings._gridTemplateColumns, innerSettings._gridTemplateRows);
  const innerRequired = innerUsesGrid
    ? {
        _display: 'grid',
        _gridTemplateColumns: '',
        _alignItemsGrid: '',
        _columnGap: '',
        _rowGap: '',
      }
    : {
        _display: 'flex',
        _direction: 'row',
        _alignItems: '',
        _justifyContent: '',
        _columnGap: '',
        _rowGap: '',
      };
  for (const [key, expected] of Object.entries(innerRequired)) {
    const value = firstString(innerSettings[key]);
    if (!value || (expected && value !== expected)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_inner_layout_incomplete', 'p2', `Header inner wrapper "${innerId}" must set ${key}${expected ? ` to "${expected}"` : ''}.`));
    }
  }
  if (!firstString(
    innerSettings['_direction:mobile_portrait'],
    innerSettings['_direction:tablet_portrait'],
    innerSettings['_flexWrap:mobile_portrait'],
    innerSettings['_flexWrap:tablet_portrait'],
    innerSettings['_gridTemplateColumns:mobile_portrait'],
    innerSettings['_gridTemplateColumns:tablet_portrait'],
  )) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_inner_responsive_direction_missing', 'p1', `Header inner wrapper "${innerId}" must include a responsive _direction, _flexWrap, or grid-column override for narrow screens before final insertion.`));
  }

  const innerChildren = content.filter((element) => firstString(element?.parent) === innerId);
  const navMenu = innerChildren.find((element) => firstString(element?.name) === 'nav-menu');
  const semanticNav = innerChildren.find((element) => {
    if (firstString(objectValue(element?.settings).tag).toLowerCase() !== 'nav') return false;
    const childIds = arrayValue(element?.children).map((id) => firstString(id)).filter(Boolean);
    return childIds.filter((id) => ['text-link', 'button'].includes(firstString(byId.get(id)?.name))).length >= 2;
  });
  const innerClassText = [
    firstString(inner?.name),
    ...arrayValue(objectValue(inner?.settings)._cssGlobalClasses)
      .map((id) => firstString(globalClassById.get(firstString(id))?.name)),
  ].join(' ');
  const innerIsSourceNav = /\b(?:nav|menu)\b/i.test(innerClassText)
    && innerChildren.filter((element) => ['text-link', 'button', 'block', 'container', 'div'].includes(firstString(element?.name))).length >= 2
    && (innerUsesGrid || firstString(innerSettings._display) === 'flex');
  const nav = navMenu || semanticNav || innerChildren.find((element) => {
    if (!['block', 'container', 'div'].includes(firstString(element?.name))) return false;
    const childIds = Array.isArray(element.children) ? element.children : [];
    return childIds.some((id) => firstString(byId.get(firstString(id))?.name) === 'button');
  });
  if (!nav && !innerIsSourceNav) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_nav_block_missing', 'p2', 'Header inner wrapper must contain a Bricks nav-menu element or a fallback nav/action block with CTA button children.'));
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  if (!nav && innerIsSourceNav) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }

  if (firstString(nav.name) === 'nav-menu') {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  // A semantic source <nav> with multiple native Bricks link children is a
  // complete navigation block even when the CTA remains its sibling, matching
  // the accepted HTML structure instead of forcing an artificial action row.
  if (nav === semanticNav) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }

  const navId = firstString(nav.id);
  const navSettings = resolveStageBElementStyleSettings(nav, globalClassById);
  const navRequired = {
    _display: 'flex',
    _direction: 'row',
    // Source-accurate action rows may intentionally stay nowrap when their nav
    // and CTA children have explicit narrow-screen visibility controls.
    _flexWrap: '',
    _alignItems: '',
    _justifyContent: '',
    _columnGap: '',
    _rowGap: '',
  };
  for (const [key, expected] of Object.entries(navRequired)) {
    const value = firstString(navSettings[key]);
    if (!value || (expected && value !== expected)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_header_nav_layout_incomplete', 'p2', `Header nav/action block "${navId}" must set ${key}${expected ? ` to "${expected}"` : ''}.`));
    }
  }

  return { errors, warnings };
}

function inspectStageBElementAttributes(settings, elementId) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(settings, '_attributes')) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  if (!Array.isArray(settings._attributes)) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attributes_invalid', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" _attributes must be an array.`));
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  settings._attributes.forEach((attribute, index) => {
    if (!attribute || typeof attribute !== 'object' || Array.isArray(attribute)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_invalid', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" _attributes[${index}] must be an object.`));
      return;
    }
    const id = firstString(attribute.id);
    const name = firstString(attribute.name);
    if (!id || !name) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_missing_identity', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" _attributes[${index}] requires id and name.`));
    }
    if (name && !isPixflowStageBAllowedHtmlAttributeName(name)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_unusual_name', 'p1', `Element "${elementId}" _attributes[${index}] uses unusual attribute "${name}".`));
    }
    if (name.toLowerCase() === 'class') {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_class_disallowed', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" must attach classes through _cssGlobalClasses, not _attributes.`));
    }
    if (name.toLowerCase() === 'class' && firstString(attribute.value) && !/^[A-Za-z0-9_:\-[\]\s/%.]+$/.test(firstString(attribute.value))) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_class_value_invalid', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" _attributes[${index}] has an unsafe class attribute value.`));
    }
    if (/^on/i.test(name)) {
      errors.push(stageBIssue('stage_b_attribute_inline_handler', 'p0', `Element "${elementId}" must not use inline event handler attribute "${name}".`));
    }
  });
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function stageBCustomCssTargetsOnlyUnexposedInlineMarkup(customCss, inlineMarkupClassNames = new Set()) {
  const rules = extractStageBCssRuleSummaries(customCss);
  const nonPseudoRules = rules.filter((rule) => !splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector).every((selector) => (
    /::(?:before|after|marker|selection|backdrop|placeholder|file-selector-button)\b/i.test(selector)
  )));
  if (nonPseudoRules.length === 0) return false;
  return nonPseudoRules.every((rule) => splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector).every((selector) => {
    const classTargets = extractPixflowCssClassNames(selector);
    if (classTargets.some((className) => inlineMarkupClassNames.has(className))) return true;
    return /\s(?:span|small|strong|b|em)(?:\s|[:.#>]|$)/i.test(selector)
      && selector.trim().split(/\s+|\s*>\s*/).length >= 3;
  }));
}

function isPixflowStageBAllowedHtmlAttributeName(value) {
  return /^(?:data|aria)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$|^(?:id|role|tabindex|title|href|type|name|hidden|inert|dir|lang|draggable|contenteditable|spellcheck|download|hreflang|referrerpolicy|action|method|enctype|accept-charset|novalidate|cite|scope|headers|colspan|rowspan|datetime|min|max|low|high|optimum|value|width|height|open|reversed|start)$/i.test(firstString(value));
}

function normalizeStageBSourceRichTextDescendantCss(result, styleMap) {
  // Strong/span/em nodes frequently remain inside one editable Bricks rich
  // text value. They cannot receive a separate synthetic global class, so
  // retain their authored ancestor relationship in page-scoped CSS.
  const rules = arrayValue(objectValue(styleMap).rules).filter((rule) => (
    /(^|[\s>+~,])(?:span|strong|b|em|small)(?=$|[\s.#:[>+~,])/i.test(firstString(rule?.selector))
    && Object.keys(objectValue(rule?.declarations)).length > 0
  ));
  if (rules.length === 0) return;
  const chunks = [];
  const selectorGroups = [];
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const declarations = serializePixflowCssDeclarations(rule.declarations);
    if (!declarations) continue;
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector)
      .map((selector) => selector.trim())
      .filter(Boolean)
      .map((selector) => /^#brx-content\b/i.test(selector) ? selector : `#brx-content ${selector}`);
    if (selectors.length === 0) continue;
    chunks.push(`${selectors.join(', ')} { ${declarations} }`);
    selectorGroups.push(rule.selector);
  }
  if (chunks.length === 0) return;
  const block = chunks.join('\n');
  for (const key of ['page_settings', 'stage_b_page_settings']) {
    const settings = objectValue(result[key]);
    settings.customCss = replaceStageBPageCssSelectorGroups(
      firstString(settings.customCss),
      selectorGroups,
      block,
    );
    result[key] = settings;
  }
}

function isStageBSvgArtworkCodeElement(settings) {
  if (firstString(settings?.source) !== 'code' && !firstString(settings?.code)) {
    return false;
  }
  return arrayValue(settings?._attributes).some((attribute) => (
    firstString(attribute?.name).toLowerCase() === 'data-pixflow-svg-role'
    && firstString(attribute?.value).toLowerCase() === 'artwork'
  ));
}

function countCssVariableDeclarations(cssText) {
  const matches = String(cssText || '').match(/--[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*\s*:/g);
  return Array.isArray(matches) ? matches.length : 0;
}

function countStageBRootCssVariableDeclarations(cssText) {
  const rules = extractStageBCssRuleSummaries(cssText);
  let count = 0;
  for (const rule of rules) {
    const selectors = splitPixflowCssSelectorList(rule.selector);
    if (!selectors.some((selector) => /^%root%\s*$/i.test(selector.trim()))) {
      continue;
    }
    count += Object.keys(objectValue(rule.declarations)).filter((key) => /^--[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(key)).length;
  }
  return count;
}

function collectStageBLocalAssetRefs(settings) {
  const refs = [];
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.image, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.src, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.url, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?._background, refs);
  return [...new Set(refs.filter((ref) => isStageBLocalAssetRef(ref)))];
}

function inspectStageBSourceCssFidelity(context) {
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const styleMap = objectValue(context?.styleMap);
  const stageAHtml = firstString(context?.stageAHtml);
  const sourceRules = Array.isArray(styleMap.rules) ? styleMap.rules : [];
  if (sourceRules.length === 0) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }

  const payloadCssText = collectStageBPayloadCssText(context);
  const payloadSearchText = [
    payloadCssText,
    // Background images and other native class settings are not CSS text, but
    // they are still valid preservation evidence for source-fidelity QA.
    JSON.stringify(arrayValue(context?.globalClasses)),
    JSON.stringify(arrayValue(context?.content)),
    JSON.stringify(arrayValue(context?.headerContent)),
    JSON.stringify(arrayValue(context?.footerContent)),
  ].join('\n');

  // Pixflow-owned: inline text marks such as <span class="hero-mark"> only
  // render correctly when their source selector CSS is carried into scoped
  // Bricks CSS. The class name appearing in editable text is not enough.
  const inlineClassNames = collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNames([
    ...arrayValue(context?.content),
    ...arrayValue(context?.headerContent),
    ...arrayValue(context?.footerContent),
  ]);
  for (const className of inlineClassNames) {
    const relatedRules = sourceRules.filter((rule) => arrayValue(rule.classNames).includes(className));
    if (relatedRules.length === 0) {
      continue;
    }
    const cssCarriesSelector = new RegExp(`\\.${escapeRegExp(encodePixflowCssIdentifier(className))}(?:\\b|[\\s:{.#>+~\\[])`, 'i').test(payloadCssText);
    if (!cssCarriesSelector) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_inline_markup_css_missing',
        'p1',
        `Editable text contains inline class "${className}", but the Bricks payload does not carry source CSS for ".${className}". Preserve the source selector in page_settings.customCss or scoped _cssCustom so marked words render like Stage A.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const backgroundAssets = collectStageBSourceBackgroundAssets(sourceRules);
  for (const asset of backgroundAssets) {
    if (!payloadSearchText.includes(asset.url)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_background_asset_missing',
        'p1',
        `Stage A source CSS uses background image "${asset.url}" in selector "${asset.selector}", but the Bricks payload does not reference it. Preserve it as a Bricks background/image setting or scoped CSS background.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const formControlRules = collectStageBSourceControlRules(sourceRules);
  // Stylesheets commonly ship generic `input`/`select` rules for components
  // that are not present in the accepted page (for example, an unused search
  // component in a design-system bundle). Only require a native Bricks form
  // when the source document contains an actual control to preserve.
  const sourceControlCount = countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'input')
    + countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'select')
    + countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'textarea');
  if (formControlRules.length > 0 && sourceControlCount > 0 && countStageBBricksFormFields([
    ...arrayValue(context?.content),
    ...arrayValue(context?.headerContent),
    ...arrayValue(context?.footerContent),
  ]) === 0) {
    errors.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_controls_missing_bricks_form',
      'p0',
      'Stage A contains input/select/textarea control styling, but the Bricks payload has no native form fields. Rebuild source controls with Bricks form elements instead of flattening them to div/text.'
    ));
  }
  for (const rule of formControlRules) {
    const classNames = arrayValue(rule.classNames).filter(Boolean);
    if (classNames.length === 0) {
      continue;
    }
    const carried = classNames.some((className) => new RegExp(`\\.${escapeRegExp(encodePixflowCssIdentifier(className))}(?:\\b|[\\s:{.#>+~\\[])`, 'i').test(payloadCssText));
    if (!carried) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_control_selector_css_missing',
        'p1',
        `Stage A control selector "${rule.selector}" defines form/input styling, but no matching scoped CSS was carried into the Bricks payload. Rebuild the control with Bricks form/filter elements or preserve the source control selector CSS.`
      ));
    }
  }

  return { errors, warnings };
}

function inspectStageBSourceSemanticFidelity(context) {
  // Pixflow-owned: bridge QA must catch source inventory loss before the model
  // marks a handoff as ready. These checks are generic parity gates, not
  // project-specific patches for the current fixtures.
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const sourceMap = objectValue(context?.sourceMap);
  const documentStats = objectValue(sourceMap.document);
  const stageAHtml = firstString(context?.stageAHtml);
  const elements = [
    ...arrayValue(context?.content),
    ...arrayValue(context?.headerContent),
    ...arrayValue(context?.footerContent),
  ];
  const payloadText = [
    JSON.stringify(elements),
    collectStageBPayloadCssText(context),
    firstString(objectValue(context?.pageSettings).customScriptsBodyFooter),
    firstString(objectValue(context?.pageSettings).customScriptsHeader),
    firstString(objectValue(context?.pageSettings).customCss),
    firstString(objectValue(objectValue(context?.result).stage_b_page_settings).customScriptsBodyFooter),
    firstString(objectValue(objectValue(context?.result).stage_b_page_settings).customCss),
  ].join('\n');

  const inventoryCounts = buildStageBEffectiveSourceActionCounts(documentStats, context);
  const sourceLinkCount = inventoryCounts.linkCount;
  const sourceButtonCount = inventoryCounts.buttonCount;
  const sourceActionCount = sourceLinkCount + sourceButtonCount;
  if (sourceActionCount > 0) {
    const bricksLinkCount = countStageBEffectiveLinkAffordances(elements);
    const minimum = Math.max(1, Math.floor(sourceActionCount * 0.85));
    if (bricksLinkCount < minimum) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_source_links_missing',
        'p1',
        `Stage A source declares ${sourceLinkCount} links and ${sourceButtonCount} buttons/action anchors, but the Bricks payload exposes only ${bricksLinkCount} link affordances. Restore dropped nav, CTA, card, social, or inline links with Bricks settings.link before apply-ready.`
      ));
    } else if ((sourceActionCount <= 5 && bricksLinkCount > sourceActionCount + 10) || (sourceActionCount > 5 && bricksLinkCount > sourceActionCount * 2)) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_source_links_overgenerated',
        'p1',
        `Stage A source declares ${sourceLinkCount} links and ${sourceButtonCount} buttons/action anchors, but the Bricks payload exposes ${bricksLinkCount}. Remove duplicated or accidental links unless this expansion is documented in handoff-critique.md.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const sourceImageCount = Number(documentStats.imageCount || 0);
  if (sourceImageCount > 0) {
    const bricksImageCount = countStageBEffectiveElementOccurrences(elements, 'image');
    if (bricksImageCount < sourceImageCount) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_source_images_missing',
        'p1',
        `Stage A source declares ${sourceImageCount} image elements, but the Bricks payload has ${bricksImageCount} image elements. Preserve image slots, aspect ratios, and local/source refs before apply-ready.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const sourceVideoCount = countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'video');
  // Ignore hidden/1x1 implementation iframes (analytics, route announcers,
  // and saved-resource shims). They are not visual surfaces that need a
  // Bricks fallback; visible runtime media still remains a parity requirement.
  const sourceIframeCount = countStageBVisualSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'iframe');
  const sourceCanvasCount = countStageBVisualSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'canvas');
  const bricksVideoCount = countStageBEffectiveElementOccurrences(elements, 'video');
  const payloadHasIframeOrCanvasFallback = /\b(?:iframe|canvas|embed|video-fallback|media-fallback|shader|player)\b/i.test(payloadText);
  if (sourceVideoCount > 0 && bricksVideoCount < sourceVideoCount) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_video_missing',
      'p1',
      `Stage A source declares ${sourceVideoCount} video elements, but the Bricks payload has ${bricksVideoCount}. Preserve videos with native Bricks video settings or a documented visual fallback.`
    ));
  }
  if ((sourceIframeCount > 0 || sourceCanvasCount > 0) && !payloadHasIframeOrCanvasFallback) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_runtime_media_missing',
      'p1',
      `Stage A source declares iframe/canvas runtime media (${sourceIframeCount} iframe, ${sourceCanvasCount} canvas), but the Bricks payload has no recognizable runtime media or fallback. Preserve the visual surface before apply-ready.`
    ));
  }

  const sourceControlCount = countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'input')
    + countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'select')
    + countStageBSourceTags(stageAHtml, 'textarea');
  if (sourceControlCount > 0) {
    const bricksFieldCount = countStageBBricksFormFields(elements)
      + countStageBSafeCssStateControls(elements);
    if (bricksFieldCount < sourceControlCount) {
      warnings.push(stageBIssue(
        'stage_b_source_form_fields_incomplete',
        'p1',
        `Stage A source declares ${sourceControlCount} form controls, but the Bricks payload has ${bricksFieldCount} native Bricks form fields. Preserve field order, placeholders, labels, and frontend styling.`
      ));
    }
  }

  const sourceHasReveal = /\bdata-reveal\b/i.test(stageAHtml)
    || /\bclass\s*=\s*(["'])[^"']*\breveal\b/i.test(stageAHtml)
    || /\bIntersectionObserver\b/i.test(stageAHtml);
  if (sourceHasReveal && !/\b(?:data-reveal|data-revealed|IntersectionObserver|\breveal\b)/i.test(payloadText)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_reveal_behavior_missing',
      'p1',
      'Stage A source uses reveal/IntersectionObserver runtime behavior, but the Bricks payload does not preserve reveal attributes, CSS, or page settings script. Preserve the source interaction state or document a deliberate visual fallback.'
    ));
  }

  const sourceScriptCount = Number(documentStats.scriptCount || 0);
  if (sourceScriptCount > 0 && !/\bcustomScripts(?:BodyFooter|Header)\b|<script\b|IntersectionObserver|addEventListener|querySelector/i.test(payloadText)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_source_scripts_not_represented',
      'p2',
      `Stage A source declares ${sourceScriptCount} script blocks, but the Bricks result does not appear to carry page-level script behavior. Verify the scripts are unnecessary or preserve safe behavior in page settings.`
    ));
  }

  return { errors, warnings };
}

function inspectStageBVisualParityReport(report, prepared = {}) {
  // Pixflow-owned: browser side-by-side evidence is the final quality signal
  // for handoff parity. When the harness writes this report, feed major visual
  // deltas back into the same repair loop as schema/source-inventory QA.
  const errors = [];
  const warnings = [];
  const visualReport = objectValue(report);
  if (Object.keys(visualReport).length === 0) {
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  const reportSignature = objectValue(visualReport.resultSignature);
  const currentSignature = fileContentSignature(firstString(prepared?.resultFile)) || fileSignature(firstString(prepared?.resultFile));
  if (Object.keys(reportSignature).length === 0) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_visual_parity_report_unsigned',
      'p2',
      'stage-b-visual-parity.json has no result signature and may describe an older Bricks payload. Re-run the live side-by-side harness before treating visual parity as apply-ready evidence.'
    ));
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  if (Object.keys(reportSignature).length > 0 && currentSignature && !signaturesEqual(reportSignature, currentSignature)) {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_visual_parity_report_stale',
      'p2',
      'stage-b-visual-parity.json was captured for an older bricks-result.json. Re-run the live side-by-side harness after the current repair before using visual deltas as apply-ready evidence.'
    ));
    return { errors, warnings };
  }
  for (const issue of arrayValue(visualReport.issues)) {
    const viewport = firstString(issue.viewport, 'unknown');
    const message = firstString(issue.message);
    if (!message) continue;
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      `stage_b_visual_parity_${slugify(viewport)}`,
      'p1',
      `Visual parity ${viewport}: ${message}. Repair layout, spacing, source interactions, or responsive settings so the Bricks render matches the accepted HTML side-by-side.`
    ));
  }
  if (arrayValue(visualReport.issues).length === 0 && firstString(visualReport.status).toLowerCase() === 'failed') {
    warnings.push(stageBIssue(
      'stage_b_visual_parity_failed',
      'p1',
      'stage-b-visual-parity.json reports failed visual parity but did not include detailed issues. Re-run the side-by-side harness or inspect screenshots before apply-ready.'
    ));
  }
  return { errors, warnings };
}

function buildStageBEffectiveSourceActionCounts(documentStats, context = {}) {
  // Pixflow-owned: page baseline QA should not penalize intentionally omitted
  // header/footer template candidates. Those parts are handled by their own
  // include decisions and template payloads, not by normal page content.
  let linkCount = Number(documentStats?.linkCount || 0);
  let buttonCount = Number(documentStats?.buttonCount || 0);
  buttonCount -= countStageBSourceFormNonLinkButtons(firstString(context?.stageAHtml));
  for (const [planKey, includeKey] of [
    ['headerPlan', 'includeHeader'],
    ['footerPlan', 'includeFooter'],
  ]) {
    const plan = objectValue(context?.[planKey]);
    if (!plan || plan[includeKey]) {
      continue;
    }
    const selected = objectValue(plan.selectedSection);
    linkCount -= Number(selected.linkCount || 0);
    buttonCount -= Number(selected.buttonCount || 0);
  }
  return {
    linkCount: Math.max(0, linkCount),
    buttonCount: Math.max(0, buttonCount),
  };
}

function countStageBBricksLinkAffordances(elements) {
  let count = 0;
  const visit = (value, elementName = '') => {
    if (!value) return;
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      for (const item of value) visit(item, elementName);
      return;
    }
    if (typeof value !== 'object') return;
    const name = firstString(value.name, elementName);
    const settings = objectValue(value.settings);
    if (name === 'button' || name === 'text-link' || firstString(settings.tag).toLowerCase() === 'button') {
      count += 1;
    } else if (settings.link && stageBLinkSettingLooksPopulated(settings.link)) {
      count += 1;
    }
    for (const item of arrayValue(settings.items)) {
      if (stageBLinkSettingLooksPopulated(item?.link) || firstString(item?.url, item?.href)) {
        count += 1;
      }
    }
    for (const child of Object.values(value)) {
      if (child && typeof child === 'object' && child !== settings) {
        visit(child, name);
      }
    }
  };
  for (const element of arrayValue(elements)) {
    visit(element, firstString(element?.name));
  }
  return count;
}

function countStageBElementOwnLinkAffordances(element) {
  if (!element || typeof element !== 'object' || Array.isArray(element)) return 0;
  const name = firstString(element.name, element.type).toLowerCase();
  const settings = objectValue(element.settings);
  let count = 0;
  if (name === 'button' || name === 'text-link' || firstString(settings.tag).toLowerCase() === 'button') {
    count += 1;
  } else if (settings.link && stageBLinkSettingLooksPopulated(settings.link)) {
    count += 1;
  }
  for (const item of arrayValue(settings.items)) {
    if (stageBLinkSettingLooksPopulated(item?.link) || firstString(item?.url, item?.href)) {
      count += 1;
    }
  }
  return count;
}

function stageBQueryLoopRepeatCount(query) {
  const value = Number(
    query?.posts_per_page
      ?? query?.postsPerPage
      ?? query?.items_per_page
      ?? query?.itemsPerPage
      ?? query?.number
      ?? 1
  );
  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 1) return 1;
  return Math.max(1, Math.min(100, Math.floor(value)));
}

function buildStageBElementRepeatFactors(elements) {
  const flat = arrayValue(elements).filter((element) => element && typeof element === 'object' && !Array.isArray(element));
  const byId = new Map(flat.map((element) => [firstString(element.id), element]).filter(([id]) => Boolean(id)));
  const factors = new Map();
  const factorFor = (element, seen = new Set()) => {
    const id = firstString(element?.id);
    if (id && factors.has(id)) return factors.get(id);
    if (id && seen.has(id)) return 1;
    const nextSeen = new Set(seen);
    if (id) nextSeen.add(id);
    const settings = objectValue(element?.settings);
    const ownFactor = stageBControlIsEnabled(settings.hasLoop) ? stageBQueryLoopRepeatCount(objectValue(settings.query)) : 1;
    const parent = byId.get(firstString(element?.parent));
    const parentFactor = parent ? factorFor(parent, nextSeen) : 1;
    const result = Math.max(1, Math.min(1000, ownFactor * parentFactor));
    if (id) factors.set(id, result);
    return result;
  };
  for (const element of flat) factorFor(element);
  return { flat, factors };
}

export function countStageBEffectiveLinkAffordances(elements) {
  const { flat, factors } = buildStageBElementRepeatFactors(elements);
  return flat.reduce((count, element) => {
    const factor = factors.get(firstString(element.id)) || 1;
    return count + (countStageBElementOwnLinkAffordances(element) * factor);
  }, 0);
}

function countStageBEffectiveElementOccurrences(elements, wantedName) {
  const wanted = firstString(wantedName).toLowerCase();
  const { flat, factors } = buildStageBElementRepeatFactors(elements);
  return flat.reduce((count, element) => {
    if (firstString(element?.name, element?.type).toLowerCase() !== wanted) return count;
    return count + (factors.get(firstString(element.id)) || 1);
  }, 0);
}

function stageBLinkSettingLooksPopulated(link) {
  if (!link) return false;
  if (typeof link === 'string') return Boolean(link.trim());
  if (typeof link !== 'object' || Array.isArray(link)) return false;
  return Boolean(firstString(link.url, link.href, link.anchor, link.useDynamicData, link.ariaLabel, link.type));
}

function countStageBElementsByName(elements, wantedName) {
  const wanted = firstString(wantedName).toLowerCase();
  return arrayValue(elements).filter((element) => firstString(element?.name).toLowerCase() === wanted).length;
}

function countStageBSourceTags(html, tagName) {
  const tag = firstString(tagName).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9:-]/g, '');
  if (!tag) return 0;
  const matches = firstString(html).match(new RegExp(`<${tag}(?=\\s|>|/)`, 'gi'));
  return matches ? matches.length : 0;
}

function countStageBVisualSourceTags(html, tagName) {
  const tag = firstString(tagName).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9:-]/g, '');
  if (!tag) return 0;
  const pattern = new RegExp(`<${tag}\\b([^>]*)>`, 'gi');
  let count = 0;
  for (const match of firstString(html).matchAll(pattern)) {
    const attributes = firstString(match[1]).toLowerCase();
    if (/\baria-hidden\s*=\s*["']?true\b/.test(attributes)) continue;
    if (/(?:^|\s)hidden(?:\s|=|$)/.test(attributes)) continue;
    if (/\b(?:display\s*:\s*none|visibility\s*:\s*hidden|opacity\s*:\s*0)\b/.test(attributes)) continue;
    const width = attributes.match(/\bwidth\s*=\s*["']?([0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?)\s*(?:px)?/i)?.[1];
    const height = attributes.match(/\bheight\s*=\s*["']?([0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?)\s*(?:px)?/i)?.[1];
    if (width && Number(width) <= 1 && height && Number(height) <= 1) continue;
    count += 1;
  }
  return count;
}

function countStageBBricksFormFields(elements) {
  let count = 0;
  for (const element of arrayValue(elements)) {
    if (!element || typeof element !== 'object' || Array.isArray(element)) {
      continue;
    }
    if (firstString(element.name) === 'form') {
      count += arrayValue(objectValue(element.settings).fields).length;
    }
  }
  return count;
}

function collectStageBPayloadCssText(context) {
  const chunks = [];
  for (const classItem of arrayValue(context?.globalClasses)) {
    const css = firstString(objectValue(classItem?.settings)._cssCustom);
    if (css) chunks.push(css);
  }
  const result = objectValue(context?.result);
  const pageSettings = objectValue(context?.pageSettings);
  const stageBPageSettings = objectValue(result.stage_b_page_settings || result.stageBPageSettings);
  for (const settings of [pageSettings, stageBPageSettings]) {
    const customCss = firstString(objectValue(settings).customCss);
    if (customCss) chunks.push(customCss);
  }
  return chunks.join('\n');
}

function collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNames(elements) {
  const classNames = [];
  for (const element of arrayValue(elements)) {
    collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNamesFromValue(objectValue(element).settings, classNames);
  }
  return uniqueStrings(classNames.filter(Boolean));
}

function collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNamesFromValue(value, classNames) {
  if (!value) return;
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    for (const match of value.matchAll(/\bclass\s*=\s*(["'])(.*?)\1/gi)) {
      for (const className of String(match[2] || '').split(/\s+/)) {
        if (/^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/.test(className)) {
          classNames.push(className);
        }
      }
    }
    return;
  }
  if (typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) return;
  for (const item of Object.values(value)) {
    collectStageBInlineMarkupClassNamesFromValue(item, classNames);
  }
}

function collectStageBSourceBackgroundAssets(sourceRules) {
  const assets = [];
  for (const rule of arrayValue(sourceRules)) {
    const declarations = objectValue(rule.declarations);
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(declarations)) {
      if (!/^background(?:$|-)/i.test(key)) {
        continue;
      }
      for (const url of collectStageBCssUrls(value)) {
        if (isStageBImageSourceRef(url)) {
          assets.push({
            selector: firstString(rule.selector),
            url,
          });
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const uniqueAssets = new Map();
  for (const asset of assets) {
    uniqueAssets.set(`${asset.selector}::${asset.url}`, asset);
  }
  return [...uniqueAssets.values()];
}

function collectStageBCssUrls(cssValue) {
  const urls = [];
  for (const match of String(cssValue || '').matchAll(/url\(\s*(["']?)(.*?)\1\s*\)/gi)) {
    const url = String(match[2] || '').trim();
    if (url) urls.push(url);
  }
  return uniqueStrings(urls);
}

function collectStageBImageSourceRefs(settings) {
  // Pixflow-owned: source HTML often uses remote WordPress/media URLs; those
  // are valid handoff image sources until the insert layer sideloads media.
  const refs = [];
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.image, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.src, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?.url, refs);
  collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(settings?._background, refs);
  return [...new Set(refs.filter((ref) => isStageBImageSourceRef(ref)))];
}

function collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(value, refs) {
  if (!value) return;
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    refs.push(value);
    return;
  }
  if (typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) return;
  // Pixflow-owned: Bricks image settings can store source/local refs under
  // nested path/local/localPath/asset keys after the handoff asset pass.
  for (const key of ['url', 'full', 'src', 'sourceUrl', 'image', 'background', 'raw', 'path', 'local', 'localPath', 'asset', 'filename']) {
    if (typeof value[key] === 'string') {
      refs.push(value[key]);
    } else if (value[key] && typeof value[key] === 'object') {
      collectStageBAssetRefsFromValue(value[key], refs);
    }
  }
}

function isStageBImageSourceRef(ref) {
  const value = String(ref || '').trim();
  if (!value || value.startsWith('#') || value.startsWith('data:')) return false;
  if (/^(?:mailto:|tel:|blob:)/i.test(value)) return false;
  if (/^https?:\/\//i.test(value)) return true;
  return /\.(?:avif|gif|jpe?g|png|svg|webp)(?:[?#].*)?$/i.test(value);
}

function isStageBLocalAssetRef(ref) {
  const value = String(ref || '').trim();
  if (!value || value.startsWith('#') || value.startsWith('data:')) return false;
  if (/^(?:https?:|blob:|mailto:|tel:)/i.test(value)) return false;
  return /\.(?:avif|gif|jpe?g|png|svg|webp)(?:[?#].*)?$/i.test(value);
}

function stageBLocalAssetExists(workspaceDir, ref) {
  const cleanRef = String(ref || '').split('#')[0].split('?')[0].trim();
  if (!cleanRef) return false;
  const workspaceRoot = path.resolve(workspaceDir);
  const relativeRef = cleanRef.replace(/^[\\/]+/, '');
  const candidates = [
    path.resolve(workspaceRoot, relativeRef),
    // Saved-page resources are materialized beside the source evidence. The
    // sanitized HTML intentionally keeps its browser-relative `./Foo_files/*`
    // refs, so resolve that shape against the snapshot resource directory too.
    path.resolve(workspaceRoot, 'stage-a', 'source-resources', relativeRef),
    // Stage A HTML lives under stage-a/drafts. Its canonical split-source
    // media refs therefore begin ../source/assets and must resolve from that
    // directory before the containment check is applied.
    path.resolve(workspaceRoot, 'stage-a', 'drafts', relativeRef),
    path.resolve(workspaceRoot, 'stage-a', relativeRef),
  ];
  return candidates.some((candidate) => {
    const relative = path.relative(workspaceRoot, candidate);
    if (!relative || relative.startsWith('..') || path.isAbsolute(relative)) {
      return false;
    }
    return existsSync(candidate);
  });
}

function isStageBLocalMediaRef(ref) {
  const value = String(ref || '').trim();
  if (!value || value.startsWith('#') || value.startsWith('data:')) return false;
  if (/^(?:https?:|blob:|mailto:|tel:)/i.test(value)) return false;
  return /\.(?:avif|gif|jpe?g|png|svg|webp|m4a|mov|mp3|mp4|ogg|wav|webm)(?:[?#].*)?$/i.test(value);
}

function stageBIssue(id, severity, message) {
  return { id, severity, qa_severity: severity, message };
}

function summarizeStageBQa(qa) {
  return {
    status: firstString(qa?.status, 'unknown'),
    blocking: Boolean(qa?.blocking),
    score: Number(qa?.score || 0),
    severity: qa?.severity || {},
    qualityGate: qa?.qualityGate
      ? {
          passed: qa.qualityGate.passed === true,
          minScore: Number(qa.qualityGate.minScore || 0),
          allowP1: qa.qualityGate.allowP1 === true,
          allowLowQa: qa.qualityGate.allowLowQa === true,
          failures: Array.isArray(qa.qualityGate.failures) ? qa.qualityGate.failures.map((failure) => firstString(failure)).filter(Boolean) : [],
        }
      : null,
    issueCount: Array.isArray(qa?.issues) ? qa.issues.length : 0,
    issues: (Array.isArray(qa?.issues) ? qa.issues : []).slice(0, 12).map((issue) => ({
      id: firstString(issue?.id),
      severity: firstString(issue?.severity, issue?.qa_severity),
      message: firstString(issue?.message),
    })),
  };
}

function parseStageBQualityPolicy(flags = {}) {
  const minScore = Math.min(100, parseNonNegativeIntegerFlag(
    firstString(flags.stageBMinScore, flags.stage_b_min_score, flags.minStageBScore, flags.min_score, flags.minScore),
    DEFAULT_STAGE_B_MIN_QA_SCORE
  ));
  return {
    minScore,
    // Pixflow-owned: preserve already-normalized policy objects when the QA
    // gate re-enters this parser from repair/apply helpers.
    allowP1: isTruthyFlag(firstDefined(flags.allowP1, flags.stageBAllowP1, flags.stage_b_allow_p1, flags.allowStageBP1, flags.allow_stage_b_p1)),
    allowLowQa: isTruthyFlag(firstDefined(flags.allowLowQa, flags.allowLowStageBQa, flags.allow_low_stage_b_qa, flags.skipStageBQaGate, flags.skip_stage_b_qa_gate)),
  };
}

function applyStageBQualityGate(qa, policyInput = {}) {
  const policy = parseStageBQualityPolicy(policyInput);
  const qualityGate = buildStageBQualityGate(qa, policy);
  return makeStageBQualityFindingsNonBlocking(qa, qualityGate);
}

function buildStageBQualityGate(qa, policyInput = {}) {
  const policy = parseStageBQualityPolicy(policyInput);
  const severity = normalizedStageBSeverityCounts(qa);
  const score = Number.isFinite(Number(qa?.score)) ? Number(qa.score) : 0;
  const failures = [];
  if (severity.p0 > 0) {
    failures.push(`P0 issues remaining: ${severity.p0}`);
  }
  if (!policy.allowLowQa && score < policy.minScore) {
    failures.push(`Structural QA score ${score} is below required minimum ${policy.minScore}`);
  }
  if (!policy.allowP1 && severity.p1 > 0) {
    failures.push(`P1 repair-required issues remaining: ${severity.p1}`);
  }
  return {
    passed: failures.length === 0,
    minScore: policy.minScore,
    allowP1: policy.allowP1,
    allowLowQa: policy.allowLowQa,
    score,
    severity,
    failures,
  };
}

function normalizedStageBSeverityCounts(qa) {
  const severity = objectValue(qa?.severity);
  if (Object.keys(severity).length > 0) {
    return {
      p0: Number(severity.p0 || 0),
      p1: Number(severity.p1 || 0),
      p2: Number(severity.p2 || 0),
    };
  }
  return severityCounts(Array.isArray(qa?.issues) ? qa.issues : []);
}

function firstDefined(...values) {
  for (const value of values) {
    if (typeof value !== 'undefined') return value;
  }
  return undefined;
}

function isTruthyFlag(value) {
  if (value === true || value === 1) return true;
  return /^(?:1|true|yes|on)$/i.test(String(value || '').trim());
}

function fileSignature(filePath) {
  try {
    const stats = statSync(filePath);
    return {
      mtimeMs: Number(stats.mtimeMs || 0),
      size: Number(stats.size || 0),
    };
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

function signaturesEqual(left, right) {
  if (!left || !right) return false;
  if (firstString(left.sha256) || firstString(right.sha256)) {
    return firstString(left.sha256) === firstString(right.sha256) && Number(left.size || 0) === Number(right.size || 0);
  }
  return left.mtimeMs === right.mtimeMs && left.size === right.size;
}

function fileContentSignature(filePath) {
  try {
    const bytes = readFileSync(filePath);
    return {
      sha256: createHash('sha256').update(bytes).digest('hex'),
      size: Number(bytes.length || 0),
    };
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

function renderStageBRepairPrompt(prepared, qa, attempt, maxAttempts, policyInput = {}) {
  if (isStageBVisualOnlyRepair(qa, policyInput) && existsSync(path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'stage-b-visual-parity.json'))) {
    return renderStageBVisualRepairPrompt(prepared, qa, attempt, maxAttempts, policyInput);
  }
  const qualityPolicy = parseStageBQualityPolicy(policyInput);
  const qualityGate = buildStageBQualityGate(qa, qualityPolicy);
  const severityRank = { p0: 0, p1: 1, p2: 2 };
  const repairSeverities = new Set(['p0']);
  if (!qualityPolicy.allowLowQa) {
    repairSeverities.add('p1');
    if (Number(qa?.score || 0) < qualityPolicy.minScore) {
      repairSeverities.add('p2');
    }
  }
  const issueLines = (Array.isArray(qa?.issues) ? qa.issues : [])
    .filter((issue) => repairSeverities.has(firstString(issue?.severity, issue?.qa_severity, 'p2').toLowerCase()))
    .sort((a, b) => (severityRank[firstString(a?.severity, a?.qa_severity, 'p2').toLowerCase()] ?? 9)
      - (severityRank[firstString(b?.severity, b?.qa_severity, 'p2').toLowerCase()] ?? 9))
    .slice(0, 36)
    .map((issue) => {
      const severity = firstString(issue?.severity, issue?.qa_severity, 'p2').toUpperCase();
      return `- ${severity} ${firstString(issue.id, 'stage_b_issue')}: ${firstString(issue.message)}`;
    });
  const lines = [];
  lines.push('You are repairing Pixflow Design Stage B Bricks JSON.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push(`Repair attempt ${attempt} of ${maxAttempts}.`);
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('The Stage A artifact is already accepted. Do not redesign the page, rename the project, change content strategy, or remove sections to make QA easier.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Goal: exact side-by-side parity with the accepted Stage A HTML after Bricks insertion. Valid JSON is not enough. Repair toward the source screenshot, source inventory, and Bricks editability at the same time.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push(`Local QA gate: score must be at least ${qualityPolicy.minScore}, P0 must be zero, and P1 must be zero${qualityPolicy.allowP1 ? ' unless explicitly allowed' : ''}.`);
  lines.push(`Current QA: status ${firstString(qa?.status, 'unknown')}, score ${Number(qa?.score || 0)}, severity ${JSON.stringify(normalizedStageBSeverityCounts(qa))}.`);
  if (qualityGate.failures.length > 0) {
    lines.push(`Gate failures: ${qualityGate.failures.join('; ')}.`);
  }
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Files you may edit:');
  lines.push(`- ${path.basename(prepared.resultFile)}: main Stage B result; keep content/global_classes/stage_b_header/stage_b_footer synchronized.`);
  lines.push(`- ${path.basename(prepared.payloadFile)}: must exactly mirror bricks-result.json content.`);
  lines.push(`- ${path.basename(prepared.headerPayloadFile)}: must exactly mirror bricks-result.json stage_b_header.content when a header is included.`);
  lines.push(`- ${path.basename(prepared.footerPayloadFile)}: must exactly mirror bricks-result.json stage_b_footer.content when a footer is included.`);
  lines.push(`- ${path.basename(prepared.globalClassesFile)}: must exactly mirror bricks-result.json global_classes.`);
  lines.push('- conversion-report.md: update only if the repair changes mapping or preservation notes.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Output and inspection limits:');
  lines.push('- This workspace is not a Git repository. Do not run Git commands.');
  lines.push('- Do not print or dump full JSON maps, full CSS text, full HTML, full skill files, AGENTS.md, TODO.md, Bricks payloads, or global class arrays.');
  lines.push('- Do not run `Get-Content -Raw` or broad `cat`/`type` commands against large workspace files. Use targeted `rg`/`Select-String`, `Get-Content -TotalCount`, concise JSON key summaries, and capped scripts.');
  lines.push('- Keep terminal output to concrete failing ids, counts, selectors, and repair notes; full raw logs are not useful in the browser stream.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Repair-required QA issues to fix:');
  lines.push(issueLines.length > 0 ? issueLines.join('\n') : '- No detailed QA issue lines were recorded; rerun QA after checking result consistency and sidecar parity.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Required source-fidelity repair pass before editing JSON:');
  lines.push('- Read stage-b-source-map.json, stage-b-style-map.json, stage-b-section-map.json, stage-b-fidelity-plan.md, and handoff-critique.md.');
  lines.push('- If stage-b-visual-parity.json exists, read it before editing. Treat its desktop/tablet/mobile deltas, sectionLayoutDeltas, and screenshot paths as repair evidence.');
  lines.push('- Inventory the accepted source: sections, nested landmarks, headings, links/buttons, images/background media, videos/iframes/canvas, forms/fields, data attributes, scripts, sticky/fixed layers, and repeated components.');
  lines.push('- Compare that inventory against bricks-result.json. Missing source links, media, fields, reveal behavior, or nested hero/header content are repair issues, not acceptable omissions.');
  lines.push('- Preserve DOM order and visual section rhythm. Do not satisfy section-count QA by creating empty or visually collapsed sections.');
  lines.push('- If browser metrics or screenshots are available, prioritize large deltas in scroll height, hero heading position, second-section height, media counts, form field styling, and link counts.');
  lines.push('- For each failing viewport, compare stage-b-visual-parity.json sectionLayoutDeltas source vs Bricks: section top/height, child count, absoluteCount, display, gridTemplateColumns, flexDirection/flexWrap, gap, padding, and first children. Repair the section wrapper and its global class settings until the computed layout family matches the source.');
  lines.push('- For large positive height deltas, look for flattened source grids/collages that became vertical Bricks stacks, missing absolute positioning, missing grid template columns, incorrect card aspect-ratio, or repeated child wrappers with unintended block flow.');
  lines.push('- For large negative height deltas, look for collapsed source sections, missing min-height, missing media/background layers, missing cards, or responsive wrappers that need row-to-column behavior only at the source breakpoint.');
  lines.push('- For hero heading top deltas, repair hero section min-height, alignment, padding, sticky/header offset, and background/media layers before changing typography.');
  lines.push('- For link/action deltas, repair actual anchors/buttons and nav/action groups; do not satisfy visual QA by adding hidden or empty links.');
  lines.push('- Repair broad causes: missing sticky/scroll section behavior, incorrect section min-height, incorrect section/container display, missing absolute/fixed media layers, reveal states, responsive breakpoint settings, or Bricks Theme Style defaults. Do not patch only one fixture title or selector.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Targeted craft repair rules:');
  lines.push('- If an issue mentions Pixflow SVG icon styling, move SVG icon size/colour to a global class `settings.icon` object with `height`, `width`, `stroke`, optional `strokeWidth`, and optional `fill`; do not use `iconSize` or `iconColor` for SVG icons.');
  lines.push('- If an issue mentions stat rings, avoid a dashed border on the stat container. Build a circular number element plus separate label text and preserve the source geometry.');
  lines.push('- If an issue mentions plate borders, remove added solid borders unless the accepted Stage A source visibly had that border.');
  lines.push('- If an issue mentions row, action, nav, wrapper, or marquee layout, set `_display: "flex"` and `_direction: "row"` on the same Bricks element or class, plus `_flexWrap` only when the source allows wrapping.');
  lines.push('- If an issue mentions responsive header direction, add suffixed Bricks controls such as `_direction:mobile_portrait` to the actual inner wrapper, not an unrelated child.');
  lines.push('- If a visual report shows source section/card children using grid or multi-column layout, add Bricks `_display: "grid"` or flex row settings to the same wrapper/class and set matching column/gap controls instead of leaving children as normal blocks.');
  lines.push('- If a visual report shows source decorative cards/shapes as absolute/fixed/sticky descendants, preserve that positioning and z-index in Bricks settings/global classes or page CSS. Do not convert an absolute collage into stacked content cards.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Header contract when stage_b_header.includeHeader is true:');
  lines.push('- Keep header elements in stage_b_header.content, not in the normal page content array.');
  lines.push('- Repair the approved source header section identified by stage_b_header.sourceSectionOdId or stage-b-header-plan.json.selectedSectionOdId. Source-backed rails/topbar may stay as auxiliary bands, but they are not the nav/header wrapper unless that selected section id says so.');
  lines.push('- The header section must contain an inner container/block wrapper with explicit Bricks layout settings that match Stage A. Use grid controls for source grid headers and flex controls for source flex headers.');
  lines.push('- The nav/action block must preserve the source layout family. Source grid navs need _display "grid", _gridTemplateColumns, grid alignment, and gaps; source flex navs need _display "flex", _direction "row", optional _flexWrap, alignment, justification, and gaps.');
  lines.push('- Add responsive suffixed settings where needed, for example _direction:mobile_portrait "column" on the inner wrapper.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('Footer contract when stage_b_footer.includeFooter is true:');
  lines.push('- Keep footer elements in stage_b_footer.content, not in the normal page content array.');
  lines.push('- Preserve footer links, brand/copyright text, closing CTA/caption rhythm, and template scope.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('General Stage B contract:');
  lines.push('- Use Bricks underscore settings, not raw unprefixed layout keys.');
  lines.push('- Use `_direction` only on Section/Container/Block/Div layout elements. Use `_flexDirection` on headings, text, buttons, media, forms, and every other non-layout element; preserve that distinction for responsive suffixes.');
  lines.push('- Move routine source CSS into Bricks settings before `_cssCustom`: position/insets use `_position`, `_top`, `_right`, `_bottom`, `_left`, `_zIndex`, `_transform`; spacing uses `_padding`/`_margin` side objects; radius uses `_border.radius`; shadows use `_boxShadow`; media uses `_aspectRatio`, `_objectFit`, and `_objectPosition`.');
  lines.push('- Correct setting shapes: `_padding: { "top": "24px", "right": "32px", "bottom": "24px", "left": "32px" }`, `_border: { "width": "1px", "style": "solid", "color": { "raw": "var(--line)" }, "radius": { "top": "18px", "right": "18px", "bottom": "18px", "left": "18px" } }`, `_position: "absolute"`, `_top: "0"`, `_right: "0"`, `_zIndex: "4"`, `_transform: "translate3d(0, -12px, 0)"`.');
  lines.push('- Responsive setting shapes use Bricks suffixes such as `_padding:mobile_portrait`, `_direction:tablet_portrait`, `_top:mobile_portrait`, and `_gridTemplateColumns:mobile_portrait`; do not hide routine responsive fixes in media-query `_cssCustom` when a Bricks setting exists.');
  lines.push('- Heading elements must use `settings.tag` for `h1`-`h6`; replace any `tagName` fields because Bricks ignores them.');
  lines.push('- Preserve data attributes from Stage A and place any safe source JavaScript in page settings, not Bricks code elements.');
  lines.push('- Preserve every source anchor/button as a Bricks link or button unless it is provably decorative and documented in handoff-critique.md.');
  lines.push('- Preserve videos, iframes, canvas/runtime media, and background media as native Bricks elements or visual fallbacks with the same dimensions and layering.');
  lines.push('- Preserve real source controls as native Bricks form fields and ensure custom control CSS targets Bricks frontend form DOM.');
  lines.push('- Preserve source reveal/sticky/marquee/runtime hooks with `_attributes`, page CSS, and safe page scripts when they affect the visible result.');
  lines.push('- Do not use .od-root, --od-* token leakage, dashed stat approximations, incorrect extra wrapper structures, or %root%::before/after for visible dividers that can be Bricks child elements.');
  lines.push('- Keep global class IDs valid and children/parent references consistent.');
  lines.push('');
  lines.push('After editing, stop. The CLI will rerun local Stage B QA.');
  return lines.join('\n');
}

function assertStageBQaPasses(qa, policyInput = {}) {
  if (!stageBQaReportExists(qa)) {
    throw new CliError('Stage B local QA did not produce a diagnostic report.');
  }
}

function assertStageBRemoteQaReady(qa, qaFile, flags, label) {
  if (!stageBQaReportExists(qa)) {
    throw new CliError(`${label} requires a local Stage B QA report before remote import/insert: ${qaFile}`);
  }
}

async function collectStageAEventFiles(workspaceDir) {
  let entries = [];
  try {
    entries = await fs.readdir(workspaceDir);
  } catch {
    return [];
  }
  return entries
    .filter((entry) => /^stage-a-codex-events\.jsonl$/i.test(entry))
    .sort((a, b) => a.localeCompare(b))
    .map((entry) => path.join(workspaceDir, entry));
}

function buildStageARunnerInvocation(prepared, flags, overrides = {}) {
  const customCommand = firstString(flags.runnerCommand);
  if (customCommand) {
    const command = customCommand
      .replace(/\{workspace\}/g, prepared.workspaceDir)
      .replace(/\{prompt\}/g, firstString(prepared.promptFile, prepared.runnerPromptFile))
      .replace(/\{artifact\}/g, prepared.artifactFile);
    return {
      kind: 'custom_shell',
      display: command,
      command,
      shell: true,
      stdin: null,
      eventsFile: overrides.eventsFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'stage-a-runner-events.log'),
      stderrFile: overrides.stderrFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'stage-a-runner-stderr.log'),
    };
  }

  return buildBridgeStageRunnerInvocation('stage-a', prepared, flags, overrides);
}

function buildLibraryPageRunnerInvocation(prepared, flags, overrides = {}) {
  const customCommand = firstString(flags.runnerCommand);
  if (customCommand) {
    const command = customCommand
      .replace(/\{workspace\}/g, prepared.workspaceDir)
      .replace(/\{prompt\}/g, prepared.promptFile)
      .replace(/\{artifact\}/g, prepared.artifactFile);
    return {
      kind: 'custom_shell',
      display: command,
      command,
      shell: true,
      stdin: null,
      label: 'Pixflow Library planner',
      eventsFile: overrides.eventsFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'library-page-runner-events.log'),
      stderrFile: overrides.stderrFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'library-page-runner-stderr.log'),
    };
  }

  return buildBridgeStageRunnerInvocation('library-page', prepared, flags, overrides);
}

function buildBridgeStageRunnerInvocation(stage, prepared, flags, overrides = {}) {
  const runnerId = normalizeBridgeRunnerId(firstString(flags.runner, flags.agent, 'codex'));
  const agent = BRIDGE_AGENT_CATALOG.find((item) => item.id === runnerId);
  if (!agent) {
    throw new CliError(`Unknown local CLI runner "${runnerId}". Use one of: ${BRIDGE_AGENT_CATALOG.map((item) => item.id).join(', ')}.`);
  }
  if (!BRIDGE_STAGE_RUNNER_AGENT_IDS.has(agent.id)) {
    throw new CliError(`${agent.label} is detected/installable, but Pixflow does not yet have a verified non-interactive Stage A/B adapter for it. Select a runner-ready provider or use --runner-command.`);
  }

  const command = detectFirstCommandSync(agent);
  if (!command.path) {
    throw new CliError(`${agent.label} was selected, but none of these commands were found on this machine: ${agent.commands.join(', ')}.`);
  }

  const runnerSpec = buildBridgeStageRunnerSpec(agent.id, prepared, flags);
  const stagePrefix = stage === 'stage-b' ? 'stage-b' : (stage === 'library-page' ? 'library-page' : 'stage-a');
  const safeRunnerId = agent.id.replace(/[^a-z0-9-]/g, '-');
  const args = Array.isArray(runnerSpec.args) ? runnerSpec.args : [];
  return {
    kind: agent.id,
    display: [quoteForShell(command.path), ...args.map(quoteForShell)].join(' '),
    command: command.path,
    args,
    shell: shouldSpawnThroughShell(command.path),
    stdinFile: Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(runnerSpec, 'stdinFile')
      ? runnerSpec.stdinFile
      : (overrides.stdinFile || prepared.runnerPromptFile),
    stdin: runnerSpec.stdin ?? null,
    env: runnerSpec.env || {},
    label: stage === 'library-page' ? 'Pixflow Library planner' : undefined,
    eventsFile: overrides.eventsFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, `${stagePrefix}-${safeRunnerId}-events.jsonl`),
    stderrFile: overrides.stderrFile || path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, `${stagePrefix}-${safeRunnerId}-stderr.log`),
    // Pixflow-owned: only Stage B/Handoff runners are artifact-gated. Stage A
    // generation must still wait for the normal CLI exit semantics.
    completionFile: stage === 'stage-b' ? prepared.resultFile : null,
    completionRequiredFiles: stage === 'stage-b'
      ? [path.join(prepared.workspaceDir, 'handoff-critique.md')]
      : [],
    completionQuietMs: stage === 'stage-b' ? 12_000 : 0,
    maxRuntimeMs: stage === 'stage-b'
      ? parsePositiveIntegerFlag(
          firstString(overrides.maxRuntimeMs, flags.stageBRunnerTimeoutMs, flags.stage_b_runner_timeout_ms, flags.runnerTimeoutMs, flags.runner_timeout_ms),
          DEFAULT_STAGE_B_RUNNER_TIMEOUT_MS
        )
      : 0,
  };
}

function shouldSpawnThroughShell(commandPath) {
  return process.platform === 'win32' && /\.(cmd|bat)$/i.test(firstString(commandPath));
}

function commandLineForShellInvocation(invocation) {
  return [
    quoteForShell(invocation.command),
    ...(Array.isArray(invocation.args) ? invocation.args : []).map(quoteForShell),
  ].join(' ');
}

function buildOpenCodeStageRunnerEnv(workspaceDir) {
  let config = {};
  const inherited = String(process.env.OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT || '').trim();
  if (inherited) {
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(inherited);
      if (parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed)) {
        config = parsed;
      }
    } catch {
      config = {};
    }
  }

  const permission = config.permission && typeof config.permission === 'object' && !Array.isArray(config.permission)
    ? { ...config.permission }
    : {};
  const externalDirectory = permission.external_directory
    && typeof permission.external_directory === 'object'
    && !Array.isArray(permission.external_directory)
    ? { ...permission.external_directory }
    : {};
  const roots = Array.from(new Set([
    path.resolve(workspaceDir),
    path.resolve(workspaceDir, '..'),
    path.resolve(workspaceDir, '..', '..'),
  ]));
  for (const root of roots) {
    externalDirectory[root] = 'allow';
    externalDirectory[path.join(root, '*')] = 'allow';
    externalDirectory[path.join(root, '**')] = 'allow';
  }
  permission.external_directory = externalDirectory;
  config.permission = permission;

  return {
    OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT: JSON.stringify(config),
    OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG: 'true',
  };
}

function buildBridgeStageRunnerSpec(runnerId, prepared, flags) {
  const model = firstString(flags.model);
  if (runnerId === 'codex') {
    const args = bridgeCodexNeedsDangerFullAccessSandbox()
      ? ['exec', '--json', '--skip-git-repo-check', '--sandbox', 'danger-full-access']
      : [
          'exec',
          '--json',
          '--skip-git-repo-check',
          '--sandbox',
          'workspace-write',
          '-c',
          'sandbox_workspace_write.network_access=true',
        ];
    args.push('-c', 'default_permissions=":workspace"', '-c', 'web_search="live"', '-C', prepared.workspaceDir);
    if (process.env.OD_CODEX_DISABLE_PLUGINS === '1') {
      args.push('--disable', 'plugins');
    }
    if (model && model !== 'default') {
      args.push('--model', model);
    }
    const reasoning = firstString(flags.reasoning, flags.reasoningEffort);
    if (reasoning && reasoning !== 'default') {
      args.push('-c', `model_reasoning_effort="${bridgeClampCodexReasoning(model, reasoning)}"`);
    }
    if (flags.fastMode === true || flags['fast-mode'] === true) {
      args.push('-c', 'service_tier="fast"');
    }
    return { args };
  }

  if (runnerId === 'claude') {
    // Claude Code 2.1.162 can otherwise infer stream-json input from the
    // structured output mode and try to parse the plain prompt as consecutive
    // JSON records. Pin the stdin contract explicitly: Pixflow sends one UTF-8
    // text prompt here and only stdout is JSONL.
    const args = [
      '-p',
      '--input-format',
      'text',
      '--output-format',
      'stream-json',
      '--verbose',
      '--permission-mode',
      'bypassPermissions',
    ];
    if (model && model !== 'default') {
      args.push('--model', model);
    }
    return { args };
  }

  if (runnerId === 'opencode') {
    // Pixflow-owned: OpenCode otherwise spends a separate provider request on
    // an automatic session title before it processes the actual prompt. Some
    // provider/model combinations return an empty "unknown" title completion,
    // which prevents the real Bricks request from ever starting. Keep bridge
    // runs deterministic and non-interactive: no unrelated external plugins,
    // no title-model request, and no hidden permission prompt while writing the
    // Pixflow-owned workspace artifacts.
    const args = [
      'run',
      '--pure',
      '--title',
      'Pixflow Bricks Agent',
      '--dangerously-skip-permissions',
      '--format',
      'json',
    ];
    if (model && model !== 'default') {
      args.push('-m', model);
    }
    return {
      args,
      env: buildOpenCodeStageRunnerEnv(prepared.workspaceDir),
    };
  }

  if (runnerId === 'cursor-agent') {
    const args = [
      '--print',
      '--output-format',
      'stream-json',
      '--stream-partial-output',
      '--force',
      '--trust',
      '--workspace',
      prepared.workspaceDir,
    ];
    if (model && model !== 'default') {
      args.push('--model', model);
    }
    return { args };
  }

  if (runnerId === 'qwen') {
    const args = ['--yolo'];
    if (model && model !== 'default') {
      args.push('--model', model);
    }
    return { args };
  }

  if (runnerId === 'antigravity') {
    return buildBridgeAntigravityRunnerSpec(prepared, model, firstString(flags.reasoning));
  }

  throw new CliError(`Pixflow has no Stage A/B runner adapter for "${runnerId}".`);
}

function bridgeCodexNeedsDangerFullAccessSandbox() {
  if (firstString(process.env.OD_CODEX_SANDBOX).trim() === 'danger-full-access') return true;
  if (process.platform === 'win32') return true;
  return Boolean(firstString(process.env.WSL_DISTRO_NAME).trim());
}

function bridgeClampCodexReasoning(modelId, effort) {
  if (!effort) return effort;
  const raw = firstString(modelId).trim();
  const id = raw.includes('/') ? raw.split('/').pop() : raw;
  const lateGpt5Family =
    !id ||
    id === 'default' ||
    id.startsWith('gpt-5.2') ||
    id.startsWith('gpt-5.3') ||
    id.startsWith('gpt-5.4') ||
    id.startsWith('gpt-5.5');
  if (lateGpt5Family && effort === 'minimal') return 'low';
  if (id === 'gpt-5.1' && effort === 'xhigh') return 'high';
  if (id === 'gpt-5.1-codex-mini') {
    return effort === 'high' || effort === 'xhigh' ? 'high' : 'medium';
  }
  return effort;
}

function normalizeBridgeRunnerId(value) {
  const raw = firstString(value, 'codex').toLowerCase().trim().replace(/_/g, '-');
  return BRIDGE_STAGE_RUNNER_ALIASES.get(raw) || raw;
}

async function runStageAInvocation(invocation, cwd) {
  return runLocalInvocation(invocation, cwd, invocation.label || 'Stage A');
}

async function runLocalInvocation(invocation, cwd, label) {
  const liveOutput = invocation.jsonOutput ? process.stderr : process.stdout;
  process.stderr.write(`Running ${label} command in ${cwd}\n${invocation.display}\n`);
  const stdoutFile = invocation.eventsFile ? createWriteStream(invocation.eventsFile, { flags: 'w' }) : null;
  const stderrFile = invocation.stderrFile ? createWriteStream(invocation.stderrFile, { flags: 'w' }) : null;
  const stdin = invocation.stdinFile ? await fs.readFile(invocation.stdinFile, 'utf8') : invocation.stdin;
  if (firstString(invocation.env?.CODEX_HOME)) {
    await ensureIsolatedCodexHome(invocation.env.CODEX_HOME);
  }
  const eventSummary = {
    stdoutBytes: 0,
    stderrBytes: 0,
    jsonEventCount: 0,
    usage: null,
  };
  const runnerParserState = createBridgeRunnerParserState();
  let stdoutRemainder = '';
  let runnerFailureMessage = '';
  let lastOutputAt = Date.now();

  const handleRunnerJsonLine = (line) => {
    const trimmed = firstString(line).trim();
    if (!trimmed.startsWith('{')) return;
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed);
      eventSummary.jsonEventCount += 1;
      const usage = extractUsageFromRunnerEvent(parsed);
      if (usage) eventSummary.usage = usage;
      const failureMessage = bridgeRunnerEventFailureMessage(parsed, label);
      if (failureMessage) runnerFailureMessage = failureMessage;
      if (invocation.jsonOutput) {
        const semanticEvents = runnerEventToBridgeSemanticEvents(parsed, runnerParserState);
        eventSummary.toolUseCount = runnerParserState.toolUseCount;
        eventSummary.assistantTextCount = runnerParserState.assistantTextCount;
        for (const semanticEvent of semanticEvents) {
          process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(semanticEvent)}\n`);
        }
      } else {
        eventSummary.toolUseCount = runnerParserState.toolUseCount;
        eventSummary.assistantTextCount = runnerParserState.assistantTextCount;
      }
    } catch {
      // Runner output can include non-event lines; keep the raw log.
    }
  };

  const handleRunnerJsonChunk = (chunk, previousRemainder) => {
    const combined = `${previousRemainder}${chunk.toString('utf8')}`;
    const lines = combined.split(/\r?\n/);
    const nextRemainder = lines.pop() || '';
    for (const line of lines) {
      handleRunnerJsonLine(line);
    }
    return nextRemainder;
  };

  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    let settled = false;
    let completedViaFile = false;
    let completionTimer = null;
    let forceKillTimer = null;
    let runtimeTimer = null;
    let timedOut = false;
    const completionFile = firstString(invocation.completionFile);
    const completionQuietMs = Math.max(0, Number(invocation.completionQuietMs || 0));
    const maxRuntimeMs = Math.max(0, Number(invocation.maxRuntimeMs || 0));
    // Pixflow-owned: Stage B prepares a deterministic baseline before the
    // model starts. Artifact-gated completion must only count after the model
    // updates that artifact, otherwise the baseline can finish the handoff
    // before any real model conversion/repair work happens.
    const initialCompletionFileSignature = completionFile ? fileSignature(completionFile) : null;
    const completionRequiredFiles = arrayValue(invocation.completionRequiredFiles)
      .map((file) => firstString(file))
      .filter(Boolean);
    const initialCompletionRequiredFileSignatures = new Map(
      completionRequiredFiles.map((file) => [file, fileSignature(file)]),
    );
    const completionArtifactsUpdated = () => {
      if (!completionFile || !existsSync(completionFile)) return false;
      const currentCompletionSignature = fileSignature(completionFile);
      if (!currentCompletionSignature || signaturesEqual(currentCompletionSignature, initialCompletionFileSignature)) {
        return false;
      }
      return completionRequiredFiles.every((file) => {
        const current = fileSignature(file);
        return current && !signaturesEqual(current, initialCompletionRequiredFileSignatures.get(file));
      });
    };
    const cleanupTimers = () => {
      if (completionTimer) {
        clearInterval(completionTimer);
        completionTimer = null;
      }
      if (forceKillTimer) {
        clearTimeout(forceKillTimer);
        forceKillTimer = null;
      }
      if (runtimeTimer) {
        clearTimeout(runtimeTimer);
        runtimeTimer = null;
      }
    };
    const rejectOnce = (error) => {
      if (settled) return;
      settled = true;
      cleanupTimers();
      stdoutFile?.end();
      stderrFile?.end();
      reject(error);
    };
    const resolveOnce = (value) => {
      if (settled) return;
      settled = true;
      cleanupTimers();
      stdoutFile?.end();
      stderrFile?.end();
      resolve(value);
    };
    const childEnv = { ...process.env, ...(invocation.env || {}) };
    if (invocation.kind === 'opencode') {
      for (const key of Object.keys(childEnv)) {
        if (['OPENCODE', 'OPENCODE_PID', 'OPENCODE_RUN_ID', 'OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD'].includes(key.toUpperCase())) {
          delete childEnv[key];
        }
      }
    }
    const child = invocation.shell
      ? spawn(commandLineForShellInvocation(invocation), {
          cwd,
          shell: true,
          env: childEnv,
          stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
          windowsHide: true,
        })
      : spawn(invocation.command, invocation.args || [], {
          cwd,
          shell: false,
          env: childEnv,
          stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
          windowsHide: true,
        });

    child.stdout?.on('data', (chunk) => {
      lastOutputAt = Date.now();
      eventSummary.stdoutBytes += chunk.length;
      if (!invocation.jsonOutput) {
        liveOutput.write(chunk);
      }
      stdoutFile?.write(chunk);
      stdoutRemainder = handleRunnerJsonChunk(chunk, stdoutRemainder);
      if (runnerFailureMessage && shouldRejectRunnerFailureAfterArtifact({
        completedViaFile,
        completionFileExists: Boolean(completionFile && existsSync(completionFile)),
        completionArtifactsUpdated: completionArtifactsUpdated(),
      })) {
        try {
          child.kill('SIGTERM');
        } catch {
          // Ignore; rejectOnce below owns the user-facing failure.
        }
        rejectOnce(new CliError(runnerFailureMessage));
      }
    });

    child.stderr?.on('data', (chunk) => {
      lastOutputAt = Date.now();
      eventSummary.stderrBytes += chunk.length;
      process.stderr.write(chunk);
      stderrFile?.write(chunk);
    });

    if (stdin !== null && stdin !== undefined) {
      child.stdin?.end(stdin);
    } else {
      child.stdin?.end();
    }

    if (completionFile && completionQuietMs > 0) {
      completionTimer = setInterval(() => {
        if (settled || completedViaFile || !existsSync(completionFile)) return;
        if (!completionArtifactsUpdated()) return;
        if (Date.now() - lastOutputAt < completionQuietMs) return;
        completedViaFile = true;
        // Pixflow-owned: the Bricks handoff result is durable at this point.
        // Terminate a lingering runner shutdown so the UI receives the result
        // instead of waiting for a stale child process forever.
        process.stderr.write(`\n${label} runner produced ${completionFile} and went quiet; finishing from artifact.\n`);
        try {
          child.kill('SIGTERM');
        } catch {
          // Ignore; close/error handlers below settle the promise.
        }
        forceKillTimer = setTimeout(() => {
          try {
            if (!child.killed) child.kill('SIGKILL');
          } catch {
            // Ignore.
          }
        }, 5_000);
      }, 2_000);
    }

    if (maxRuntimeMs > 0) {
      runtimeTimer = setTimeout(() => {
        if (settled || completedViaFile) return;
        timedOut = true;
        process.stderr.write(`\n${label} runner exceeded ${Math.round(maxRuntimeMs / 1000)}s without producing a final quiet artifact; stopping runner.\n`);
        try {
          child.kill('SIGTERM');
        } catch {
          // Ignore; close/error handlers below settle the promise.
        }
        forceKillTimer = setTimeout(() => {
          try {
            if (!child.killed) child.kill('SIGKILL');
          } catch {
            // Ignore.
          }
        }, 5_000);
      }, maxRuntimeMs);
    }

    child.on('error', (error) => {
      rejectOnce(new CliError(`Could not launch ${label} runner: ${error.message}`));
    });

    child.on('close', (code) => {
      handleRunnerJsonLine(stdoutRemainder);
      if (runnerFailureMessage && shouldRejectRunnerFailureAfterArtifact({
        completedViaFile,
        completionFileExists: Boolean(completionFile && existsSync(completionFile)),
        completionArtifactsUpdated: completionArtifactsUpdated(),
      })) {
        rejectOnce(new CliError(runnerFailureMessage));
        return;
      }
      const durableArtifactCompletion = !shouldRejectRunnerFailureAfterArtifact({
        completedViaFile,
        completionFileExists: Boolean(completionFile && existsSync(completionFile)),
        completionArtifactsUpdated: completionArtifactsUpdated(),
      });
      if (timedOut && !durableArtifactCompletion) {
        rejectOnce(new CliError(`${label} runner timed out after ${Math.round(maxRuntimeMs / 1000)}s before producing a completed Stage B result. The baseline preview may still be inserted, but final Stage B repair was not applied.`));
        return;
      }
      if (code !== 0 && !durableArtifactCompletion) {
        rejectOnce(new CliError(`${label} runner exited with code ${code}.`));
        return;
      }
      resolveOnce({
        code: code || 0,
        kind: invocation.kind,
        eventSummary,
        eventsFile: invocation.eventsFile || null,
        stderrFile: invocation.stderrFile || null,
        completedViaFile,
      });
    });
  });
}

async function ensureIsolatedCodexHome(codexHome) {
  const target = firstString(codexHome);
  if (!target) return;
  await fs.mkdir(target, { recursive: true });

  const source = firstString(process.env.CODEX_HOME, path.join(os.homedir(), '.codex'));
  if (!source || path.resolve(source) === path.resolve(target)) {
    return;
  }

  for (const fileName of ['auth.json', '.credentials.json', 'installation_id', 'cap_sid']) {
    const sourcePath = path.join(source, fileName);
    const targetPath = path.join(target, fileName);
    try {
      const stat = await fs.stat(sourcePath);
      if (stat.isFile()) {
        await fs.copyFile(sourcePath, targetPath);
      }
    } catch {
      // Codex auth/session filenames vary by surface; missing files are fine.
    }
  }
}

async function runLocalInvocationCapture(invocation, cwd, label) {
  process.stderr.write(`Running ${label} command in ${cwd}\n${invocation.display}\n`);
  const stdin = invocation.stdinFile ? await fs.readFile(invocation.stdinFile, 'utf8') : invocation.stdin;
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const child = invocation.shell
      ? spawn(commandLineForShellInvocation(invocation), {
          cwd,
          shell: true,
          env: { ...process.env, ...(invocation.env || {}) },
          stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
          windowsHide: true,
        })
      : spawn(invocation.command, invocation.args || [], {
          cwd,
          shell: false,
          env: { ...process.env, ...(invocation.env || {}) },
          stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
          windowsHide: true,
        });

    let stdoutText = '';
    let stderrText = '';
    child.stdout?.on('data', (chunk) => {
      const text = chunk.toString('utf8');
      stdoutText += text;
      process.stderr.write(text);
    });
    child.stderr?.on('data', (chunk) => {
      const text = chunk.toString('utf8');
      stderrText += text;
      process.stderr.write(text);
    });
    child.on('error', reject);
    child.on('close', (code, signal) => {
      if (code !== 0) {
        reject(new CliError(`${label} command failed with exit code ${code}.`, {
          code,
          signal,
          stderr: stderrText.slice(-4000),
        }));
        return;
      }
      resolve({ stdoutText, stderrText });
    });
    if (stdin !== null && stdin !== undefined) {
      child.stdin?.write(stdin);
    }
    child.stdin?.end();
  });
}

async function buildLibraryTaskInvocation(runnerId, workspaceDir, promptFile, flags) {
  const agent = BRIDGE_AGENT_CATALOG.find((item) => item.id === runnerId);
  if (!agent) {
    throw new CliError(`Unknown local CLI runner "${runnerId}".`);
  }
  const command = detectFirstCommandSync(agent);
  if (!command.path) {
    throw new CliError(`${agent.label} was selected, but none of these commands were found on this machine: ${agent.commands.join(', ')}.`);
  }

  const model = firstString(flags.model);
  const runnerSpec = runnerId === 'antigravity'
    ? buildBridgeAntigravityRunnerSpec(
        { workspaceDir, runnerPromptFile: promptFile },
        model,
        firstString(flags.reasoning),
      )
    : { args: buildLibraryTaskRunnerArgs(runnerId, workspaceDir, model), stdinFile: promptFile };
  return {
    kind: runnerId,
    display: [quoteForShell(command.path), ...args.map(quoteForShell)].join(' '),
    command: command.path,
    args: runnerSpec.args,
    shell: false,
    stdinFile: runnerSpec.stdinFile,
    env: {},
  };
}

function buildLibraryTaskRunnerArgs(runnerId, workspaceDir, model) {
  if (runnerId === 'codex') {
    const args = ['exec', '--skip-git-repo-check', '--sandbox', 'read-only', '--cd', workspaceDir];
    if (model && model !== 'default') args.push('--model', model);
    args.push('-');
    return args;
  }
  if (runnerId === 'claude') {
    const args = ['-p', '--input-format', 'text', '--output-format', 'text'];
    if (model && model !== 'default') args.push('--model', model);
    return args;
  }
  if (runnerId === 'opencode') {
    const args = ['run'];
    if (model && model !== 'default') args.push('-m', model);
    return args;
  }
  if (runnerId === 'cursor-agent') {
    const args = ['--print', '--force', '--trust', '--workspace', workspaceDir];
    if (model && model !== 'default') args.push('--model', model);
    return args;
  }
  if (runnerId === 'qwen') {
    const args = [];
    if (model && model !== 'default') args.push('--model', model);
    return args;
  }
  throw new CliError(`Pixflow Library tasks do not support runner "${runnerId}" yet.`);
}

function extractLibraryTaskTextFields(payload) {
  const fields = [];
  const visit = (value, pathParts, inheritedId) => {
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      value.forEach((item, index) => visit(item, [...pathParts, index], inheritedId));
      return;
    }
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return;
    const record = value;
    const elementId = firstString(record.id, record._id, record.elementId, inheritedId);
    for (const [key, entry] of Object.entries(record)) {
      const nextPath = [...pathParts, key];
      if (typeof entry === 'string') {
        const trimmed = entry.trim();
        if (
          elementId
          && trimmed
          && trimmed.length <= 800
          && /(?:text|title|heading|subheading|content|description|label|button|caption|eyebrow)$/i.test(key)
        ) {
          fields.push({
            id: elementId,
            path: nextPath,
            key,
            text: entry,
            fieldType: key,
          });
        }
      } else {
        visit(entry, nextPath, elementId);
      }
    }
  };
  visit(payload, [], '');
  const seen = new Set();
  return fields.filter((field) => {
    const signature = `${field.id}:${field.path.join('.')}`;
    if (seen.has(signature)) return false;
    seen.add(signature);
    return true;
  });
}

function buildLibraryTemplateAdaptationPrompt(request, fields) {
  const workspace = objectValue(request.workspace);
  const page = objectValue(request.page);
  const selectedTemplate = objectValue(request.selected_template);
  const sectionContext = objectValue(request.section_context);
  const compactFields = fields.map((field) => ({
    id: field.id,
    path: field.path.join('.'),
    fieldType: field.fieldType,
    currentText: field.text,
  }));

  return [
    'You are a Pixflow Library section copy worker.',
    'Return only valid JSON. Do not include markdown fences or commentary.',
    'Rewrite only the provided fields. Keep wording concise, commercially useful, and specific to the page/business.',
    'Do not invent statistics, awards, testimonials, prices, guarantees, or compliance claims.',
    'Output schema: {"filled_fields":[{"id":"","path":"","text":"","field_type":"","semantic_role":""}]}',
    '',
    `Business: ${firstString(workspace.business_name, workspace.project_name, 'the business')}`,
    `Business description: ${firstString(workspace.business_description, workspace.overview)}`,
    `Page title: ${firstString(page.title)}`,
    `Page summary: ${firstString(page.summary)}`,
    `Section type: ${firstString(sectionContext.planned_type)}`,
    `Section purpose: ${firstString(sectionContext.section_purpose)}`,
    `Section description: ${firstString(sectionContext.section_description)}`,
    `Template: ${firstString(selectedTemplate.title)} (${firstString(selectedTemplate.slug)})`,
    `Copy brief: ${firstString(request.copy_brief)}`,
    `Unique angle: ${firstString(request.unique_angle)}`,
    '',
    'Fields to rewrite:',
    JSON.stringify(compactFields, null, 2),
  ].join('\n');
}

function extractLibraryTaskJson(text) {
  const trimmed = String(text || '').trim();
  const direct = parseJsonObjectOrNull(trimmed);
  if (direct) return direct;

  const fenced = trimmed.match(/```(?:json)?\s*([\s\S]*?)```/i);
  if (fenced) {
    const parsed = parseJsonObjectOrNull(fenced[1].trim());
    if (parsed) return parsed;
  }

  const start = trimmed.indexOf('{');
  const end = trimmed.lastIndexOf('}');
  if (start !== -1 && end > start) {
    const parsed = parseJsonObjectOrNull(trimmed.slice(start, end + 1));
    if (parsed) return parsed;
  }

  throw new CliError('Pixflow Library CLI worker did not return valid JSON.');
}

function parseJsonObjectOrNull(text) {
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
    return parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

function normalizeLibraryTaskFilledFields(value, fields) {
  if (!Array.isArray(value)) return [];
  const fieldByPath = new Map(fields.map((field) => [field.path.join('.'), field]));
  const fieldById = new Map(fields.map((field) => [field.id, field]));
  const normalized = [];
  for (const entry of value) {
    const record = objectValue(entry);
    const text = firstString(record.text).trim();
    if (!text) continue;
    const pathKey = firstString(record.path);
    const source = fieldByPath.get(pathKey) || fieldById.get(firstString(record.id));
    if (!source) continue;
    normalized.push({
      id: source.id,
      path: source.path,
      text: text.slice(0, 900),
      field_type: firstString(record.field_type, record.fieldType, source.fieldType, 'text'),
      semantic_role: firstString(record.semantic_role, record.semanticRole, source.fieldType, 'body'),
    });
  }
  return normalized;
}

function applyLibraryTaskFilledFields(payload, filledFields) {
  const cloned = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(payload));
  for (const field of filledFields) {
    setValueAtPath(cloned, field.path, field.text);
  }
  return cloned;
}

function setValueAtPath(target, pathParts, value) {
  let cursor = target;
  for (let index = 0; index < pathParts.length - 1; index += 1) {
    cursor = cursor?.[pathParts[index]];
    if (cursor === null || cursor === undefined) return;
  }
  const key = pathParts[pathParts.length - 1];
  if (cursor && key !== undefined) {
    cursor[key] = value;
  }
}

